/* =========================================================
   MAGIC ITEMS DATA
   Content for the "Magic Items" section, nested inside the
   "Items" dropdown in the Reference pane as a sibling of
   Equipment. This file holds ONE entry, MAGIC_ITEMS_DATA, whose
   own id/title ("items-magic-items" / "Magic Items") is appended
   as a child into #itemsContainer's .condition-list by
   dm-screen.js's renderDataDrivenReferenceSections(), rather than
   being rendered into its own top-level dropdown.

   Structure: MAGIC_ITEMS_DATA is a single entry whose "children"
   are category containers (Ammunition, Potions, Alchemical Items,
   Rings, Rods, Wands, Poisons, Staves), each of which has
   "children" that are rarity-bucket containers (Common, Uncommon,
   Rare, Very Rare, Legendary, Artifact), each of which has
   "children" that are the actual item entries. All container
   entries (the top-level entry, category containers, and rarity
   buckets) use an empty "html" field — only individual item
   entries carry real content.
   ========================================================= */

const MAGIC_ITEMS_DATA = {"id": "items-magic-items", "title": "Magic Items", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-ammunition", "title": "Ammunition", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-ammunition-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-unbreakable-arrow", "title": "Unbreakable Arrow", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Common</strong></p><p>This magic arrow doesn't snap, splinter, or otherwise get destroyed when it's used, so you can simply retrieve and reuse it after every shot instead of losing it the way ordinary ammunition is sometimes lost. Its one weakness is an antimagic field or similar effect: while inside one, the arrow loses its magic, and it can be broken like an ordinary arrow for as long as it remains there.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-walloping-ammunition", "title": "Walloping Ammunition", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Common</strong></p><p>This piece of magic ammunition is built to stagger a target rather than just wound it. A <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a> hit by it must succeed on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-strength\">Strength</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 10) or be knocked <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a>, on top of whatever damage the attack itself deals.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-ammunition-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ammunition-1", "title": "Ammunition, +1", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This magic ammunition carries a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. That bonus is spent the instant the ammunition hits a target — once it deals damage, it reverts to an ordinary, nonmagical piece of ammunition.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-ammunition-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ammunition-2", "title": "Ammunition, +2", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Rare</strong></p><p>This magic ammunition carries a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. That bonus is spent the instant the ammunition hits a target — once it deals damage, it reverts to an ordinary, nonmagical piece of ammunition.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-ammunition-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ammunition-3", "title": "Ammunition, +3", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This magic ammunition carries a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. That bonus is spent the instant the ammunition hits a target — once it deals damage, it reverts to an ordinary, nonmagical piece of ammunition.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ammunition-of-slaying", "title": "Ammunition of Slaying", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Ammunition), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This ammunition is crafted to bring down one particular kind of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a>, either chosen by the DM ahead of time or rolled randomly on the table below. Whenever it deals damage to a creature of that type, the target must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take an extra 6d10 Force <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, or half as much on a success. The instant it deals that extra damage, the ammunition burns out and becomes an ordinary, nonmagical piece of gear.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Creature Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–10</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-aberration\">Aberrations</a></td></tr><tr><td>11–15</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-beast\">Beasts</a></td></tr><tr><td>16–20</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-celestial\">Celestials</a></td></tr><tr><td>21–25</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a></td></tr><tr><td>26–35</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragons</a></td></tr><tr><td>36–45</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-elemental\">Elementals</a></td></tr><tr><td>46–50</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoids</a></td></tr><tr><td>51–60</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fey\">Fey</a></td></tr><tr><td>61–70</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiends</a></td></tr><tr><td>71–75</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giants</a></td></tr><tr><td>76–80</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-monstrosity\">Monstrosities</a></td></tr><tr><td>81–85</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-ooze\">Oozes</a></td></tr><tr><td>86–90</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-plant\">Plants</a></td></tr><tr><td>91–00</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a></td></tr></tbody></table><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (Arrow), Very Rare</strong></p><p>Called an arrow of slaying, this weapon is built to slay one particular kind of creature — as broad as an entire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature-type\">creature type</a> or as narrow as a single named race, chosen by the DM rather than rolled randomly (an arrow of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">dragon</a> slaying and an arrow of blue dragon slaying are both valid, for instance). Whenever it deals damage to a creature matching that type, race, or group, the target must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take an extra 6d10 Piercing <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, or half as much on a success. Once it deals that extra damage, the arrow becomes an ordinary, nonmagical one. Bolts built the same way exist for crossbows, though the arrow form is by far the most common.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-potions", "title": "Potions", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-potions-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-potion-of-climbing", "title": "Potion of Climbing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Common</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain a climbing <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> equal to your walking Speed for 1 hour. During that time, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Strength (Athletics) checks you make to climb.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-healing", "title": "Potion of Healing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Common</strong></p><p>You regain 2d4 + 2 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when you drink this potion. Whatever its potency, a Potion of Healing's red liquid glimmers when agitated.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-plantspeak", "title": "Potion of Plantspeak", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Common</strong></p><p>This clear, brown liquid turns pale yellow once opened. Drinking it grants you the ability to communicate with <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-plant\">Plants</a> for 5 minutes.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-willowshade-oil", "title": "Willowshade Oil", "html": "<p><strong>Potion (Oil), Common</strong></p><p>A creature can use its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to apply this dark blue oil to another creature that's been petrified for less than 1 minute, ending the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-petrified\">Petrified</a> condition at the start of what would be that creature's next turn.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-potions-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-keoghtom-s-restorative-ointment-piccolo", "title": "Keoghtom's Restorative Ointment", "html": "<p><strong>Potion (Ointment), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This glass jar holds 3 doses of a thick ointment that smells faintly of aloe. As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, one dose can be swallowed or applied to the skin; the creature that receives it regains 2d8+2 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>, stops being <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>, and is cured of any disease.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-lesser-potion-of-mana", "title": "Lesser Potion of Mana", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Drinking this deeply purple potion lets you regain 2 points of a resource that recovers through short rests — 2 uses of Arcane Recovery for a Wizard, or 2 Sorcery Points for a Sorcerer.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-oil-of-slipperiness", "title": "Oil of Slipperiness", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>One vial of this oil can cover one Medium or smaller creature, along with the equipment it's wearing and carrying (one additional vial is needed for each size category above Medium). Applying the oil takes 10 minutes, after which the creature gains the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-freedom-of-movement\">Freedom of Movement</a> spell for 8 hours.</p><p>Alternatively, the oil can be poured on the ground as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, where it covers a 10-foot square and duplicates the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-grease\">Grease</a> spell in that area for 8 hours.</p><p>This sticky, black unguent is thick and heavy, but flows quickly when poured.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-advantage", "title": "Potion of Advantage", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this shimmering, golden potion, you gain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on one <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-ability-check\">ability check</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> of your choice that you make within the next hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-animal-friendship", "title": "Potion of Animal Friendship", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you can cast the level 3 version of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animal-friendship\">Animal Friendship</a> spell (save DC 13).</p><p>Agitating this potion's muddy liquid brings little bits into view: a fish scale, a hummingbird feather, a cat claw, or a squirrel hair.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you can cast the animal friendship spell (save DC 13) for 1 hour at will. Agitating this muddy liquid brings little bits into view: a fish scale, a hummingbird tongue, a cat claw, or a squirrel hair.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-fire-breath", "title": "Potion of Fire Breath", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>After drinking this potion, you can use a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to exhale fire at a target within 30 feet of you. The target must make a DC 13 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 4d6 Fire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The effect ends after you exhale the fire three times or when 1 hour has passed.</p><p>This potion's orange liquid flickers, and smoke fills the top of its container and wafts out whenever it is opened.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-hill", "title": "Potion of Giant Strength (hill)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to 21 for 1 hour. The potion has no effect on you if your Strength is already 21 or higher.</p><p>This potion's transparent liquid has a sliver of a giant's fingernail floating in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-greater-healing-piccolo", "title": "Potion of Greater Healing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>You regain 4d4+4 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when you drink this potion. It confers no benefit to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-growth", "title": "Potion of Growth", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the “enlarge” effect of the Enlarge/Reduce spell for 10 minutes (no Concentration required).</p><p>The red in the potion's liquid continuously expands from a tiny bead to color the clear liquid around it and then contracts. Shaking the bottle fails to interrupt this process.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the “enlarge” effect of the enlarge/reduce spell for 1d4 hours (no concentration required). The red in the potion's liquid continuously expands from a tiny bead to color the clear liquid around it and then contracts. Shaking the bottle fails to interrupt this process.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-healing-greater", "title": "Potion of Healing (greater)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>You regain 4d4 + 4 Hit Points when you drink this potion. Whatever its potency, a Potion of Healing's red liquid glimmers when agitated.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-maximum-power", "title": "Potion of Maximum Power", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>The first time you cast a damage-dealing spell of 4th level or lower within 1 minute of drinking this potion, you can use the highest possible number on each of that spell's damage dice instead of rolling them.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-resistance", "title": "Potion of Resistance", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to one type of damage for 1 hour. The DM chooses the type or determines it randomly.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-swimming", "title": "Potion of Swimming", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain a swimming <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> equal to your walking Speed for 1 hour. During that time, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Strength (Athletics) checks you make to swim.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-water-breathing", "title": "Potion of Water Breathing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>You can breathe underwater for 24 hours after drinking this potion. This potion's cloudy green fluid smells of the sea and has a jellyfish-like bubble floating in it.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>You can breathe underwater for 1 hour after drinking this potion. Its cloudy green fluid smells of the sea and has a jellyfish-like bubble floating in it.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-potions-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-elixir-of-health", "title": "Elixir of Health", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you are cured of all magical contagions. In addition, the following conditions end on you: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafened</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-paralyzed\">Paralyzed</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>.</p><p>The clear, red liquid has tiny bubbles of light in it.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, it cures any disease afflicting you, and it removes the blinded, deafened, paralyzed, and poisoned conditions. The clear red liquid has tiny bubbles of light in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-liquid-luck", "title": "Liquid Luck", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Indistinguishable from water by sight or smell, but tasting and smelling like the drinker's favorite fruit, this potion grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on all Deception, Insight, and Persuasion checks for 3 hours.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-oil-of-dragon-s-bane", "title": "Oil of Dragon's Bane", "html": "<p><strong>Potion (Oil), Rare</strong></p><p>This oil can coat a single weapon for 3 uses, or be used to dip up to 3 pieces of ammunition for 1 use each. A <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragon</a> that takes damage from a weapon or piece of ammunition coated in this oil takes an extra 6d6 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> of the same type from that attack. The oil dries and becomes inert after 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-oil-of-etherealness", "title": "Oil of Etherealness", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>One vial of this oil can cover one Medium or smaller creature, along with the equipment it's wearing and carrying (one additional vial is needed for each size category above Medium). Applying the oil takes 10 minutes. The affected creature then gains the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-etherealness\">Etherealness</a> spell for 1 hour.</p><p>Beads of this cloudy, gray oil form on the outside of its container and quickly evaporate.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-aqueous-form", "title": "Potion of Aqueous Form", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you transform into a pool of water, returning to your true form after 10 minutes or if you're Incapacitated or die. While transformed, you have a swimming Speed of 30 feet, can move over or through other liquids, can enter and occupy another creature's space, can shrink to fit through even Tiny openings, and extinguish any nonmagical flame you enter. You also have Resistance to nonmagical damage and Advantage on Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution saving throws, but you can't talk, attack, cast spells, or activate magic items. Anything you're carrying that doesn't meld into your new form (such as armor you're wearing) continues to affect you as normal, but becomes inaccessible.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-clairvoyance", "title": "Potion of Clairvoyance", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-clairvoyance\">Clairvoyance</a> spell (no <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a> required).</p><p>An eyeball bobs in this potion's yellowish liquid but vanishes when the potion is opened.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-diminution", "title": "Potion of Diminution", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the “reduce” effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-enlarge-reduce\">Enlarge/Reduce</a> spell for 1d4 hours (no Concentration required).</p><p>The red in the potion's liquid continuously contracts to a tiny bead and then expands to color the clear liquid around it. Shaking the bottle fails to interrupt this process.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-gaseous-form", "title": "Potion of Gaseous Form", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gaseous-form\">Gaseous Form</a> spell for 1 hour (no Concentration required) or until you end the effect as a Bonus Action.</p><p>This potion's container seems to hold fog that moves and pours like water.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-piccolo", "title": "Potion of Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to a set value for 1 hour, depending on which type of giant provided the fingernail sliver used to brew it — 21 for a Hill giant, 23 for a Frost or Stone giant, 25 for a Fire giant, 27 for a Cloud giant, or 29 for a Storm giant. The potion has no effect if your Strength is already equal to or higher than that value.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-fire", "title": "Potion of Giant Strength (fire)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to 25 for 1 hour. The potion has no effect on you if your Strength is already 25 or higher.</p><p>This potion's transparent liquid has a sliver of a giant's fingernail floating in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-frost-or-stone", "title": "Potion of Giant Strength (frost or stone)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to 23 for 1 hour. The potion has no effect on you if your Strength is already 23 or higher.</p><p>This version is brewed from either a frost giant's or a stone giant's fingernail, and both have the same effect. This potion's transparent liquid has a sliver of a giant's fingernail floating in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-healing-superior", "title": "Potion of Healing (superior)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>You regain 8d4 + 8 Hit Points when you drink this potion. Whatever its potency, a Potion of Healing's red liquid glimmers when agitated.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-heroism", "title": "Potion of Heroism", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain 10 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-temporary-hp\">Temporary Hit Points</a> that last for 1 hour. For the same duration, you are under the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-bless\">Bless</a> spell (no Concentration required).</p><p>This potion's blue liquid bubbles and steams as if boiling.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-invisibility", "title": "Potion of Invisibility", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>This potion's container looks empty but feels as though it holds liquid. When you drink the potion, you have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-invisible\">Invisible</a> condition for 1 hour. The effect ends early if you make an attack roll, deal damage, or cast a spell.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This potion's container looks empty but feels as though it holds liquid. When you drink the potion, you become invisible for 1 hour. Anything you wear or carry is invisible with you. The effect ends early if you attack or cast a spell.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-invulnerability", "title": "Potion of Invulnerability", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>For 1 minute after you drink this potion, you have Resistance to all damage.</p><p>This potion's syrupy liquid looks like liquefied iron.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-mana", "title": "Potion of Mana", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Drinking this vibrant blue and purple potion lets you regain 4 points of a resource that recovers through short rests — 4 uses of Arcane Recovery for a Wizard, or 4 Sorcery Points for a Sorcerer.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-mind-reading", "title": "Potion of Mind Reading", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-thoughts\">Detect Thoughts</a> spell (save DC 13) for 10 minutes (no Concentration required).</p><p>This potion's dense, purple liquid has an ovoid cloud of pink floating in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-superior-healing-piccolo", "title": "Potion of Superior Healing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>You regain 8d4+8 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when you drink this potion. It confers no benefit to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-true-dreaming", "title": "Potion of True Dreaming", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Drunk before falling asleep, this poison-black liquid shows you, in your dreams, true visions of the past, present, or a possible future involving a creature, location, or object of your choosing. The DM determines the nature and duration of the visions.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-thor-s-might", "title": "Thor's Might", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>This churning, deep blue liquid, shot through with white streaks, shakes and quivers in its container. For 1 minute after drinking it, any melee weapon attack you land lets out a thunderous crack, dealing an extra 1d6 Thunder <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. There's no limit to how many times this can trigger within the duration.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-tincture-of-werewolf-s-bane", "title": "Tincture of Werewolf's Bane", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature-type\">lycanthrope</a> that drinks this tincture must succeed on a DC 19 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 3d10 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and be forced to change into its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> form, if it wasn't already in that form — while in that form, it can't change shape again for 24 hours. On a successful save, it takes only half the damage.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-potions-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-oil-of-sharpness", "title": "Oil of Sharpness", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>One vial of this oil can coat one Melee weapon or twenty pieces of ammunition, but only nonmagical ammunition and Melee weapons that deal Slashing or Piercing damage are affected. Applying the oil takes 1 minute, after which it turns the coated weapon into a +3 Weapon or the coated ammunition into +3 Ammunition.</p><p>This clear, gelatinous oil sparkles with tiny, ultrathin silver shards.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-polymorph-potion", "title": "Polymorph Potion", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This almost-clear, pale green potion holds the floating, constantly-morphing projection of a creature. Drinking it lets you cast the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> spell on yourself for 15 minutes, without needing to maintain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-continuous-healing", "title": "Potion of Continuous Healing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This murky red potion is highly sought after by soldiers and adventurers alike. After drinking it, you regain 2d10 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> at the start of each of your turns for 1 minute.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-enhanced-reactions", "title": "Potion of Enhanced Reactions", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This constantly color-shifting potion grants a +2 bonus to all <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> for 1 minute after you drink it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-flying", "title": "Potion of Flying", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain a Fly <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> equal to your Speed for 1 hour and can hover. If you're in the air when the potion wears off, you fall unless you have some other means of staying aloft.</p><p>This potion's clear liquid floats at the top of its container and has cloudy white impurities drifting in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-cloud", "title": "Potion of Giant Strength (cloud)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to 27 for 1 hour. The potion has no effect on you if your Strength is already 27 or higher.</p><p>This potion's transparent liquid has a sliver of a giant's fingernail floating in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-healing-supreme", "title": "Potion of Healing (supreme)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>You regain 10d4 + 20 Hit Points when you drink this potion. Whatever its potency, a Potion of Healing's red liquid glimmers when agitated.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-legendary-resistance", "title": "Potion of Legendary Resistance", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>Highly sought after by spellcasters, this ink-black potion grants 2 uses of Legendary Resistance, letting you choose to succeed on a failed <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> instead, once per turn. Any unused charges last until you finish a Long Rest.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-longevity", "title": "Potion of Longevity", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your physical age is reduced by 1d6 + 6 years, to a minimum of 13 years. Each time you subsequently drink a Potion of Longevity, there is a cumulative 10 percent chance that you instead age by 1d6 + 6 years.</p><p>Suspended in this amber liquid is a tiny heart that, against all reason, is still beating. It vanishes when the potion is opened.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-possibility", "title": "Potion of Possibility", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this clear potion, you gain two Fragments of Possibility, each of which lasts 8 hours or until used. Whenever you make an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-ability-check\">ability check</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, or whenever an attack roll targets you, you can expend a fragment to roll an additional d20 and choose which of the d20s to use (if the original roll had <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a>, roll the extra d20 after that's been applied). While you hold one or more fragments from this potion, you can't gain another Fragment of Possibility from any source.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-protection", "title": "Potion of Protection", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This steel-grey, murky liquid is flecked with tiny beads of yellow, green, red, blue, purple, white, and black. Drinking it grants immunity to every <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-condition\">condition</a> for 1 hour except <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-grappled\">Grappled</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-unconscious\">Unconscious</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-restoration", "title": "Potion of Restoration", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This purple potion, full of floating strands of muscle, blood vessels, and organ matter, causes any of the drinker's destroyed or missing body parts and organs to regrow over the course of a week. The regrowth causes severe itching and occasional rashy pain at the site.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-revival", "title": "Potion of Revival", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>An entirely opaque, black potion with a single point of light hanging in its middle, this has no effect on a living creature. Poured down the throat of a creature that died within the last minute, it revives that creature to 1 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Point</a>. It doesn't work on a creature that died of old age, and it can't restore any body part the creature was missing at the time of death.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-speed", "title": "Potion of Speed", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-haste\">Haste</a> spell for 1 minute (no Concentration required) without suffering the wave of lethargy that normally occurs when the effect ends.</p><p>This potion's yellow fluid is streaked with black and swirls on its own.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-supreme-healing-piccolo", "title": "Potion of Supreme Healing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>You regain 10d4+20 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when you drink this potion. It confers no benefit to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-truesight", "title": "Potion of Truesight", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>Drinking this potion grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-truesight\">Truesight</a> out to a range of 120 feet for 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-vitality", "title": "Potion of Vitality", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, it removes any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> you have and ends the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition on you. For the next 24 hours, you regain the maximum number of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-point-dice\">Hit Point Dice</a> for any die you spend.</p><p>This potion's crimson liquid regularly pulses with dull light, calling to mind a heartbeat.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, it removes any exhaustion you are suffering and cures any disease or poison affecting you. For the next 24 hours, you regain the maximum number of hit points for any Hit Die you spend. The potion's crimson liquid regularly pulses with dull light, calling to mind a heartbeat.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-reincarnation-dust", "title": "Reincarnation Dust", "html": "<p><strong>Potion (Dust), Very Rare</strong></p><p>When this small pouch of purple dust is sprinkled onto a dead <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> or the remains of one, the dust is absorbed and, if the creature is willing, it returns to life with a new body as though the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-reincarnate\">Reincarnate</a> spell had been cast on the remains.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-superior-potion-of-mana", "title": "Superior Potion of Mana", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>Drinking this vibrant blue and purple potion lets you regain 8 points of a resource that recovers through short rests — 8 uses of Arcane Recovery for a Wizard, or 8 Sorcery Points for a Sorcerer.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-vampiric-essence", "title": "Vampiric Essence", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This violently sour, vibrant green potion is among the most difficult to brew correctly — small mistakes can turn it into a bitter, poisonous concoction instead. Brewed correctly, for 1 minute after drinking it, a fifth of all Piercing, Slashing, or Bludgeoning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> dealt to you is instead absorbed and used to restore your own <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">hit points</a>.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-potions-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-storm", "title": "Potion of Giant Strength (storm)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Legendary</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to 29 for 1 hour. The potion has no effect on you if your Strength is already 29 or higher.</p><p>This potion's transparent liquid has a sliver of a giant's fingernail floating in it.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-alchemical-items", "title": "Alchemical Items", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-alchemical-items-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-blasting-powder", "title": "Blasting Powder", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This volatile powder comes in a small pouch. Ignited by an open flame or a fuse, it explodes, and each <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a> within 5 feet of it must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 3d6 Bludgeoning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, or half as much on a success. Multiple pouches can be bound together to explode at once — each additional pouch adds 1d6 to the damage (maximum 10d6) and 5 feet to the blast radius (maximum 20 feet).</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-bottled-breath", "title": "Bottled Breath", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This bottle holds a breath of elemental air. Inhaling it, you can either exhale it immediately or hold it. Exhaling grants the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gust-of-wind\">Gust of Wind</a> spell. Holding it means you don't need to breathe for 1 hour, though you can end that benefit early — for example, to speak — without gaining the gust of wind effect.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-fake-blood", "title": "Fake Blood", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>Crafted to look, smell, and taste exactly like real blood, this concoction only gives itself away to an Investigation check of 15 or higher, or to any level of identification magic.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-grenade-smoke", "title": "Grenade, Smoke", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, this grenade can be thrown up to 60 feet away, or up to 120 feet with a grenade launcher. One round after landing, it fills a 20-foot-radius area with smoke that's Heavily Obscured for 4 rounds in a moderate wind (at least 10 miles per hour), or just 1 round in a strong wind (20 miles per hour or more).</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ink-spell-writing-common", "title": "Ink, Spell Writing (Common)", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is used to write spells of 1st through 3rd level into scrolls and spellbooks.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-muroosa-balm", "title": "Muroosa Balm", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>Made from the muroosa bush, this paste is known to prevent sunburn and resist fire. Spending 1 minute applying a quarter pint of it to your skin grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Fire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> for 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-pepper-peppers", "title": "Pepper Peppers", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This fiery, crunchy snack grants 3 temporary <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when eaten. Each batch produces 6 Pepper Peppers, and they can also be made with a cook's utensils.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-soothing-salve", "title": "Soothing Salve", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This sticky, sour-smelling salve is applied to a wound. For 1 hour after it's applied, spending a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-point-dice\">Hit Point Die</a> to recover hit points restores an extra 3 hit points per die spent.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-alchemical-items-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-blight-ichor", "title": "Blight Ichor", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Distilled from a fungus native to the Blightshore badlands, this bitter, chartreuse liqueur grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Intelligence and Wisdom checks for 1 hour to any creature that drinks it, provided it's neither a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a> nor <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> — though it also carries a Vulnerability to Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> for the same duration. For each dose consumed, the drinker must also succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 1d6 hours and suffer the effect of a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-confusion\">Confusion</a> spell for 1 minute. An <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> creature that drinks it instead gains Advantage on all Dexterity checks and immunity to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> condition for 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-brew-of-babel", "title": "Brew of Babel", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This baby-blue, highly opaque potion grants the ability to speak and understand — but not read or write — a language of your choice for 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-fire-balm", "title": "Fire Balm", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Applying a dose of this orange, herbal paste grants a +3 bonus to a single Constitution, Wisdom, or Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> made within the next 14 hours.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-forgetfulness-antidote", "title": "Forgetfulness Antidote", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This moss-green liquid is brewed to counteract the Forgetfulness poison. Drinking it immediately ends all effects of that poison.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-greater-antitoxin", "title": "Greater Antitoxin", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This murky, pumpkin-orange liquid grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on saving throws against Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> or the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition for 12 hours. During that time, the drinker also takes no damage over time from any poison, and can't be reduced to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> by poison damage.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ink-spell-writing-uncommon", "title": "Ink, Spell Writing (Uncommon)", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is used to write spells of 4th through 6th level into scrolls and spellbooks.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-invisible-ink", "title": "Invisible Ink", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is invisible once written, becoming visible only to spells, traits, or items that reveal invisible things, or by applying a mild acid.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-life-s-liquor", "title": "Life's Liquor", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This strong pink liquid appears completely clear apart from the image of a red heart floating in its middle, which always seems to face the drinker no matter the angle. Drinking it grants 2d6+2 temporary <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-midnight-oil", "title": "Midnight Oil", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When burned in a lantern, this oil sheds Bright Light out to 5 feet and Dim Light for another 5 feet, for 8 hours. A creature that stays within the light it sheds for the full 8 hours gains all the benefits of a Long Rest without needing to sleep, provided it only engages in light activity such as reading, studying, or talking during that time.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-murgaxor-s-elixir-of-life", "title": "Murgaxor's Elixir of Life", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Whoever drinks this concoction gains <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on death saving throws for 24 hours.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-pixie-dust", "title": "Pixie Dust", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, you can sprinkle this dust on yourself or another creature within 5 feet. The recipient gains a flying <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> of 30 feet and the ability to hover for 1 minute. If the creature is airborne when the effect ends, it drifts safely to the ground, landing on its feet without taking damage. A packet holds enough dust for one use.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-pomander-of-warding", "title": "Pomander of Warding", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Once unwrapped, this ball of aromatic spices and perfumes fills a 15-foot-radius area with a strong scent for 24 hours. Any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-challenge-rating\">challenge rating</a> 2 or lower that enters the area must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be turned, exactly as with a cleric's Turn Undead feature.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-quenching-philter", "title": "Quenching Philter", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This blue potion always has 2 ice cubes and 2 slices of lemon floating in it, and stays cool to the touch. Drinking it completely quenches thirst and removes the drinker's need to drink anything for 2 days, making it a favorite treat for travelers crossing arid country.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-soothsalts", "title": "Soothsalts", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>These crystalline, lozenge-sized doses are consumed orally, leaving a telltale crimson stain around a frequent user's mouth. A dose grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on all Intelligence checks for 1d4 hours, but for each dose taken, the creature must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or gain a level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> — an effect that stacks with multiple doses. Soothsalts can fetch up to 150 gp from the right buyer, but are illegal to trade in many places.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-alchemical-items-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-bottled-rest", "title": "Bottled Rest", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This purple potion seems to hold clouds that continuously roll past the upper part of its container. Drinking it restores 3 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-point-dice\">Hit Point Dice</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ink-spell-writing-rare", "title": "Ink, Spell Writing (Rare)", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is used to write spells of 7th or 8th level into scrolls and spellbooks.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-meditative-rest", "title": "Meditative Rest", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This vibrant orange liquid holds the vague images of two shapes locked in constant struggle. Drinking it restores 4 Ki Points.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-tea-of-refreshment", "title": "Tea of Refreshment", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This warm drink removes one level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> from whoever drinks it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-thessaltoxin-antidote", "title": "Thessaltoxin Antidote", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This potion changes color and texture every time it's looked at. Drinking it ends the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> effect imposed by Thessaltoxin.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-alchemical-items-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ink-spell-writing-very-rare", "title": "Ink, Spell Writing (Very Rare)", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is used to write spells of 9th level into scrolls and spellbooks.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rings", "title": "Rings", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-rings-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ring-of-jumping", "title": "Ring of Jumping", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-jump\">Jump</a> from it, but only on yourself, without expending a spell slot.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-mind-shielding", "title": "Ring of Mind Shielding", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you're immune to any magic that would let another creature read your thoughts, detect your alignment, or learn whether you're lying, and other creatures can communicate with you telepathically only if you allow it (you can end that welcome with a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>). If you die while wearing the ring, your soul immediately transfers into it, provided the ring isn't already holding one — you can then either linger there or move on to the afterlife. While your soul is in the ring, you can communicate telepathically with anyone wearing it, and that wearer can't block the contact the way a living creature normally could; they can use an action to release your soul if you're willing to go. To bring you back to life this way, someone needs to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-true-resurrection\">True Resurrection</a> targeting your soul while it's in the ring — successfully doing so uses up the ring.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-swimming", "title": "Ring of Swimming", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing this ring, you have a swimming <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> of 40 feet.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-warmth", "title": "Ring of Warmth", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you have Resistance to Cold <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, and you're comfortable in temperatures as low as −50 degrees Fahrenheit without needing extra protection. Wrap up in heavy clothing on top of that, and you can shrug off cold as extreme as −100 degrees Fahrenheit.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-water-walking", "title": "Ring of Water Walking", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing this ring, you can stand on and move across any liquid surface — water, lava, acid, and the like — as though it were solid ground.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rings-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ring-of-animal-influence", "title": "Ring of Animal Influence", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong></p><p>This ring has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing it, you can expend 1 charge (Action) to cast one of the following spells: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animal-friendship\">Animal Friendship</a>; <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fear\">Fear</a>, though it affects only <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-beast\">Beasts</a> and uses this ring's own <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">DC</a> of 13 rather than your own spellcasting DC; or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-speak-with-animals\">Speak with Animals</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-evasion", "title": "Ring of Evasion", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This ring has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. If you fail a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dexterity\">Dexterity</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> while wearing it, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> and expend 1 charge to succeed instead.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-feather-falling", "title": "Ring of Feather Falling", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Whenever you fall while wearing this ring, you drift down at a rate of 60 feet per round and take no falling <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> when you land.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-free-action", "title": "Ring of Free Action", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficult-terrain\">Difficult Terrain</a> doesn't cost you extra movement, and magic can neither reduce any of your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speeds</a> nor give you the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-paralyzed\">Paralyzed</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a> condition.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-poison-resistance", "title": "Ring of Poison Resistance", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You have Resistance to Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> while wearing this ring.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-protection", "title": "Ring of Protection", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you get a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">AC</a> and to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-resistance", "title": "Ring of Resistance", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong></p><p>You have Resistance to one <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-types\">damage type</a> while wearing this ring — Acid, Cold, Fire, Force, Lightning, Necrotic, Poison, Psychic, Radiant, or Thunder — chosen by the DM or determined randomly when the ring is found.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you have Resistance to one damage type, chosen by the DM or determined randomly when the ring is found.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-spell-storing", "title": "Ring of Spell Storing", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This ring can hold up to 5 levels' worth of prepared <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell\">spells</a> at once. Any creature can cast a spell of 1st through 5th level into the ring by touching it while casting — doing so has no effect beyond storing the spell, using up a share of the ring's capacity equal to the spell's level, and the spell stays there until it's cast from the ring or the ring is emptied. If the ring can't hold a spell being cast into it, that casting fails and is wasted. While wearing the ring, you can cast any spell stored inside it; doing so uses the original caster's spellcasting ability, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell-attack\">spell attack</a> bonus, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">DC</a>, not your own, but is otherwise treated as you casting it. When found, this ring already holds 1d6 levels' worth of randomly determined spells chosen by the DM.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-the-ram", "title": "Ring of the Ram", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This ring has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing it, you can take an action and expend 1 to 3 of its charges to project a spectral ram's head at a target within 60 feet, making a ranged <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell-attack\">spell attack</a> with a +7 bonus. On a hit, the target takes Force <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> equal to 2d10 per charge spent, and if it's a creature, it must succeed on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-strength\">Strength</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be pushed back 5 feet per charge spent, unless it's too large or too firmly anchored to budge. Instead of attacking a creature, you can use this property to strike an object within range without needing an attack roll; doing so grants a +5 bonus to the Strength check needed to break that object for 1 charge spent, +10 for 2 charges, or +20 for 3 charges.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-x-ray-vision", "title": "Ring of X-ray Vision", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can speak its command word (action) to see into and through solid matter for 1 minute, out to a range of 30 feet. Matter in that range looks transparent to you and doesn't block light — up to 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, or 3 feet of wood or dirt; anything thicker blocks the vision, as does a thin sheet of lead. Using this property three or more times within a 24-hour period leaves you unable to see anything for 1d6 × 10 minutes afterward, as your eyes struggle to recover.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rings-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ring-of-regeneration", "title": "Ring of Regeneration", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you regain 1d6 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> every 10 minutes, as long as you have at least 1 hit point. If you lose a body part, it grows back over 1d6+1 days, provided you keep at least 1 hit point the entire time.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-shooting-stars", "title": "Ring of Shooting Stars", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring in <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkness\">Darkness</a>, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dancing-lights\">Dancing Lights</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-light\">Light</a> from it at will (action). The ring separately has 6 charges for two stronger properties, regaining 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn:</p><ul><li><strong>Faerie Fire.</strong> Expend 1 charge (action) to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-faerie-fire\">Faerie Fire</a> from the ring.</li><li><strong>Ball Lightning.</strong> Expend 2 charges (action) to conjure 1 to 4 spheres of lightning, each about 3 feet across, in unoccupied spaces you can see within 120 feet — the more spheres you make at once, the weaker each one is individually. Each sheds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> in a 30-foot radius and lasts as long as you <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">concentrate</a> on it (as if concentrating on a spell), up to 1 minute; you can move each one up to 30 feet as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>, though never more than 120 feet from you. If a creature other than you comes within 5 feet of a sphere, the sphere discharges its lightning at that creature (DC 15 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dexterity\">Dexterity</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> for half <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, with the amount scaling to how many spheres you made at once) and then winks out.</li></ul>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-telekinesis", "title": "Ring of Telekinesis", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-telekinesis\">Telekinesis</a> from it at will, though you can target only objects that aren't currently being worn or carried by anyone.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rings-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ring-of-djinni-summoning", "title": "Ring of Djinni Summoning", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can speak its command word (action) to summon a specific djinni from the Elemental Plane of Air into an unoccupied space you choose within 120 feet. It stays as long as you <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">concentrate</a> on sustaining the summons (as if concentrating on a spell), up to 1 hour, or until it drops to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>, at which point it returns home. While summoned, it's friendly toward you and your companions and follows any commands you give it regardless of language; left uncommanded, it defends itself but takes no other actions. Once it departs, you can't summon it again for 24 hours, and if it ever dies, the ring loses its magic for good.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-elemental-command", "title": "Ring of Elemental Command", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This ring is bound to one of the four Elemental Planes — Air, Earth, Fire, or Water — chosen by the DM or determined randomly. While wearing it, you have Advantage on attack rolls against <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-elemental\">Elementals</a> native to that plane, and they have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you. As a Magic action, you can also target an elemental of that plane within 60 feet and force it to make a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-wisdom\">Wisdom</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 18) or take the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-charmed\">Charmed</a> condition until the start of your next turn; while it's charmed this way, you control its movement and its action on your turn. The ring separately has 5 charges for casting spells tied to its element, regaining 1d4+1 expended charges daily at dawn, with a save DC of 18 for any of them that call for one:</p><ul><li><strong>Air.</strong> You can speak and understand Auran. When you fall, you descend at only 60 feet per round and take no falling <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. You have Resistance to Lightning damage, and you have a flying <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> equal to your walking Speed, including the ability to hover. You can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-chain-lightning\">Chain Lightning</a> (3 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gust-of-wind\">Gust of Wind</a> (2 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wind-wall\">Wind Wall</a> (1 charge) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Earth.</strong> You can speak and understand Terran. Rubble, rocks, and dirt aren't <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficult-terrain\">Difficult Terrain</a> for you, and you have Resistance to Acid damage. You can move through solid earth or rock as though it were Difficult Terrain, without disturbing the material you pass through; if you end your turn inside solid matter this way, you're shunted out to the nearest unoccupied space you last occupied. You can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stone-shape\">Stone Shape</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stoneskin\">Stoneskin</a> (3 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-stone\">Wall of Stone</a> (3 charges) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Fire.</strong> You can speak and understand Ignan, and you're immune to Fire damage. You can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-burning-hands\">Burning Hands</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (2 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-fire\">Wall of Fire</a> (3 charges) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Water.</strong> You can speak and understand Aquan. You can stand on and move across liquid surfaces as though they were solid ground, you can breathe underwater, and you have a swimming Speed equal to your walking Speed.</li></ul><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This version exists as four separately named rings — Ring of Air Elemental Command, Ring of Earth Elemental Command, Ring of Fire Elemental Command, and Ring of Water Elemental Command — each granting a modest baseline benefit simply for wearing it, plus a much stronger set of benefits that unlock only once you help slay an elemental matching the ring's element while attuned to it. Each version also lets you expend 2 of the ring's 3 charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dominate-monster\">Dominate Monster</a> (DC 17) on an elemental of its matching type; the ring regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn.</p><ul><li><strong>Air (baseline).</strong> You can speak and understand Auran, and when you fall, you descend at only 60 feet per round and take no falling damage. <strong>Air (after helping slay an air elemental).</strong> You gain Resistance to Lightning damage and a flying Speed equal to your walking Speed, including the ability to hover.</li><li><strong>Earth (baseline).</strong> You can speak and understand Terran, and rubble, rocks, and dirt aren't Difficult Terrain for you. <strong>Earth (after helping slay an earth elemental).</strong> You gain Resistance to Acid damage, and you can move through solid earth or rock as though it were Difficult Terrain, being shunted to the nearest unoccupied space you last occupied if you end your turn inside it; you can also cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stone-shape\">Stone Shape</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stoneskin\">Stoneskin</a> (3 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-stone\">Wall of Stone</a> (3 charges) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Fire (baseline).</strong> You can speak and understand Ignan, and you have Resistance to Fire damage. <strong>Fire (after helping slay a fire elemental).</strong> Your Fire Resistance upgrades to immunity, and you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-burning-hands\">Burning Hands</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (2 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-fire\">Wall of Fire</a> (3 charges) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Water (baseline).</strong> You can speak and understand Aquan, and you can stand on and move across liquid surfaces as though they were solid ground. <strong>Water (after helping slay a water elemental).</strong> You can also breathe underwater and gain a swimming Speed equal to your walking Speed.</li></ul>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-invisibility", "title": "Ring of Invisibility", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can take an action to turn invisible, taking anything you're wearing or carrying with you. You stay <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-invisible\">Invisible</a> until you remove the ring, until you attack or cast a spell, or until you spend a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to become visible again.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-spell-turning", "title": "Ring of Spell Turning", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you have Advantage on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> against spells. If you succeed on a save this way against a spell of level 7 or lower, that spell has no effect on you. If the spell also targeted only you, without creating any area of effect, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to hurl it back at its caster instead, who must then make their own saving throw against it, using their own spell save <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">DC</a>.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you have Advantage on saving throws against any spell that targets only you, without including you as part of a larger area of effect. If you roll a natural 20 on such a save and the spell is 7th level or lower, the spell has no effect on you at all, and instead targets its own caster — using that caster's slot level, spell save DC, spell attack bonus, and spellcasting ability, exactly as though they'd cast it at themselves.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-three-wishes", "title": "Ring of Three Wishes", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong></p><p>This ring has 3 charges. While wearing it, you can take an action and expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> from it. Once its last charge is spent, the ring loses its magic and becomes an ordinary ring.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rods", "title": "Rods", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-rods-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-immovable-rod", "title": "Immovable Rod", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This flat iron rod has a button on one end. As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, you can press the button to fix the rod magically in place — it doesn't move even if it's defying gravity, and holds up to 8,000 pounds of weight before deactivating and falling. Pressing the button again (an action, by you or anyone else) releases it. A creature can also free it by succeeding on a DC 30 Strength check.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-rod-of-the-pact-keeper-1", "title": "Rod of the Pact Keeper, +1", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a Warlock)</p><p>While holding this rod, you gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">saving throw DCs</a> of spells you cast using your Warlock spell slots. In addition, once per day while holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to regain one expended Warlock spell slot; this property can't be used again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rods-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-rod-of-rulership", "title": "Rod of Rulership", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>As a Magic action, you can present this rod and command obedience from each <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a> of your choice that you can see within 120 feet. Each target must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-charmed\">Charmed</a> by you for 8 hours, treating you as its trusted leader. The effect on a target ends early if you or your allies harm it, or if you order it to act against its own nature. Once used, this property can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-rod-of-the-pact-keeper-2", "title": "Rod of the Pact Keeper, +2", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Warlock)</p><p>While holding this rod, you gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">saving throw DCs</a> of spells you cast using your Warlock spell slots. In addition, once per day while holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to regain one expended Warlock spell slot; this property can't be used again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-tentacle-rod", "title": "Tentacle Rod", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Rare</strong></p><p>Made by the drow, this magic weapon ends in three rubbery tentacles. As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, you can direct each tentacle to attack a creature you can see within 15 feet of you, making a separate melee attack roll for each with a +9 bonus. Each tentacle that hits deals 1d6 Bludgeoning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. If all three tentacles hit the same target, that target must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> halved, gain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on Dexterity saving throws, and lose the ability to take <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reactions</a> for 1 minute; while affected this way, it can take either an action or a Bonus Action on its turn, but not both. It can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rods-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-rod-of-absorption", "title": "Rod of Absorption", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While holding this rod, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> when a spell that targets only you (and not an area including others) is cast, absorbing that spell's magic before it can affect you. Doing so doesn't store the spell itself, only the level of spell slot used to cast it, as points of stored energy — the rod can hold up to 50 points over its entire existence, and stops absorbing spells once that limit is reached, or if absorbing a spell's levels would push it over that limit. While attuned to the rod, a spellcaster can channel its stored energy into their own spell slots, up to 5th level, expending points equal to the slot's level to create it; a rod found already in play holds 1d10 points of stored energy.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-rod-of-alertness", "title": "Rod of Alertness", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While holding this rod, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Wisdom (Perception) checks and on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> rolls. You can also take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to cast one of the following spells from it: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-evil-and-good\">Detect Evil and Good</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-magic\">Detect Magic</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-poison-and-disease\">Detect Poison and Disease</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-see-invisibility\">See Invisibility</a>.</p><p>As a Magic action, you can also plant the rod's haft in the ground, causing its head to shed Bright Light in a 60-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 60 feet. While within that bright light, you and your friendly creatures gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">AC</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a>, and can pinpoint the location of any Invisible hostile creature that's also within the bright light. This effect lasts 10 minutes, or until the rod is removed from the ground (a Magic action), and can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-rod-of-security", "title": "Rod of Security", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Very Rare</strong></p><p>While holding this rod, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to activate it, instantly transporting yourself and up to 199 other willing creatures you can see into a paradise of your choosing that exists in an extraplanar space — a tranquil garden, a cheery tavern, an immense palace, a tropical island, or anything else you can imagine. The paradise always contains enough food and water to sustain its visitors, but anything else there can only exist there — an object taken outside the extraplanar space disappears. Every hour spent in the paradise restores <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">hit points</a> to a visitor as though it had spent one <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-point-dice\">Hit Point Die</a>, and no one ages while inside, though time still passes normally. Visitors can remain for up to 200 days divided by the number of creatures present (rounding down). Whoever activated the rod can end the effect early with an action, without needing the rod in hand to do so, sending everyone back to where they left from; the rod can't be activated again until the effect has ended.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-rod-of-the-pact-keeper-3", "title": "Rod of the Pact Keeper, +3", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Warlock)</p><p>While holding this rod, you gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">saving throw DCs</a> of spells you cast using your Warlock spell slots. In addition, once per day while holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to regain one expended Warlock spell slot; this property can't be used again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rods-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-rod-of-lordly-might", "title": "Rod of Lordly Might", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This rod normally functions as a magic mace with a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a>. It also has six numbered buttons that you can press as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>; whichever function is currently active stays active until you press a different button, or press the same button again to return the rod to its normal form.</p><ul><li><strong>Button 1: Flame Tongue.</strong> The rod becomes a Flame Tongue of a bladed weapon type you choose.</li><li><strong>Button 2: Battleaxe.</strong> The rod becomes a magic battleaxe with a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls.</li><li><strong>Button 3: Spear.</strong> The rod becomes a magic spear with a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls.</li><li><strong>Button 4: Climbing Pole.</strong> The rod extends into a pole up to 50 feet long, capped with a spike and hooks that anchor it even in granite-hard surfaces, and sprouts a ladder of climbing bars spaced 1 foot apart along its length. It can support up to 4,000 pounds.</li><li><strong>Button 5: Battering Ram.</strong> The rod becomes a handheld battering ram, granting a +10 bonus to Strength (Athletics) checks made to break through doors, barricades, and similar barriers.</li><li><strong>Button 6: Normal.</strong> Any other function ends, returning the rod to its normal mace form. While in this form, the rod also indicates magnetic north and gives you a rough sense of how deep underground or how high up you currently are.</li></ul>"}, {"id": "magic-item-rod-of-resurrection", "title": "Rod of Resurrection", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This rod has 5 charges, regaining 1 expended charge daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-heal\">Heal</a> from it (expending 1 charge) or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-resurrection\">Resurrection</a> from it (expending all 5 charges). If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the rod disappears in a harmless burst of radiance.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wands", "title": "Wands", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-wands-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-wand-of-conducting", "title": "Wand of Conducting", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Common</strong></p><p>This wand has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to conjure instrumental music or mimic the sound of a full orchestra for up to 1 minute.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-pyrotechnics", "title": "Wand of Pyrotechnics", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Common</strong></p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to create a harmless burst of multicolored light at a point you can see within 60 feet.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-scowls", "title": "Wand of Scowls", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Common</strong></p><p>This wand has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to force a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> within 30 feet that you can see to scowl for 1 minute.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-smiles", "title": "Wand of Smiles", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Common</strong></p><p>This wand has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to force a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> within 30 feet that you can see to smile for 1 minute.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wands-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-wand-of-magic-detection", "title": "Wand of Magic Detection", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This wand has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-magic\">Detect Magic</a> from it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-magic-missiles", "title": "Wand of Magic Missiles", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend no more than 3 charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-missile\">Magic Missile</a> from it — 1 charge casts it at its base (1st) level, and each additional charge spent casts it one level higher, up to a 3rd-level casting for 3 charges.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wand, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-missile\">Magic Missile</a> from it — 1 charge casts it at its base level, and each additional charge spent casts it one level higher, limited only by the wand’s own charge pool.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-secrets", "title": "Wand of Secrets", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This wand has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to sense the presence and general direction of any secret door or trap within 30 feet.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-web", "title": "Wand of Web", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-web\">Web</a> (save DC 15) from it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-the-war-mage-1", "title": "Wand of the War Mage, +1", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>While holding this wand, you gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell-attack\">spell attack rolls</a>. In addition, you ignore Half <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-half-cover\">Cover</a> when making a spell attack.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wands-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-wand-of-binding", "title": "Wand of Binding", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-hold-monster\">Hold Monster</a> (5 charges, save DC 17) or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-hold-person\">Hold Person</a> (2 charges, save DC 17) from it. You can also use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> and expend 1 charge to give yourself <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on a saving throw you're making against being <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-paralyzed\">Paralyzed</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a>, or on a check you're making to escape a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-grappling\">grapple</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-enemy-detection", "title": "Wand of Enemy Detection", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to speak its command word; for the next minute, you know the direction (but not the distance) of the nearest hostile creature within 60 feet of you. As long as the effect lasts, it ends early if you stop holding the wand.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-fear", "title": "Wand of Fear", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and point it at a creature you can see within 30 feet, expending 1 charge to force it to succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or use its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a>, if it has one, to move as far away from you as its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> allows. Alternatively, you can expend 2 charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fear\">Fear</a> (save DC 15) from it instead.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-fireballs", "title": "Wand of Fireballs", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend no more than 3 charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (save DC 15) from it — 1 charge casts it at its base (3rd) level, and each additional charge spent casts it one level higher, up to a 5th-level casting for 3 charges.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (save DC 15) from it — 1 charge casts it at its base level, and each additional charge spent casts it one level higher, limited only by the wand’s own charge pool.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-lightning-bolts", "title": "Wand of Lightning Bolts", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend no more than 3 charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lightning-bolt\">Lightning Bolt</a> (save DC 15) from it — 1 charge casts it at its base (3rd) level, and each additional charge spent casts it one level higher, up to a 5th-level casting for 3 charges.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lightning-bolt\">Lightning Bolt</a> (save DC 15) from it — 1 charge casts it at its base level, and each additional charge spent casts it one level higher, limited only by the wand’s own charge pool.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-paralysis", "title": "Wand of Paralysis", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and point it at a creature you can see within 60 feet, expending 1 charge to force it to succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-paralyzed\">Paralyzed</a> for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-wonder", "title": "Wand of Wonder", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to choose a target within 120 feet you can see — a creature, an object, or a point in space — then roll 1d100 and consult the table below to discover what happens. If the effect casts a spell from the wand, that spell's save DC is 15, and its range becomes 120 feet if it isn't already that long or longer. If an effect covers an area, it must be centered on and include the target; if an effect has multiple possible subjects, the DM randomly determines which ones are affected.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–05</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-slow\">Slow</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>06–10</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-faerie-fire\">Faerie Fire</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>11–15</td><td>You are <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-stunned\">Stunned</a> until the start of your next turn, believing something awesome just happened.</td></tr><tr><td>16–20</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gust-of-wind\">Gust of Wind</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>21–25</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-thoughts\">Detect Thoughts</a> on the target you chose. If you didn't target a creature, you instead take 1d6 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>26–30</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stinking-cloud\">Stinking Cloud</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>31–33</td><td>Heavy rain falls in a 60-foot radius centered on the target. The area becomes <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-lightly-obscured\">Lightly Obscured</a>. The rain falls until the start of your next turn.</td></tr><tr><td>34–36</td><td>An animal appears in the unoccupied space nearest the target. The animal isn't under your control and acts as it normally would. Roll again: on a 01–25 a rhinoceros appears, on a 26–50 an elephant appears, and on a 51–00 a rat appears.</td></tr><tr><td>37–46</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lightning-bolt\">Lightning Bolt</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>47–49</td><td>A cloud of 600 oversized butterflies fills a 30-foot radius centered on the target. The area becomes <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-heavily-obscured\">Heavily Obscured</a>. The butterflies remain for 10 minutes.</td></tr><tr><td>50–53</td><td>You enlarge the target as if you had cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-enlarge-reduce\">Enlarge/Reduce</a>. If the target can't be affected by that spell, or if you didn't target a creature, you become the target instead.</td></tr><tr><td>54–58</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-darkness\">Darkness</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>59–62</td><td>Grass grows on the ground in a 60-foot radius centered on the target. If grass is already there, it grows to ten times its normal size and remains overgrown for 1 minute.</td></tr><tr><td>63–65</td><td>An object of the DM's choice disappears into the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-ethereal\">Ethereal Plane</a>. The object must be neither worn nor carried, within 120 feet of the target, and no larger than 10 feet in any dimension.</td></tr><tr><td>66–69</td><td>You shrink yourself as if you had cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-enlarge-reduce\">Enlarge/Reduce</a> on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>70–79</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>80–84</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-invisibility\">Invisibility</a> on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>85–87</td><td>Leaves grow from the target. If you chose a point in space, leaves sprout from the creature nearest to that point instead. Unless picked off, the leaves turn brown and fall off after 24 hours.</td></tr><tr><td>88–90</td><td>A stream of 1d4×10 gems, each worth 1 gp, shoots from the wand's tip in a line 30 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each gem deals 1 Bludgeoning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, and the total damage of the gems is divided equally among all creatures in the line.</td></tr><tr><td>91–95</td><td>A burst of colorful shimmering light extends from you in a 30-foot radius. You and each creature in the area that can see must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a> for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</td></tr><tr><td>96–97</td><td>The target's skin turns bright blue for 1d10 days. If you chose a point in space, the creature nearest to that point is affected instead.</td></tr><tr><td>98–00</td><td>If you targeted a creature, it must make a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>; if you didn't target a creature, you become the target and make the save instead. Failing by 5 or more instantly <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-petrified\">Petrifies</a> the target; any other failure leaves it <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a> and beginning to turn to stone, forcing it to repeat the saving throw at the end of its next turn, becoming petrified on another failure or ending the effect on a success. The petrification lasts until removed by a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-greater-restoration\">Greater Restoration</a> spell or similar magic.</td></tr></tbody></table>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-the-war-mage-2", "title": "Wand of the War Mage, +2", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>While holding this wand, you gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell-attack\">spell attack rolls</a>. In addition, you ignore Half <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-half-cover\">Cover</a> when making a spell attack.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wands-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-wand-of-polymorph", "title": "Wand of Polymorph", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> (save DC 15) from it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-the-war-mage-3", "title": "Wand of the War Mage, +3", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>While holding this wand, you gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell-attack\">spell attack rolls</a>. In addition, you ignore Half <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-half-cover\">Cover</a> when making a spell attack.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wands-artifact", "title": "Artifact", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-wand-of-orcus", "title": "Wand of Orcus", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Artifact</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Made from a demon lord's own bones and topped with an enlarged human skull, this wand can be wielded as a magic mace with a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a>, dealing an extra 2d12 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> on a hit. It also grants a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">AC</a> while held.</p><p>Any creature other than Orcus himself that attempts to attune to the wand must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or die and rise as a Zombie under the wand's control; even on a success, the creature takes 10d6 Necrotic damage.</p><p>The wand has 7 charges, regaining 1d4+3 expended charges daily at dawn (Orcus himself, or a follower he's blessed, spends 2 fewer charges — minimum 0 — for the same spells). While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend charges to cast one of the following spells (save DC 18) from it: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animate-dead\">Animate Dead</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-speak-with-dead\">Speak with Dead</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-blight\">Blight</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-circle-of-death\">Circle of Death</a> (3 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-finger-of-death\">Finger of Death</a> (3 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-power-word-kill\">Power Word Kill</a> (4 charges).</p><p>Separately, once per day, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to conjure Skeletons and Zombies totaling up to 500 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> worth of undead (each with average hit points), rising from the ground or forming in unoccupied spaces within 300 feet of you. They obey your commands until destroyed or until the next dawn, when they collapse into inanimate piles of bone and rotting flesh.</p><p>Like other artifacts, the wand carries its own set of random beneficial and detrimental properties (2 minor and 1 major of each) determined when it's introduced to the campaign; its detrimental properties are suppressed while it's attuned to Orcus himself.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-poisons", "title": "Poisons", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-poisons-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-acid-tablets", "title": "Acid Tablets", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Common</strong></p><p>Disguised as ordinary stomach tablets, these force a creature who swallows one to make a DC 14 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 1d6 Acid <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and be unable to vomit for 30 seconds. At the start of each of its turns after that, the creature repeats the save; success lets it throw up and rid itself of the poison.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-basic-poison", "title": "Basic Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Common</strong></p><p>This vial of poison can coat one slashing or piercing weapon, or up to three pieces of ammunition; applying it takes an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>. A <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a> hit by the coated weapon or ammunition must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 1d4 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. Once applied, the poison stays potent for 1 minute before drying out.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-biza-s-breath", "title": "Biza's Breath", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Common</strong></p><p>A creature exposed to this poison must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 1 minute. While poisoned this way, it must use its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to make a melee attack against a randomly determined creature within its reach, or do nothing on its turn if no other creature is in reach. It can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dazzling-bomb", "title": "Dazzling Bomb", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Common</strong></p><p>Set off by a fuse or tripwire, this small bomb fills a 30-foot-diameter sphere with a highly irritating powder. Creatures caught in the powder must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be Stunned for 1 turn. <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> are unaffected.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-liquid-paranoia", "title": "Liquid Paranoia", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Common</strong></p><p>A creature that ingests this poison gains the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> condition, with the source of its fear being the next <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> it sees within 5 minutes of drinking it. The creature must make a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>; on a failure, the fear lasts 1 hour, or half as long on a success.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-nausea-pellet", "title": "Nausea Pellet", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Common</strong></p><p>This black pellet can be thrown as an improvised weapon with a 20/40 range. On impact, it shatters into a fine powder filling a 5-foot square. Creatures in that square must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 30 seconds, repeating the save at the end of each of their turns. A poisoned creature can also use its action, or a Bonus Action while holding a Stomach Stopper, to throw up and end the poison early. Holding one's breath doesn't help, since the powder targets the nasal membranes; <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> are unaffected.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-perfume-of-bewitching", "title": "Perfume of Bewitching", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact), Common</strong></p><p>This tiny vial holds enough magic perfume for one use. As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, you can apply it to yourself; for 1 hour afterward, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on all Charisma checks directed at <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoids</a> of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-challenge-rating\">challenge rating</a> 1 or lower, and those affected don't realize they've been magically influenced.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-poisons-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-angel-s-powder", "title": "Angel's Powder", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This hyper-fine, bright white powder is blown into a target's face before dispersing harmlessly. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or, for 1 hour, perceive everyone around it as trusted friends, becoming extremely suggestible to non-aggressive persuasion and deception.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-assassin-s-blood", "title": "Assassin's Blood", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 150 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must make a DC 10 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 6 (1d12) Poison damage and has the Poisoned condition for 24 hours. On a successful save, the creature takes half damage and isn't Poisoned.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-bane-berry-extract", "title": "Bane Berry Extract", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>A creature that swallows this poison must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>. While poisoned this way, it has <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on Strength, Constitution, and Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> for 15 minutes. On a successful save, the target feels no effect at all.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-black-paste", "title": "Black Paste", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact via clothing), Uncommon</strong></p><p>Designed to resemble leather or boot polish, this poison shines like new once applied to a piece of clothing. Wearing the treated garment for a total of 12 hours (not necessarily consecutive) forces a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the wearer takes 1d8 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. Unless the poisoned garment is removed, the saving throw repeats every 12 hours for the next 3 months.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-directed-delay", "title": "Directed Delay", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This thick black liquid, viscous as concentrated molasses, is delivered through a wound or injection. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or suffer the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-slow\">Slow</a> spell, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns. On a successful save, its movement Speed is instead reduced by 5 feet for 3 turns.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-lava-paste", "title": "Lava Paste", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This mundane-looking yellowish paste is applied to skin or clothing. The target must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d6 Fire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and become Vulnerable to fire damage for the next 12 hours; on a success, it takes half damage and avoids the vulnerability.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-malice", "title": "Malice", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled)</strong> &middot; Cost 250 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Blinded conditions for 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-noxious-transpiration", "title": "Noxious Transpiration", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This pale turquoise poison isn't dangerous to drink by itself, but starting 2 hours after ingestion, the drinker's sweat turns poisonous for 1 hour. Any contact with a patch of the drinker's skin roughly palm-sized or larger forces the toucher to succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 1d10+4 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>; a success avoids the damage entirely. Once a creature is exposed and takes no damage, it can't be affected by that dose again for 12 hours.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-pale-tincture", "title": "Pale Tincture", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 250 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution saving throw or take 3 (1d6) Poison damage and have the Poisoned condition. The Poisoned creature repeats the save every 24 hours, taking another 3 (1d6) Poison damage on each failure; none of this damage can be healed by any means while the creature remains Poisoned. After seven successful saves, the creature is no longer Poisoned and can heal normally.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-philter-of-love", "title": "Philter of Love", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>The next time you see a creature within 10 minutes after drinking this potion, you are <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-charmed\">Charmed</a> by that creature and have the Charmed condition for 1 hour.</p><p>This rose-hued, effervescent liquid contains one easy-to-miss bubble shaped like a heart.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>The next time you see a creature within 10 minutes after drinking this philter, you become charmed by that creature for 1 hour. If the creature is of a species and gender you are normally attracted to, you regard it as your true love while you are charmed. This potion's rose-hued, effervescent liquid contains one easy-to-miss bubble shaped like a heart.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-poison", "title": "Potion of Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This concoction looks, smells, and tastes exactly like a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"magic-item-potion-of-healing\">Potion of Healing</a> or other beneficial potion — only an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-identify\">Identify</a> spell reveals its true nature. Drinking it deals 4d6 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and forces a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition for 1 hour.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This concoction looks, smells, and tastes exactly like a Potion of Healing or other beneficial potion — only an Identify spell reveals its true nature. Drinking it deals 3d6 Poison damage and forces a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or the Poisoned condition; while poisoned this way, the drinker takes another 3d6 Poison damage at the start of each of its turns and can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, with each successful save reducing the damage taken on subsequent turns by 1d6 until it reaches 0.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-serpent-venom", "title": "Serpent Venom", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated giant poisonous snake. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or take 3d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-taratella-the-great-humiliator", "title": "Taratella: The Great Humiliator", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This murky, muddy brown liquid forces the drinker to succeed on a DC 14 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> indefinitely. While poisoned this way, the target experiences vivid dreams and occasional hallucinations of onlookers laughing at it, taking 1d4+1 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> every 6 hours. On a successful save, the target is instead poisoned for 2 days, taking only 2 Psychic damage every 6 hours. The only known cure is to dance as poorly as possible for 1 hour in a town square during daylight.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-truth-serum", "title": "Truth Serum", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 150 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition and be unable to speak a deliberate lie for 1 hour.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-poisons-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "equipment-burnt-othur-fumes", "title": "Burnt Othur Fumes", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled)</strong> &middot; Cost 500 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or take 10 (3d6) Poison damage, then repeat the saving throw at the start of each of its turns, taking 3 (1d6) Poison damage on each further failure. The poison ends after three successful saves.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-devil-s-powder", "title": "Devil's Powder", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Rare</strong></p><p>This hyper-fine red powder is blown into a target's face before dispersing harmlessly. The target must succeed on a DC 18 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or perceive the world for 1 hour as a hellscape crawling with foul creatures, becoming extremely susceptible to intimidation, aggressive persuasion, and deception during that time. On a successful save, the target instead feels only mild paranoia and skittishness.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dracula-s-essence", "title": "Dracula's Essence", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested, Injury), Rare</strong></p><p>Kept as a small vial of what looks like fresh blood, this poison turns to a still, rust-colored liquid once opened. If drunk, or if it enters the bloodstream through a wound or injection, the target must succeed on a DC 18 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or immediately vomit up everything in its stomach and take 2d10 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, becoming unable to sleep; on a success, it instead vomits and takes 2d8 Poison damage. An hour later, the target becomes supremely sensitive to direct sunlight, taking 1d4 Fire damage for every minute it spends outside of shade while not wearing Muroosa Balm, and craves nothing but raw meat and blood (especially its own species') — trying to eat or drink anything else forces it to vomit and take 1d6 Poison damage. Each hour it goes without raw meat or blood, it gains 1 level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a>. These effects last 24 hours.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-drider-poison", "title": "Drider Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Rare</strong></p><p>Harvested directly from a drider rather than brewed, this venom forces a creature hit by a weapon or piece of ammunition coated in it to succeed on a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 1 hour. If the save fails by 5 or more, the target is also <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-unconscious\">Unconscious</a> while poisoned this way. The target wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-essence-of-ether", "title": "Essence of Ether", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled)</strong> &middot; Cost 300 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Unconscious conditions for 8 hours. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-fire-plague", "title": "Fire Plague", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Rare</strong></p><p>This rose-orange powder is baked into bread or pastry. Eating at least a quarter of the treated food forces a DC 14 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the eater takes 1d6 Fire and 1d6 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, becomes <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>, and develops necrotic patches across its skin. While poisoned this way, it suffers vivid hallucinations of death and dying, and can remake the saving throw each morning; a success ends all the effects.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-forgetfulness", "title": "Forgetfulness", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Rare</strong></p><p>This fine, lavender powder forces anyone who breathes it in to succeed on a DC 14 Intelligence <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>. While poisoned this way, the target has <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on Intelligence <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> and checks, and must succeed on a DC 7 Intelligence check whenever it tries to recall anything that happened 4 or more weeks ago. It can repeat the saving throw at the start of every morning, ending the effect on a success.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-lolth-s-sting", "title": "Lolth's Sting", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. If it fails the save by 5 or more, it also has the Unconscious condition while Poisoned this way. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Called \"Drow Poison.\" A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. If it fails the save by 5 or more, it also falls Unconscious for the same duration. The creature wakes up if it takes damage.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-magebane", "title": "Magebane", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Rare</strong></p><p>Smelling of old boots despite its red-wine appearance, this poison grants the drinker the benefit of the Mage Slayer feat for 1 minute.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-magic-s-bane", "title": "Magic's Bane", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Rare</strong></p><p>This clear, colorless poison holds a purple, cloudy sphere that darts through it. Once it enters a creature's bloodstream, the target must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or its ability to cast spells is disrupted for 1 minute, requiring a successful DC 10 Arcana check each time it tries to cast one anyway; a success avoids the disruption entirely. The saving throw can be repeated at the end of each of the target's turns.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-oil-of-taggit", "title": "Oil of Taggit", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 400 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Unconscious conditions for 24 hours. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 400 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Unconscious conditions for 24 hours. The creature wakes up if it takes damage.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-thessaltoxin", "title": "Thessaltoxin", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Rare</strong></p><p>First distilled from the blood of the artificer Thessalar, this poison forces a creature struck by it to succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take on a new form as if affected by the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> spell — a random beast, or a creature it's seen within the last 24 hours, chosen by the DM. The transformation lasts until the end of the target's next long rest, and isn't cured by <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dispel-magic\">Dispel Magic</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-remove-curse\">Remove Curse</a>, though a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-greater-restoration\">Greater Restoration</a> spell restores the creature's true form.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-torpor", "title": "Torpor", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 600 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition and have its Speed halved for 4d6 hours.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 600 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Incapacitated conditions for 4d6 hours.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-poisons-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-armourer-s-blight", "title": "Armourer's Blight", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This harmless-seeming, pale green liquid is designed to turn armor into a death trap. Poured, smeared, or thrown onto a piece of armor, it seeps into the metal and forces the wearer to succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> at the start of each of its turns or take 4d6 Lightning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>; a success reduces the damage to 4. The poison lasts for 10 years and can only be removed by heating the metal to at least 700°F/1300°F.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-black-thistle-poison", "title": "Black Thistle Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact, Injury, Ingested via fumes), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This jet-black poison, suspended with metallic cobalt mica-like powder, releases faint purple fumes for up to 30 minutes once its ampule is opened, filling a 10-foot cube. Applied to weapons or up to 10 pieces of ammunition, it stays active for 30 minutes (or 3 minutes on ammunition), continuing to give off the same fumes during that time.</p><p>Exposure to the fumes for more than 12 seconds forces a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the creature takes 4 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a> for 30 seconds (2 Necrotic damage on a success); repeated brief exposure has no further effect for 12 hours. Exposure for 5 minutes or more in a day instead forces a DC 16 Constitution save, dealing 2d8 Necrotic damage and Blinding the creature for 5 days on a failure (half damage, no blindness on a success); a second cumulative 5 minutes of exposure deals 2d12 Necrotic damage and Blinds the creature permanently, curable only by regeneration magic or a potion, with no saving throw. Direct contact with the poison itself (blood or injection) is far more dangerous: a DC 18 Constitution save against 15+ minutes of fuming exposure, with a failure dealing 5d12 Necrotic damage and permanently Blinding and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafening</a> the creature, ruining its sense of smell and taste, and reducing its sense of touch by 80% for the rest of its life, with severe ongoing pain reducible only by regenerative magic or repeated Potions of Restoration; a success still deals 3d8 Necrotic damage and costs a sense (DM's choice) or reduces touch by 35% for 12 hours, curable the same way or with regenerative magic of a lower level.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-carrion-crawler-mucus", "title": "Carrion Crawler Mucus", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated carrion crawler. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Paralyzed conditions for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns to end the effect early.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Called \"Crawler Mucus.\" A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-coup-de-poudre", "title": "Coup de Poudre", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Very Rare</strong></p><p>Made from herbs, powdered human bones, and animal poisons, this concoction is the first step in turning a living <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> into a loyal Revenant. If ingested, the target must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 5d8 Necrotic and 5d8 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and fall into a death-like state at the stroke of midnight (half damage and no death-state on a success). A creature reduced to 0 hit points this way must be buried within 3 days and exhumed within 8 hours of burial, after which a 4-hour ritual binds its captured soul to the poisoner in a sealed jar; the body then reanimates as a Revenant that follows only verbal commands (given as a Bonus Action) in a language it understood in life, healing to full whenever it's midnight while the jar stays sealed and intact.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-deathsleep", "title": "Deathsleep", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Very Rare</strong></p><p>A creature that ingests this poison must succeed on a DC 19 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 24 hours, appearing dead for the duration. Only a successful DC 20 Medicine check can determine that the creature is merely poisoned rather than truly dead.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-essence-of-rage", "title": "Essence of Rage", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested, Injury), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This muddy brown poison turns bright, violent red when agitated with more than the lightest touch. Drinking it grants the Barbarian class's Rage feature for 30 seconds. If instead introduced through a wound or injection, the target must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be forced into that same Rage for 30 seconds, compelled to attack the nearest target with melee attacks; on a success, it gains the benefit of Rage voluntarily for 60 seconds instead. A forced target can attempt another saving throw starting on its second turn under the effect, ending it on a success. This poison has no effect on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-medusa-s-vengeance", "title": "Medusa's Vengeance", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This thick, grey poison is applied to weapons or ammunition, remaining active for 5 minutes on a weapon or 3 days on up to 20 pieces of ammunition (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> are unaffected by it). The third time a coated weapon draws blood from the same target, that target must succeed on a DC 16 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or begin petrifying: it loses 5 feet of Speed at the start of each of its next 3 turns and, over the following 15 minutes, becomes increasingly sluggish before turning fully to stone. Once a target succeeds on the saving throw, it's immune to this poison for the next minute.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-midnight-tears", "title": "Midnight Tears", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 1,500 GP per dose</p><p>A creature that ingests this poison suffers no effect until the stroke of midnight. If the poison hasn't been neutralized by then, the creature must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution saving throw or take 9d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-night-hag-s-curse", "title": "Night Hag's Curse", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested, Injury), Very Rare</strong></p><p>Meant to torment rather than kill, this clear, lilac poison forces a target who ingests it or has it injected into their blood to succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. On a success, the target suffers vivid nightmares for a week, taking 4 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> each morning upon waking. On a failure, the target's mind is permanently afflicted: it experiences night terrors that deal 2d10 Psychic damage upon waking each morning, and no longer automatically clears a level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> by completing a long rest — instead, the target rolls 1d100 each morning, restoring the level only on a 25 or lower, gaining a level instead on a 75 or higher, and seeing no change in between. The only cure is a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-greater-restoration\">Greater Restoration</a> spell of 6th level or higher, cast after the target drinks a Tea of Refreshment while it has no levels of Exhaustion.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sandman-s-revenge", "title": "Sandman's Revenge", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This yellowish, chunky powder is blown into a target's face. On contact, the target must succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d10 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and gain 3 levels of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a>; on a success, it takes 4 Necrotic damage and gains only 1 level of Exhaustion. Holding one's breath doesn't help, since the powder targets the nasal membranes; <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> are unaffected.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-water-of-death", "title": "Water of Death", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury, Ingested), Very Rare</strong></p><p>Looking, smelling, and tasting exactly like water, this poison defies even most magical and alchemical tests — only an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-identify\">Identify</a> spell cast at 7th level or higher, or 24 hours of detailed alchemical testing costing 300 gp, reveals what it truly is. Any contact with it forces a DC 20 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafened</a> for 48 hours and too wracked with pain to move for 24 hours, its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Point</a> maximum permanently reduced by 2d12 before it takes 7d10 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> 12 hours later. On a successful save, its hit point maximum is still permanently reduced by 2d12, and it has blurred vision and muffled hearing for 24 hours. The lost hit point maximum can only be restored by healing after drinking a Potion of Vitality, or by a Greater Restoration or Regenerate spell cast at 8th level or higher.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-poisons-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "equipment-purple-worm-poison", "title": "Purple Worm Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 2,000 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated purple worm. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 21 Constitution saving throw or take 10d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 2,000 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated purple worm. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 19 Constitution saving throw or take 12d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-wyvern-poison", "title": "Wyvern Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 1,200 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or take 7d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-staves", "title": "Staves", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-staves-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-staff-of-adornment", "title": "Staff of Adornment", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Common</strong></p><p>If you place an object weighing no more than 1 pound (such as a shard of crystal, an egg, or a stone) above the tip of the staff while holding it, the object floats an inch above the staff's tip and remains there until it is removed or until the staff leaves your possession. The staff can have up to three such objects floating above its tip at any given time. While holding the staff, you can cause one or more of the floating objects to slowly spin or turn in place.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-birdcalls", "title": "Staff of Birdcalls", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Common</strong></p><p>This wooden staff is decorated with bird carvings. It has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to create one of the following sounds out to a range of 60 feet: a finch's chirp, a raven's caw, a duck's quack, a chicken's cluck, a goose's honk, a loon's call, a turkey's gobble, a seagull's cry, an owl's hoot, or an eagle's shriek. The staff regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff explodes in a harmless cloud of feathers and is lost forever.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-flowers", "title": "Staff of Flowers", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Common</strong></p><p>This wooden staff has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to cause a flower to sprout from a patch of earth or soil within 5 feet of you, or from the staff itself. Unless you choose a specific kind of flower, the staff creates a mild-scented daisy. The flower is harmless and nonmagical, and it grows or withers as an ordinary flower would. The staff regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff turns into flower petals and is lost forever.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-staves-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-staff-of-the-adder", "title": "Staff of the Adder", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a Cleric, Druid, or Warlock)</p><p>You can use a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to speak this staff's command word, causing the head of the staff to become that of an animate poisonous snake for 1 minute. By using another Bonus Action to speak the command word again, you return the staff to its normal, inanimate form. Using the snake head, you can make a melee <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-action\">attack</a> against a target within the staff's 5-foot reach, adding your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-proficiency\">Proficiency</a> Bonus to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>. On a hit, the target takes 1d6 Piercing <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 3d6 Poison damage. While animate, the snake head can be attacked; it has an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">AC</a> of 15 and 20 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>. If it drops to 0 Hit Points, the staff is destroyed. As long as the staff isn't destroyed, the snake head regains all its lost Hit Points when it reverts to its inanimate form.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-the-python", "title": "Staff of the Python", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a Cleric, Druid, or Warlock)</p><p>You can use an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to speak this staff's command word and throw the staff on the ground within 10 feet of you. The staff becomes a Giant Constrictor Snake under your control and acts on its own initiative count in combat. By using a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to speak the command word again, you return the staff to its normal form in a space formerly occupied by the snake. On your turn, you can mentally command the snake if it's within 60 feet of you and you aren't <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> — you decide what action the snake takes and where it moves on its next turn, or you can issue it a general command, such as to attack your enemies or guard a location. If the snake is reduced to 0 Hit Points, it dies, reverts to its staff form, and the staff then shatters and is destroyed. If the snake reverts to its staff form before losing all its Hit Points, it regains all of them.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-staves-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-staff-of-charming", "title": "Staff of Charming", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard, Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>This staff has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-charm-person\">Charm Person</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-command\">Command</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-comprehend-languages\">Comprehend Languages</a> from it, using your spell save DC. The staff can also be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff. If you're holding it and fail a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> against an Enchantment spell that targets only you, you can turn that failed save into a success; once you do so, you can't use this property again until the next dawn. If you succeed on a save against an Enchantment spell that targets only you, with or without the staff's help, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to expend 1 charge and turn the spell back on its caster as if you had cast it yourself. The staff regains 1d8+2 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff becomes a nonmagical Quarterstaff.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-healing", "title": "Staff of Healing", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard, Cleric, or Druid)</p><p>This staff has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC and spellcasting ability: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-cure-wounds\">Cure Wounds</a> (1 charge per spell level, up to 4th), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lesser-restoration\">Lesser Restoration</a> (2 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-mass-cure-wounds\">Mass Cure Wounds</a> (5 charges). The staff regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff vanishes in a flash of light and is lost forever.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-swarming-insects", "title": "Staff of Swarming Insects", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard, Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>This staff has 10 charges and regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, a swarm of insects consumes and destroys the staff, then disperses. While holding the staff, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend some of its charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-giant-insect\">Giant Insect</a> (4 charges) or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-insect-plague\">Insect Plague</a> (5 charges) from it, using your spell save DC. You can also take an action and expend 1 charge to cause a swarm of harmless flying insects to spread out from you in a 30-foot radius; the swarm moves with you, remains for 10 minutes, and makes its area <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-heavily-obscured\">Heavily Obscured</a> for any creature but you. A wind of at least 10 miles per hour disperses the swarm and ends the effect.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-the-woodlands", "title": "Staff of the Woodlands", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Druid)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. While holding it, you have a +2 bonus to spell <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a>. The staff has 6 charges for the properties below, and regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff loses all its properties except its Quarterstaff bonus and becomes a nonmagical Quarterstaff with a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> While holding the staff, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animal-friendship\">Animal Friendship</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-awaken\">Awaken</a> (5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-barkskin\">Barkskin</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-locate-animals-or-plants\">Locate Animals or Plants</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-pass-without-trace\">Pass without Trace</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-speak-with-animals\">Speak with Animals</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-speak-with-plants\">Speak with Plants</a> (3 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-thorns\">Wall of Thorns</a> (6 charges).</p><p><strong>Tree Form.</strong> You can take an action, plant one end of the staff in fertile earth, and expend 1 charge to transform the staff into a healthy tree 60 feet tall with a 5-foot-diameter trunk and a 20-foot-radius canopy of branches and leaves. The tree looks ordinary but radiates a faint aura of Transmutation magic if targeted by <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-magic\">Detect Magic</a>. While touching the tree and using another action to speak its command word, you return the staff to its normal form; any creature in the tree falls when it reverts to a staff.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Druid)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. While holding it, you have a +2 bonus to spell attack rolls. The staff has 10 charges for the properties below, and regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff loses all its properties except its Quarterstaff bonus and becomes a nonmagical Quarterstaff with a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> While holding the staff, you can take an action and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC: Animal Friendship (1 charge), Awaken (5 charges), Barkskin (2 charges), Locate Animals or Plants (2 charges), Speak with Animals (1 charge), Speak with Plants (3 charges), or Wall of Thorns (6 charges). You can also take an action to cast Pass without Trace from the staff at no charge cost.</p><p><strong>Tree Form.</strong> You can take an action, plant one end of the staff in fertile earth, and expend 1 charge to transform the staff into a healthy tree 60 feet tall with a 5-foot-diameter trunk and a 20-foot-radius canopy of branches and leaves. The tree looks ordinary but radiates a faint aura of Transmutation magic if targeted by Detect Magic. While touching the tree and using another action to speak its command word, you return the staff to its normal form; any creature in the tree falls when it reverts to a staff.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-withering", "title": "Staff of Withering", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This staff has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. It can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff; on a hit, it deals damage as a normal Quarterstaff, and you can expend 1 charge to deal an extra 2d10 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> to the target and force it to make a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. On a failed save, the target has <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> for 1 hour on any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-ability-check\">ability check</a> or saving throw that uses Strength or Constitution.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Cleric, Druid, or Warlock)</p><p>This staff has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. It can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff; on a hit, it deals damage as a normal Quarterstaff, and you can expend 1 charge to deal an extra 2d10 Necrotic damage to the target and force it to make a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target has Disadvantage for 1 hour on any ability check or saving throw that uses Strength or Constitution.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-staves-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-staff-of-fire", "title": "Staff of Fire", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Fire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> while you hold this staff. The staff has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-burning-hands\">Burning Hands</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (3 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-fire\">Wall of Fire</a> (4 charges). The staff regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff blackens, crumbles into cinders, and is destroyed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-frost", "title": "Staff of Frost", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Cold <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> while you hold this staff. The staff has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-cone-of-cold\">Cone of Cold</a> (5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fog-cloud\">Fog Cloud</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-ice-storm\">Ice Storm</a> (4 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-ice\">Wall of Ice</a> (4 charges). The staff regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff turns to water and is destroyed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-power", "title": "Staff of Power", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. While holding it, you gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a>, and spell <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a>. The staff has 20 charges for the properties below. It regains 2d8+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff keeps its +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls but loses all other properties (including its remaining Retributive Strike). On a 20, the staff regains 1d8+2 charges.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> While holding the staff, you can take an action and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC and spell attack bonus: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-cone-of-cold\">Cone of Cold</a> (5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (5th-level version, 5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-globe-of-invulnerability\">Globe of Invulnerability</a> (6 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-hold-monster\">Hold Monster</a> (5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-levitate\">Levitate</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lightning-bolt\">Lightning Bolt</a> (5th-level version, 5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-missile\">Magic Missile</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-ray-of-enfeeblement\">Ray of Enfeeblement</a> (1 charge), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-force\">Wall of Force</a> (5 charges).</p><p><strong>Retributive Strike.</strong> You can take an action to break the staff over your knee or against a solid surface, releasing all its remaining magic in an explosion that fills a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on it. You have a 50 percent chance to instantly travel to a random plane of existence, avoiding the explosion; if you fail to avoid it, you take Force damage equal to 16 times the number of charges in the staff. The staff is destroyed. Every other creature in the area of the explosion must make a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw, taking 8 times the number of charges within 10 feet of the staff, 6 times the number of charges between 11 and 20 feet, or 4 times the number of charges between 21 and 30 feet, or taking half as much damage on a success.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Staff, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. While holding it, you gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class, saving throws, and spell attack rolls. The staff has 20 charges for the properties below. It regains 2d8+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff keeps its +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls but loses all other properties (including its remaining Retributive Strike and Power Strike). On a 20, the staff regains 1d8+2 charges.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> While holding the staff, you can take an action and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC and spell attack bonus: Cone of Cold (5 charges), Fireball (5th-level version, 5 charges), Globe of Invulnerability (6 charges), Hold Monster (5 charges), Levitate (2 charges), Lightning Bolt (5th-level version, 5 charges), Magic Missile (1 charge), Ray of Enfeeblement (1 charge), or Wall of Force (5 charges).</p><p><strong>Power Strike.</strong> When you hit with a melee attack using the staff, you can expend 1 charge to deal an extra 1d6 Force damage to the target.</p><p><strong>Retributive Strike.</strong> You can take an action to break the staff over your knee or against a solid surface, releasing all its remaining magic in an explosion that fills a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on it. You have a 50 percent chance to instantly travel to a random plane of existence, avoiding the explosion; if you fail to avoid it, you take Force damage equal to 16 times the number of charges in the staff. The staff is destroyed. Every other creature in the area of the explosion must make a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw, taking 8 times the number of charges within 10 feet of the staff, 6 times the number of charges between 11 and 20 feet, or 4 times the number of charges between 21 and 30 feet, or taking half as much damage on a success.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-striking", "title": "Staff of Striking", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. The staff has 10 charges. When you hit with a melee attack using it, you can expend up to 3 of its charges; for each charge expended, the target takes an extra 1d6 Force <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. The staff regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff becomes a nonmagical Quarterstaff.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-thunder-and-lightning", "title": "Staff of Thunder and Lightning", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. It also has the following properties. Once a property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Lightning.</strong> When you hit with a melee attack using the staff, you can cause the target to take an extra 2d6 Lightning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>.</p><p><strong>Thunder.</strong> When you hit with a melee attack using the staff, you can cause it to issue a crack of thunder, audible out to 300 feet. The target must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-stunned\">Stunned</a> until the end of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Lightning Strike.</strong> You can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to send a bolt of lightning leaping from the staff's tip in a line 5 feet wide and 120 feet long. Each creature in the line must make a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw, taking 9d6 Lightning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a success.</p><p><strong>Thunderclap.</strong> You can take an action to make the staff issue a deafening thunderclap, audible out to 600 feet. Each creature within 60 feet of you, other than you, must make a DC 17 Constitution saving throw, taking 2d6 Thunder damage and becoming <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafened</a> for 1 minute on a failed save, or taking half as much damage and remaining undeafened on a success.</p><p><strong>Thunder and Lightning.</strong> You can take an action to use the Lightning Strike and Thunderclap properties at the same time. Doing so uses only this combined property's daily use, not those of the two individual properties.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-staves-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-staff-of-the-magi", "title": "Staff of the Magi", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. While you hold it, you gain a +2 bonus to spell <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a>. The staff has 50 charges for the properties below, and regains 4d6+2 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 20, the staff regains 1d12+1 charges.</p><p><strong>Spell Absorption.</strong> While holding the staff, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on saving throws against spells. You can also use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> when another creature casts a spell that targets only you: if you do, the staff absorbs the magic of the spell, canceling its effect and gaining a number of charges equal to the absorbed spell's level. If this brings the staff's total charges above 50, the staff instead immediately triggers its Retributive Strike, as if you had activated it yourself.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> While holding the staff, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend some of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC and spellcasting ability: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-conjure-elemental\">Conjure Elemental</a> (7 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dispel-magic\">Dispel Magic</a> (3 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (7th-level version, 7 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-flaming-sphere\">Flaming Sphere</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-ice-storm\">Ice Storm</a> (4 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-invisibility\">Invisibility</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-knock\">Knock</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lightning-bolt\">Lightning Bolt</a> (7th-level version, 7 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-passwall\">Passwall</a> (5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-plane-shift\">Plane Shift</a> (7 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-telekinesis\">Telekinesis</a> (5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-fire\">Wall of Fire</a> (4 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-web\">Web</a> (2 charges). You can also take an action to cast, at no charge cost, one of the following spells from it: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-arcane-lock\">Arcane Lock</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-magic\">Detect Magic</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-enlarge-reduce\">Enlarge/Reduce</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-light\">Light</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-mage-hand\">Mage Hand</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-protection-from-evil-and-good\">Protection from Evil and Good</a>.</p><p><strong>Retributive Strike.</strong> You can take an action to break the staff over your knee or against a solid surface, releasing all its remaining magic in an explosion that fills a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on it. You have a 50 percent chance to instantly travel to a random plane of existence, avoiding the explosion; if you fail to avoid it, you take Force <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> equal to 16 times the number of charges in the staff. The staff is destroyed. Every other creature in the area of the explosion must make a DC 17 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 8 times the number of charges within 10 feet of the staff, 6 times the number of charges between 11 and 20 feet, or 4 times the number of charges between 21 and 30 feet, or taking half as much damage on a success.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-scrolls", "title": "Scrolls", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-spell-scroll", "title": "Spell Scroll", "html": "<p><strong>Scroll, Rarity Varies</strong></p><p>A Spell Scroll bears the words of a single spell, written in a mystical cipher. If the spell is on your spell list, you can read the scroll and cast its spell without providing Material components; otherwise, the scroll is unintelligible. Casting the spell this way takes the spell's normal casting time, and once the spell is cast, the scroll crumbles to dust — if the casting is interrupted, the scroll isn't lost.</p><p>If the spell is on your spell list but of a higher level than you can normally cast, you make an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-ability-check\">ability check</a> using your spellcasting ability to determine whether you cast it successfully. The DC equals 10 + the spell's level; on a failed check, the spell disappears from the scroll with no other effect.</p><p>The level of the spell held on the scroll sets its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">saving throw DC</a>, its attack bonus, and the scroll's own rarity, as shown below.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Spell Level</th><th>Rarity</th><th>Save DC</th><th>Attack Bonus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cantrip</td><td>Common</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>1st</td><td>Common</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Uncommon</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Uncommon</td><td>15</td><td>+7</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Rare</td><td>15</td><td>+7</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Rare</td><td>17</td><td>+9</td></tr><tr><td>6th</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>17</td><td>+9</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>18</td><td>+10</td></tr><tr><td>8th</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>18</td><td>+10</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Legendary</td><td>19</td><td>+11</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Copying a Scroll into a Spellbook.</strong> A Wizard spell on a Spell Scroll can be copied into a spellbook just as other spells can. The copier must succeed on an Intelligence (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-arcana\">Arcana</a>) check with a DC equal to 10 + the spell's level; on a success, the spell is copied. Whether the check succeeds or fails, the Spell Scroll is destroyed.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Scroll, Rarity Varies</strong></p><p>A Spell Scroll bears the words of a single spell, written in a mystical cipher. If the spell is on your class's spell list, you can use an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to read the scroll and cast its spell without providing any of the spell's components; otherwise, the scroll is unintelligible. Once the spell is cast, the words on the scroll fade and it crumbles to dust — if the casting is interrupted, the scroll isn't lost.</p><p>If the spell is on your class's spell list but of a higher level than you can normally cast, you must make an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-ability-check\">ability check</a> using your spellcasting ability to determine whether you cast it successfully. The DC equals 10 + the spell's level; on a failed check, the spell disappears from the scroll with no other effect.</p><p>The level of the spell held on the scroll sets its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">saving throw DC</a>, its attack bonus, and the scroll's own rarity, as shown below.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Spell Level</th><th>Rarity</th><th>Save DC</th><th>Attack Bonus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cantrip</td><td>Common</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>1st</td><td>Common</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Uncommon</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Uncommon</td><td>15</td><td>+7</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Rare</td><td>15</td><td>+7</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Rare</td><td>17</td><td>+9</td></tr><tr><td>6th</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>17</td><td>+9</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>18</td><td>+10</td></tr><tr><td>8th</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>18</td><td>+10</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Legendary</td><td>19</td><td>+11</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Copying a Scroll into a Spellbook.</strong> A Wizard spell on a Spell Scroll can be copied just as spells in spellbooks can be copied. The copier must succeed on an Intelligence (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-arcana\">Arcana</a>) check with a DC equal to 10 + the spell's level; on a success, the spell is copied. Whether the check succeeds or fails, the Spell Scroll is destroyed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-scroll-of-protection", "title": "Scroll of Protection", "html": "<p><strong>Scroll, Rare</strong></p><p>Each Scroll of Protection works against creatures of a specific type, chosen by the DM or determined by rolling on the table below.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Creature Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–10</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-aberration\">Aberrations</a></td></tr><tr><td>11–15</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-beast\">Beasts</a></td></tr><tr><td>16–20</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-celestial\">Celestials</a></td></tr><tr><td>21–25</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a></td></tr><tr><td>26–35</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragons</a></td></tr><tr><td>36–45</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-elemental\">Elementals</a></td></tr><tr><td>46–50</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoids</a></td></tr><tr><td>51–60</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fey\">Fey</a></td></tr><tr><td>61–70</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiends</a></td></tr><tr><td>71–75</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giants</a></td></tr><tr><td>76–80</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-monstrosity\">Monstrosities</a></td></tr><tr><td>81–85</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-ooze\">Oozes</a></td></tr><tr><td>86–90</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-plant\">Plants</a></td></tr><tr><td>91–00</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Using a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to read the scroll creates a 5-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a> originating from you. For 5 minutes, creatures of the specified type can't enter or affect anything in the area; however, if you move so that a creature of the specified type would end up inside the area, the effect ends.</p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, a creature within 5 feet of the Emanation can attempt to overcome it, forcing it to make a DC 15 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-charisma\">Charisma</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. On a success, the creature ceases to be affected by the Emanation.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Scroll, Rare</strong></p><p>Each Scroll of Protection works against creatures of one of eight types, chosen by the DM or determined at random: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-aberration\">Aberrations</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-beast\">Beasts</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-celestial\">Celestials</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-elemental\">Elementals</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fey\">Fey</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiends</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-plant\">Plants</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a>.</p><p>Using an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to read the scroll encloses you in an invisible barrier that extends from you to form a 5-foot-radius, 10-foot-high cylinder. For 5 minutes, this barrier prevents creatures of the specified type from entering or affecting anything within it; the cylinder moves with you and remains centered on you, but if you move in such a way that a creature of the specified type would end up inside it, the effect ends.</p><p>A creature can attempt to overcome the barrier by using an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to make a DC 15 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-charisma\">Charisma</a> check. On a success, the creature ceases to be affected by the barrier.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-armor", "title": "Armor", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-armor-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-armor-of-gleaming", "title": "Armor of Gleaming", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Common</strong></p><p>This armor never gets dirty.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-cast-off-armor", "title": "Cast-Off Armor", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Common</strong></p><p>You can doff this armor as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-shield-of-expression", "title": "Shield of Expression", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Common</strong></p><p>The front of this Shield is shaped like a face. While bearing the Shield, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to change the face's expression.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-smoldering-armor", "title": "Smoldering Armor", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Common</strong></p><p>Wisps of harmless, odorless smoke rise from this armor while it is worn.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-armor-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-adamantine-armor", "title": "Adamantine Armor", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Medium or Heavy, Except Hide Armor), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This armor is reinforced with adamantine, one of the hardest substances in existence. While you wear it, any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-critical-hit\">Critical Hit</a> against you becomes a normal hit.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-mariner-s-armor", "title": "Mariner's Armor", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you have a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-swim-speed\">Swim Speed</a> equal to your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a>. In addition, if you start your turn underwater with 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>, you immediately regain 1d4 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>. The armor can't heal anyone again until the next dawn.</p><p>The armor is decorated with fish and shell motifs.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-mithral-armor", "title": "Mithral Armor", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Medium or Heavy, Except Hide Armor), Uncommon</strong></p><p>Mithral is a light, flexible metal, and armor made from it can be worn under normal clothes. If the armor normally imposes <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on Dexterity (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-stealth\">Stealth</a>) checks or has a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-strength\">Strength</a> requirement, the mithral version of the armor doesn't.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sentinel-shield", "title": "Sentinel Shield", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Uncommon</strong></p><p>While holding this Shield, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> rolls and Wisdom (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-perception\">Perception</a>) checks. The Shield is emblazoned with a symbol of an eye.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-shield-1", "title": "Shield, +1", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Uncommon</strong></p><p>While holding this Shield, you have a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, in addition to the Shield's normal bonus to AC.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-armor-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-armor-1", "title": "Armor, +1", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you have a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-armor-of-resistance", "title": "Armor of Resistance", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to one type of damage while you wear this armor. The DM chooses the type or determines it randomly by rolling on the following table.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d10</th><th>Damage Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Force</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Necrotic</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Psychic</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Radiant</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Thunder</td></tr></tbody></table>"}, {"id": "magic-item-armor-of-vulnerability", "title": "Armor of Vulnerability", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this armor, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to one of the following damage types: Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing. The DM chooses the type or determines it randomly.</p><p><strong>Curse.</strong> This armor is cursed, a fact that is revealed only when the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-identify\">Identify</a> spell is cast on the armor or you attune to it. Attuning to the armor curses you until you are targeted by a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-remove-curse\">Remove Curse</a> spell or similar magic; removing the armor fails to end the curse. While cursed, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-vulnerability\">Vulnerability</a> to the other two of the three damage types associated with the armor (not the one to which it grants Resistance).</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-arrow-catching-shield", "title": "Arrow-Catching Shield", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a> against ranged <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> while you wield this Shield. This bonus is in addition to the Shield's normal bonus to AC.</p><p>Whenever an attacker makes a ranged attack roll against a target within 5 feet of you, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to become the target of the attack instead.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-elven-chain", "title": "Elven Chain", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Chain Mail or Chain Shirt), Rare</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a> while you wear this armor. You are considered trained with this armor even if you lack training with Medium or Heavy armor.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Armor (Chain Shirt), Rare</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to AC while you wear this armor. You are considered proficient with this armor even if you lack proficiency with medium armor.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-glamoured-studded-leather", "title": "Glamoured Studded Leather", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Studded Leather Armor), Rare</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>. You can also take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to cause the armor to assume the appearance of a normal set of clothing or some other kind of armor. You decide what it looks like, including color, style, and accessories, but the armor retains its normal bulk and weight. The illusory appearance lasts until you use this property again or doff the armor.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-shield-2", "title": "Shield, +2", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Rare</strong></p><p>While holding this Shield, you have a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, in addition to the Shield's normal bonus to AC.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-shield-of-missile-attraction", "title": "Shield of Missile Attraction", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While holding this Shield, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> from attacks made with Ranged weapons.</p><p><strong>Curse.</strong> This Shield is cursed. Attuning to it curses you until you are targeted by a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-remove-curse\">Remove Curse</a> spell or similar magic. Removing the Shield fails to end the curse on you. Whenever an attack with a Ranged weapon targets a creature within 10 feet of you, the curse causes you to become the target instead.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-armor-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-animated-shield", "title": "Animated Shield", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While holding this Shield, you can speak its command word as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to cause it to animate. The Shield leaps into the air and hovers in your space to protect you as if you were wielding it, leaving your hands free. The Shield remains animated for 1 minute, until you use a Bonus Action to end this effect, or until you have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> condition or die, at which point the Shield falls to the ground or into your hand if you have one free.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-armor-2", "title": "Armor, +2", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Very Rare</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you have a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-demon-armor", "title": "Demon Armor", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Plate Armor), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, and you know Abyssal. In addition, the armor's clawed gauntlets allow your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-unarmed-strike\">Unarmed Strikes</a> to deal 1d8 Slashing damage instead of the usual Bludgeoning damage, and you gain a +1 bonus to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> of your Unarmed Strikes.</p><p><strong>Curse.</strong> Once you don this cursed armor, you can't doff it unless you are targeted by a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-remove-curse\">Remove Curse</a> spell or similar magic. While wearing the armor, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on attack rolls against demons and on saving throws against their spells and special abilities.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dragon-scale-mail", "title": "Dragon Scale Mail", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Scale Mail), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Dragon Scale Mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> against the breath weapons of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragons</a>, and you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to one damage type determined by the kind of dragon that provided the scales (see the table).</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Dragon</th><th>Resistance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>Cold</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Additionally, you can focus your senses as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to discern the distance and direction to the closest dragon within 30 miles of you that is of the same type as the armor. This action can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Armor (Scale Mail), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Dragon scale mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC, you have advantage on saving throws against the Frightful Presence and breath weapons of dragons, and you have resistance to one damage type determined by the kind of dragon that provided the scales (see the table).</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Dragon</th><th>Resistance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>Cold</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Additionally, you can focus your senses as an action to magically discern the distance and direction to the closest dragon within 30 miles of you that is of the same type as the armor. This special action can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dwarven-plate", "title": "Dwarven Plate", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Half Plate Armor or Plate Armor), Very Rare</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>. In addition, if an effect moves you against your will along the ground, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to reduce the distance you are moved by up to 10 feet.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Armor (Plate), Very Rare</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you gain a +2 bonus to AC. In addition, if an effect moves you against your will along the ground, you can use your reaction to reduce the distance you are moved by up to 10 feet.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-shield-3", "title": "Shield, +3", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Very Rare</strong></p><p>While holding this Shield, you have a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, in addition to the Shield's normal bonus to AC.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-spellguard-shield", "title": "Spellguard Shield", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While holding this Shield, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> against spells and other magical effects, and spell attack rolls have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> against you.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-armor-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-armor-3", "title": "Armor, +3", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Legendary</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you have a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-armor-of-invulnerability", "title": "Armor of Invulnerability", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Plate Armor), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage while you wear this armor.</p><p><strong>Metal Shell.</strong> You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to give yourself <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-immunity\">Immunity</a> to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage for 10 minutes or until you are no longer wearing the armor. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Armor (Plate), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You have resistance to nonmagical damage while you wear this armor. Additionally, you can use an action to make yourself immune to nonmagical damage for 10 minutes or until you are no longer wearing the armor. Once this special action is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-plate-armor-of-etherealness", "title": "Plate Armor of Etherealness", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Plate Armor), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you're wearing this armor, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and use a command word to gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-etherealness\">Etherealness</a> spell. The spell ends immediately if you remove the armor or take a Magic action to repeat the command word. This property of the armor can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-weapons", "title": "Weapons", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-weapons-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-moon-touched-sword", "title": "Moon-Touched Sword", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Common</strong></p><p>In darkness, the unsheathed blade of this weapon sheds moonlight, creating <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bright-light\">Bright Light</a> in a 15-foot radius and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> for an additional 15 feet.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sylvan-talon", "title": "Sylvan Talon", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Dagger, Rapier, Scimitar, Shortsword, Sickle, or Spear), Common</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While this weapon is on your person, you understand the nonwritten communication of all <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fey\">Fey</a>, and they understand yours.</p><p><strong>Secret Message.</strong> As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can use the weapon to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-message\">Message</a>. Once this property is used, it can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-weapons-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-adamantine-weapon", "title": "Adamantine Weapon", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Ammunition or Melee Weapon), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This weapon or piece of ammunition is made of adamantine, one of the hardest substances in existence. Whenever it hits an object, the hit is a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-critical-hit\">Critical Hit</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-javelin-of-lightning", "title": "Javelin of Lightning", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Javelin), Uncommon</strong></p><p>Each time you make an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> with this magic weapon and hit, you can have it deal Lightning damage instead of Piercing damage.</p><p><strong>Lightning Bolt.</strong> When you throw this weapon at a target no farther than 120 feet from you, you can forgo making a ranged <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> and instead turn the weapon into a bolt of lightning. This bolt forms a 5-foot-wide <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-line\">Line</a> between you and the target. The target and each other creature in the Line (excluding you) makes a DC 13 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 4d6 Lightning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. Immediately after dealing this damage, the weapon reappears in your hand. This property can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (javelin), Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you hurl this magic javelin and speak its command word, it transforms into a bolt of lightning, forming a 5-foot-wide <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-line\">line</a> that extends from you to a target within 120 feet. Each creature in the line excluding you and the target must make a DC 13 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 4d6 Lightning damage on a failed save and half as much damage on a successful one. The lightning bolt turns back into a javelin when it reaches the target. Make a ranged weapon attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes damage from the javelin plus 4d6 Lightning damage.</p><p>The javelin’s property can’t be used again until the next dawn. In the meantime, the javelin can still be used as a magic weapon.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sword-of-vengeance", "title": "Sword of Vengeance", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p><strong>Curse.</strong> This weapon is cursed and possessed by a vengeful spirit. Becoming attuned to it extends the curse to you. As long as you remain cursed, you are unwilling to part with the weapon, keeping it on your person at all times. While attuned to this weapon, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> made with weapons other than this one.</p><p>In addition, while the weapon is on your person, you must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> whenever you take damage from another creature in combat. On a failed save, you must attack the creature that damaged you until you drop to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> or it does, or until you can’t reach the creature to make a melee attack against it.</p><p>You can break the curse in the usual ways. Alternatively, casting <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-banishment\">Banishment</a> on the weapon forces the vengeful spirit to leave it. The weapon then becomes a +1 weapon with no other properties.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p><strong>Curse.</strong> This sword is cursed and possessed by a vengeful spirit. Becoming attuned to it extends the curse to you. As long as you remain cursed, you are unwilling to part with the sword, keeping it on your person at all times. While attuned to this weapon, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> made with weapons other than this one.</p><p>In addition, while the sword is on your person, you must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> whenever you take damage in combat. On a failed save, you must attack the creature that damaged you until you drop to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> or it does, or until you can’t reach the creature to make a melee attack against it.</p><p>You can break the curse in the usual ways. Alternatively, casting <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-banishment\">Banishment</a> on the sword forces the vengeful spirit to leave it. The sword then becomes a +1 weapon with no other properties.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-trident-of-fish-command", "title": "Trident of Fish Command", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Trident), Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This magic weapon has 3 charges, and it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While you carry it, you can expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dominate-beast\">Dominate Beast</a> (save DC 15) from it on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-beast\">Beast</a> that has a Swim Speed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-weapon-of-warning", "title": "Weapon of Warning", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>As long as this weapon is within your reach and you are attuned to it, you and allies within 30 feet of you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Alarm.</strong> The weapon magically awakens each subject who is sleeping naturally when combat begins. This benefit doesn’t wake a subject from magically induced sleep.</p><p><strong>Supernatural Readiness.</strong> Each subject has <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> rolls.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any), Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This magic weapon warns you of danger. While the weapon is on your person, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> rolls. In addition, you and any of your companions within 30 feet of you can’t be surprised, except when incapacitated by something other than nonmagical sleep. The weapon magically awakens you and your companions within range if any of you are sleeping naturally when combat begins.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-weapon-1", "title": "Weapon, +1", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Uncommon</strong></p><p>You have a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-weapons-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-berserker-axe", "title": "Berserker Axe", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Battleaxe, Greataxe, or Halberd), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. In addition, while you are attuned to this weapon, your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Point</a> maximum increases by 1 for each level you have attained.</p><p><strong>Curse.</strong> This weapon is cursed, and becoming attuned to it extends the curse to you. As long as you remain cursed, you are unwilling to part with the weapon, keeping it within reach at all times. You also have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> with weapons other than this one.</p><p>Whenever another creature damages you while the weapon is in your possession, you must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or go berserk. This berserk state ends when you start your turn and there are no creatures within 60 feet of you that you can see or hear.</p><p>While berserk, you regard the creature nearest to you that you can see or hear as your enemy. If there are multiple possible creatures, choose one at random. On each of your turns, you must move as close to the creature as possible and take the Attack action, targeting the creature. If you’re unable to get close enough to the creature to attack it with the weapon, your turn ends after you’ve used up all your available movement. If the creature dies or can no longer be seen or heard by you, the next nearest creature that you can see or hear becomes your new target.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any axe), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. In addition, while you are attuned to this weapon, your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Point</a> maximum increases by 1 for each level you have attained.</p><p><strong>Curse.</strong> This axe is cursed, and becoming attuned to it extends the curse to you. As long as you remain cursed, you are unwilling to part with the axe, keeping it within reach at all times. You also have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> with weapons other than this one, unless no foe is within 60 feet of you that you can see or hear.</p><p>Whenever a hostile creature damages you while the axe is in your possession, you must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or go berserk. While berserk, you must use your action each round to attack the creature nearest to you with the axe. If you can make extra attacks as part of the Attack action, you use those extra attacks, moving to attack the next nearest creature after you fell your current target. If you have multiple possible targets, you attack one at random. You are berserk until you start your turn with no creatures within 60 feet of you that you can see or hear.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dagger-of-venom", "title": "Dagger of Venom", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Dagger), Rare</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to magically coat the blade with poison. The poison remains for 1 minute or until an attack using this weapon hits a creature. That creature must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d10 Poison damage and have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition for 1 minute. The weapon can’t be used this way again until the next dawn.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (dagger), Rare</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p>You can use an action to cause thick, black poison to coat the blade. The poison remains for 1 minute or until an attack using this weapon hits a creature. That creature must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d10 Poison damage and have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition for 1 minute. The dagger can’t be used this way again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dragon-slayer", "title": "Dragon Slayer", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Rare</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p>The weapon deals an extra 3d6 damage of the weapon’s type if the target is a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragon</a>.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Rare</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p>When you hit a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragon</a> with this weapon, the dragon takes an extra 3d6 damage of the weapon’s type. For the purpose of this weapon, “dragon” refers to any creature with the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragon</a> type, including dragon turtles and wyverns.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-flame-tongue", "title": "Flame Tongue", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Melee Weapon), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While holding this magic weapon, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> and use a command word to cause flames to engulf the damage-dealing part of the weapon. These flames shed <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bright-light\">Bright Light</a> in a 40-foot radius and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> for an additional 40 feet. While the weapon is ablaze, it deals an extra 2d6 Fire damage on a hit. The flames last until you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to issue the command again or until you drop, stow, or sheathe the weapon.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You can use a bonus action to speak this magic sword’s command word, causing flames to erupt from the blade. These flames shed bright light in a 40-foot radius and dim light for an additional 40 feet. While the sword is ablaze, it deals an extra 2d6 Fire damage to any target it hits. The flames last until you use a bonus action to speak the command word again or until you drop or sheathe the sword.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-giant-slayer", "title": "Giant Slayer", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Rare</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p>When you hit a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a> with this weapon, the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a> takes an extra 2d6 damage of the weapon’s type and must succeed on a DC 15 Strength <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a> condition.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any axe or sword), Rare</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p>When you hit a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a> with it, the giant takes an extra 2d6 damage of the weapon’s type and must succeed on a DC 15 Strength <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a> condition. For the purpose of this weapon, “giant” refers to any creature with the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a> type, including ettins and trolls.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-mace-of-disruption", "title": "Mace of Disruption", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Mace), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>When you hit a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiend</a> or an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> with this magic weapon, that creature takes an extra 2d6 Radiant damage. If the target has 25 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> or fewer after taking this damage, it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be destroyed. On a successful save, the creature has the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> condition until the end of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Light.</strong> While you hold this weapon, it sheds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bright-light\">Bright Light</a> in a 20-foot radius and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> for an additional 20 feet.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-mace-of-smiting", "title": "Mace of Smiting", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Mace), Rare</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. The bonus increases to +3 when you use the weapon to attack a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a>.</p><p>When you roll a 20 on an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> made with this weapon, the target takes an extra 7 Bludgeoning damage, or 14 Bludgeoning damage if it’s a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a>. If a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a> has 25 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> or fewer after taking this damage, it is destroyed.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (mace), Rare</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. The bonus increases to +3 when you use the mace to attack a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a>.</p><p>When you roll a 20 on an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> made with this weapon, the target takes an extra 2d6 Bludgeoning damage, or 4d6 Bludgeoning damage if it’s a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a>. If a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a> has 25 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> or fewer after taking this damage, it is destroyed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-mace-of-terror", "title": "Mace of Terror", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Mace), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This magic weapon has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding the weapon, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and expend 1 charge to release a wave of terror from it. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> condition for 1 minute. While <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> in this way, a creature must spend its turns trying to move as far away from you as it can, and it can’t make <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-opportunity-attacks\">Opportunity Attacks</a>. For its action, it can use only the Dash action or try to escape from an effect that prevents it from moving. If it has nowhere it can move, the creature can take the Dodge action. At the end of each of its turns, a creature repeats the save, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (mace), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This magic weapon has 3 charges. While holding it, you can use an action and expend 1 charge to release a wave of terror. Each creature of your choice in a 30-foot radius extending from you must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> of you for 1 minute. While it is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> in this way, a creature must spend its turns trying to move as far away from you as it can, and it can’t willingly move to a space within 30 feet of you. It also can’t take Reactions. For its action, it can use only the Dash action or try to escape from an effect that prevents it from moving. If it has nowhere it can move, the creature can use the Dodge action. At the end of each of its turns, a creature can repeat the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p><p>The mace regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sun-blade", "title": "Sun Blade", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Longsword), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This item appears to be a sword hilt.</p><p><strong>Blade of Radiance.</strong> While grasping the hilt, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to cause a blade of pure radiance to spring into existence or make the blade disappear. While the blade exists, this magic weapon functions as a Longsword with the Finesse property. If you are proficient with Longswords or Shortswords, you are proficient with the Sun Blade.</p><p>You gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this weapon, which deals Radiant damage instead of Slashing damage. When you hit an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> with it, that target takes an extra 1d8 Radiant damage.</p><p><strong>Sunlight.</strong> The sword’s luminous blade emits <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bright-light\">Bright Light</a> in a 15-foot radius and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> for an additional 15 feet. The light is sunlight. While the blade persists, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to expand or reduce its radius of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bright-light\">Bright Light</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> by 5 feet each, to a maximum of 30 feet each or a minimum of 10 feet each.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sword-of-life-stealing", "title": "Sword of Life Stealing", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>When you attack a creature with this magic weapon and roll a 20 on the d20 for the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, that target takes an extra 15 Necrotic damage if it isn’t a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a> or an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a>, and you gain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-temporary-hp\">Temporary Hit Points</a> equal to the amount of Necrotic damage taken.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>When you attack a creature with this magic weapon and roll a 20 on the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, that target takes an extra 3d6 Necrotic damage, provided that the target isn’t a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a> or an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a>. You gain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-temporary-hp\">Temporary Hit Points</a> equal to the extra damage dealt.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sword-of-wounding", "title": "Sword of Wounding", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>When you hit a creature with an attack using this magic weapon, the target takes an extra 2d6 Necrotic damage and must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be unable to regain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> for 1 hour. The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> lost to this weapon’s damage can be regained only through a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-short-rest\">Short Rest</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-long-rest\">Long Rest</a>, rather than by regeneration, magic, or any other means.</p><p>Once per turn, when you hit a creature with an attack using this magic weapon, you can wound the target. At the start of each of the wounded creature’s turns, it takes 1d4 Necrotic damage for each time you’ve wounded it, and it can then make a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, ending the effect of all such wounds on itself on a success. Alternatively, the wounded creature, or a creature within 5 feet of it, can use an action to make a DC 15 Wisdom (Medicine) check, ending the effect of such wounds on it on a success.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-vicious-weapon", "title": "Vicious Weapon", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Rare</strong></p><p>This magic weapon deals an extra 2d6 damage to any creature it hits. This extra damage is of the same type as the weapon’s normal damage.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any), Rare</strong></p><p>When you roll a 20 on your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> with this magic weapon, your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-critical-hit\">Critical Hit</a> deals an extra 2d6 damage of the weapon’s type.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-weapon-2", "title": "Weapon, +2", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Rare</strong></p><p>You have a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-weapons-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-dancing-sword", "title": "Dancing Sword", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to toss this magic weapon into the air. When you do so, the weapon begins to hover, flies up to 30 feet, and attacks one creature of your choice within 5 feet of itself. The weapon uses your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> and adds your ability modifier to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a>.</p><p>While the weapon hovers, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to cause it to fly up to 30 feet to another spot within 30 feet of you. As part of the same <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>, you can cause the weapon to attack one creature within 5 feet of the weapon.</p><p>After the hovering weapon attacks for the fourth time, it flies back to you and tries to return to your hand. If you have no hand free, the weapon falls to the ground in your space. If the weapon has no unobstructed path to you, it moves as close to you as it can and then falls to the ground. It also ceases to hover if you grasp it or are more than 30 feet away from it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dwarven-thrower", "title": "Dwarven Thrower", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Warhammer), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. It has the Thrown property with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. When you hit with a ranged attack using this weapon, it deals an extra 1d8 Force damage, or an extra 2d8 Force damage if the target is a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a>. Immediately after hitting or missing, the weapon flies back to your hand.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (warhammer), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a dwarf)</p><p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. It has the Thrown property with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. When you hit with a ranged attack using this weapon, it deals an extra 1d8 damage or, if the target is a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a>, 2d8 damage. Immediately after the attack, the weapon flies back to your hand.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-frost-brand", "title": "Frost Brand", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>When you hit with an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> using this magic weapon, the target takes an extra 1d6 Cold damage. In addition, while you hold the weapon, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Fire damage.</p><p>In freezing temperatures, the weapon sheds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bright-light\">Bright Light</a> in a 10-foot radius and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> for an additional 10 feet.</p><p>When you draw this weapon, you can extinguish all nonmagical flames within 30 feet of yourself. Once used, this property can’t be used again for 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-nine-lives-stealer", "title": "Nine Lives Stealer", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p><strong>Life Stealing.</strong> The weapon has 1d8 + 1 charges. When you attack a creature that has fewer than 100 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> with this weapon and roll a 20 on the d20 for the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, the creature must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be slain instantly as the weapon tears its life force from its body. Constructs and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> succeed on the save automatically. The weapon loses 1 charge if the creature is slain. When the weapon has no charges remaining, it loses this property.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p>The sword has 1d8 + 1 charges. If you score a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-critical-hit\">Critical Hit</a> against a creature that has fewer than 100 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>, it must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be slain instantly as the sword tears its life force from its body (a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a> or an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> is immune). The sword loses 1 charge if the creature is slain. When the sword has no charges remaining, it loses this property.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-oathbow", "title": "Oathbow", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Longbow or Shortbow), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>When you nock an arrow on this bow, it whispers in Elvish, “Swift defeat to my enemies.” When you use this weapon to make a ranged attack, you can utter or sign the following command words: “Swift death to you who have wronged me.” The target of your attack becomes your sworn enemy until it dies or until dawn 7 days later. You can have only one such sworn enemy at a time. When your sworn enemy dies, you can choose a new one after the next dawn.</p><p>When you make a ranged <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> with this weapon against your sworn enemy, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on the roll. In addition, your target gains no benefit from <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-half-cover\">Half Cover</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-three-quarters-cover\">Three-Quarters Cover</a>, and you suffer no <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> due to long range. If the attack hits, your sworn enemy takes an extra 3d6 Piercing damage.</p><p>While your sworn enemy lives, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> with all other weapons.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-quarterstaff-of-the-acrobat", "title": "Quarterstaff of the Acrobat", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Quarterstaff), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You have a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p>While holding this weapon, you can cause it to emit green <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> out to 10 feet, either as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> or after you roll <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a>, or you can extinguish the light as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>.</p><p>While holding this weapon, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to alter its form, turning it into a 6-inch rod (for ease of storage) or a 10-foot pole, or reverting it to a Quarterstaff; the weapon elongates only as far as the surrounding space allows.</p><p>In certain forms, the weapon has the following additional properties.</p><p><strong>Acrobatic Assist (Quarterstaff or 10-Foot Pole Forms Only).</strong> While holding this weapon, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks.</p><p><strong>Attack Deflection (Quarterstaff Form Only).</strong> When you are hit by an attack while holding the weapon, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to twirl the weapon around you, gaining a +5 bonus to your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a> against the triggering attack, potentially causing the attack to miss you. You can’t use this property again until you finish a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-short-rest\">Short Rest</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-long-rest\">Long Rest</a>.</p><p><strong>Ranged Weapon (Quarterstaff Form Only).</strong> This weapon has the Thrown property with a normal range of 30 feet and a long range of 120 feet. Immediately after you make a ranged attack with the weapon, it flies back to your hand.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-scimitar-of-speed", "title": "Scimitar of Speed", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Scimitar), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. In addition, you can make one attack with it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> on each of your turns.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sword-of-sharpness", "title": "Sword of Sharpness", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, or Scimitar), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>When you attack an object with this magic weapon and hit, maximize your weapon damage dice against the target.</p><p>When you attack a creature with this weapon and roll a 20 on the d20 for the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, that target takes an extra 14 Slashing damage and gains 1 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> level.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any sword that deals slashing damage), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>When you attack an object with this magic sword and hit, maximize your weapon damage dice against the target.</p><p>When you attack a creature with this weapon and roll a 20 on the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, that target takes an extra 4d6 Slashing damage. Then roll another d20. If you roll a 20, you lop off one of the target’s limbs, with the effect of such loss determined by the DM. If the creature has no limb to sever, you lop off a portion of its body instead.</p><p>In addition, you can speak the sword’s command word to cause the blade to shed bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet. Speaking the command word again or sheathing the sword puts out the light.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-thunderous-greatclub", "title": "Thunderous Greatclub", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Greatclub), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you are attuned to this magic weapon, your Strength is 20 unless your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score. The weapon deals an extra 1d8 Thunder damage to any creature it hits and an extra 3d8 Thunder damage to objects it hits that aren’t being worn or carried.</p><p>The weapon has the following additional properties.</p><p><strong>Clap of Thunder.</strong> As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can strike the weapon against a hard surface to create a loud clap of thunder audible out to 300 feet. You also create a 30-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-cone\">Cone</a> of thunderous energy. Each creature in the Cone must succeed on a DC 15 Strength <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a> condition. Nonmagical objects in the Cone that aren’t being worn or carried take 3d8 Thunder damage.</p><p><strong>Earthquake.</strong> As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can strike the weapon against the ground to create an intense seismic disturbance in a 50-foot-radius circle centered on the point of impact. Structures in contact with the ground in that area take 50 Bludgeoning damage, and each creature on the ground in that area must succeed on a DC 20 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a> condition. If that creature is also concentrating, it must succeed on a DC 20 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a> is broken. In addition, you can cause a 30-foot-deep, 10-foot-wide fissure to open up on the ground anywhere in the area. Any structure on a spot where the fissure opens collapses into the fissure. Once you use this property, it can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-weapon-3", "title": "Weapon, +3", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Very Rare</strong></p><p>You have a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-weapons-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-defender", "title": "Defender", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Melee Weapon), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p>The first time you attack with the weapon on each of your turns, you can transfer some or all of the weapon’s bonus to your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>. For example, you could reduce the bonus to your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> to +1 and gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>. The adjusted bonuses remain in effect until the start of your next turn, although you must hold the weapon to gain a bonus to AC from it.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p>The first time you attack with the sword on each of your turns, you can transfer some or all of the sword’s bonus to your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, instead of using the bonus on any attacks that turn. For example, you could reduce the bonus to your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> to +1 and gain a +2 bonus to AC. The adjusted bonuses remain in effect until the start of your next turn, although you must hold the sword to gain a bonus to AC from it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-hammer-of-thunderbolts", "title": "Hammer of Thunderbolts", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Maul or Warhammer), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p>The weapon has 5 charges. You can expend 1 charge and make a ranged attack with the weapon, hurling it as if it had the Thrown property with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. If the attack hits, the weapon unleashes a thunderclap audible out to 300 feet. The target and every creature within 30 feet of it other than you must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-stunned\">Stunned</a> condition until the end of your next turn. Immediately after hitting or missing, the weapon flies back to your hand. The weapon regains 1d4 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn.</p><p><strong>Giant’s Bane.</strong> While you are attuned to the weapon and wearing either a Belt of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a> Strength or Gauntlets of Ogre Power to which you are also attuned, you gain the following benefits:</p><p><strong>Giants’ Bane.</strong> When you roll a 20 on the d20 for an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> made with this weapon against a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a>, the creature must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or die.</p><p><strong>Might of Giants.</strong> The Strength score bestowed by your Belt of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a> Strength or Gauntlets of Ogre Power increases by 4, to a maximum of 30.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (maul), Legendary</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p><p><strong>Giant’s Bane (Requires Attunement).</strong> You must be wearing a Belt of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a> Strength (any variety) and Gauntlets of Ogre Power to attune to this weapon. The attunement ends if you take off either of those items. While you are attuned to this weapon and holding it, your Strength score increases by 4 and can exceed 20, but not 30. When you roll a 20 on an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> made with this weapon against a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a>, the giant must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or die.</p><p>The hammer also has 5 charges. While attuned to it, you can expend 1 charge and make a ranged weapon attack with the hammer, hurling it as if it had the Thrown property with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. If the attack hits, the hammer unleashes a thunderclap audible out to 300 feet. The target and every creature within 30 feet of it must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-stunned\">Stunned</a> condition until the end of your next turn. The hammer regains 1d4 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-holy-avenger", "title": "Holy Avenger", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement by a Paladin)</p><p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. When you hit a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiend</a> or an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> with it, that creature takes an extra 2d10 Radiant damage.</p><p>While you hold the drawn weapon, it creates a 10-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a> originating from you. You and all creatures Friendly to you in the Emanation have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> against spells and other magical effects. If you have 17 or more levels in the Paladin class, the size of the Emanation increases to 30 feet.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement by a paladin)</p><p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. When you hit a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiend</a> or an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> with it, that creature takes an extra 2d10 Radiant damage.</p><p>While you hold the drawn sword, it creates an aura in a 10-foot radius around you. You and all creatures friendly to you in the aura have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> against spells and other magical effects. If you have 17 or more levels in the Paladin class, the radius of the aura increases to 30 feet.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-luck-blade", "title": "Luck Blade", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, Sickle, or Shortsword), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. While the weapon is on your person, you also gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a>.</p><p><strong>Luck.</strong> If the weapon is on your person, you can call on its luck (no action required) to reroll one failed D20 Test if you don’t have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> condition. You must use the second roll. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Wish.</strong> The weapon has 1d3 charges. While holding it, you can expend 1 charge and cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> from it. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn. The weapon loses this property if it has no charges.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. While the sword is on your person, you also gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a>.</p><p><strong>Luck.</strong> If the sword is on your person, you can call on its luck (no action required) to reroll one <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, ability check, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> you dislike. You must use the second roll. This property can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Wish.</strong> The sword has 1d4 − 1 charges. While holding it, you can use an action to expend 1 charge and cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> from it. This property can’t be used again until the next dawn. The sword loses this property if it has no charges.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sword-of-answering", "title": "Sword of Answering", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Longsword), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement by a creature with the same alignment as the sword)</p><p>Nine of these blades exist. Each has its own name and alignment, and each bears a different gem in its pommel.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Alignment</th><th>Gem</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Answerer</td><td>Chaotic good</td><td>Emerald</td></tr><tr><td>Back Talker</td><td>Chaotic evil</td><td>Jet</td></tr><tr><td>Concluder</td><td>Lawful neutral</td><td>Amethyst</td></tr><tr><td>Last Quip</td><td>Chaotic neutral</td><td>Tourmaline</td></tr><tr><td>Rebutter</td><td>Neutral good</td><td>Topaz</td></tr><tr><td>Replier</td><td>Neutral</td><td>Peridot</td></tr><tr><td>Retorter</td><td>Lawful good</td><td>Aquamarine</td></tr><tr><td>Scather</td><td>Lawful evil</td><td>Garnet</td></tr><tr><td>Squelcher</td><td>Neutral evil</td><td>Spinel</td></tr></tbody></table><p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this sword. In addition, while you hold the sword, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to make one melee attack with it against any creature within your reach that deals damage to you. You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, and any damage dealt with this special attack ignores any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-immunity\">Immunity</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> the target has.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-vorpal-sword", "title": "Vorpal Sword", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, or Scimitar), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. In addition, the weapon ignores <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Slashing damage.</p><p>When you use this weapon to attack a creature that has at least one head and roll a 20 on the d20 for the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, you cut off one of the creature’s heads. The creature dies if it can’t survive without the lost head. A creature is immune to this effect if it has <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-immunity\">Immunity</a> to Slashing damage, if it doesn’t have or need a head, or if the DM decides that the creature is too big for its head to be cut off with this weapon. Such a creature instead takes an extra 30 Slashing damage from the hit. If the creature has Legendary <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a>, it can expend one daily use of that trait to avoid losing its head, taking the extra damage instead.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (any sword that deals slashing damage), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. In addition, the weapon ignores <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Slashing damage.</p><p>When you attack a creature that has at least one head with this weapon and roll a 20 on the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, you cut off one of the creature’s heads. The creature dies if it can’t survive without the lost head. A creature is immune to this effect if it is immune to Slashing damage, doesn’t have or need a head, has legendary actions, or the DM decides that the creature is too big for its head to be cut off with this weapon. Such a creature instead takes an extra 6d8 Slashing damage from the hit.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-weapons-artifact", "title": "Artifact", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-axe-of-the-dwarvish-lords", "title": "Axe of the Dwarvish Lords", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Battleaxe), Artifact</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p><strong>Magic Weapon.</strong> The Axe of the Dwarvish Lords is a magic weapon that grants a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. When you attack a creature with the axe and roll a 20 on the d20 for the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, the axe deals an extra 20 Slashing damage. The axe has the Thrown property with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. When you hit with a ranged attack using this weapon, it deals an extra 1d8 Force damage, or an extra 2d8 Force damage if the target is a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a>. Immediately after hitting or missing, the weapon flies back to your hand.</p><p><strong>Blessings of Moradin.</strong> While attuned to the axe, you gain the following benefits:</p><p><strong>Darkvision.</strong> You gain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkvision\">Darkvision</a> with a range of 60 feet. If you already have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkvision\">Darkvision</a>, its range increases by 60 feet.</p><p><strong>Fortitude of Stone.</strong> Your Constitution increases by 2, to a maximum of 20.</p><p><strong>Gifts of the Creator.</strong> You have proficiency with Brewer’s Supplies, Mason’s Tools, and Smith’s Tools.</p><p><strong>One with the Forge.</strong> You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-immunity\">Immunity</a> to Poison damage and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Fire damage.</p><p><strong>Sunder.</strong> When you hit an object with the axe, the object takes the maximum amount of damage possible.</p><p><strong>Conjure Earth Elemental.</strong> While holding the axe, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to summon an Earth <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-elemental\">Elemental</a>. It appears in an unoccupied space you choose within 30 feet of yourself, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> count. The elemental disappears after 24 hours, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>. You can’t use this property again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The axe has the following random properties: 2 minor beneficial properties, 1 major beneficial property, and 2 minor detrimental properties.</p><p><strong>Travel the Depths.</strong> You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to touch the axe to a fixed piece of dwarven stonework and cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-teleport\">Teleport</a> from the axe. If your intended destination is underground, there is no chance of a mishap or arriving somewhere unexpected. You can’t use this property again until 3 days have passed.</p><p><strong>Destroying the Axe.</strong> The only way to destroy the axe is to melt it down in the Earthheart Forge, where it was created. It must remain in the burning forge for 50 years before it finally succumbs to the fire and is consumed.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (battleaxe), Artifact</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p><strong>Magic Weapon.</strong> The Axe of the Dwarvish Lords is a magic weapon that grants a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. The axe also functions as a Belt of Dwarvenkind, a Dwarven Thrower, and a Sword of Sharpness.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The axe has the following randomly determined properties: 2 minor beneficial properties, 1 major beneficial property, and 2 minor detrimental properties.</p><p><strong>Blessings of Moradin.</strong> If you are a dwarf attuned to the axe, you gain the following benefits: you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-immunity\">Immunity</a> to Poison damage; the range of your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkvision\">Darkvision</a> increases by 60 feet; and you gain proficiency with artisan’s tools related to blacksmithing, brewing, and stonemasonry.</p><p><strong>Conjure Earth Elemental.</strong> If you are holding the axe, you can use your action to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-conjure-elemental\">Conjure Elemental</a> from it, summoning an Earth <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-elemental\">Elemental</a>. You can’t use this property again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Travel the Depths.</strong> You can use an action to touch the axe to a fixed piece of dwarven stonework and cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-teleport\">Teleport</a> from the axe. If your intended destination is underground, there is no chance of a mishap or arriving somewhere unexpected. You can’t use this property again until 3 days have passed.</p><p><strong>Curse.</strong> The axe bears a curse that affects any nondwarf that becomes attuned to it. Even if the attunement ends, the curse remains. With each passing day, the creature’s physical appearance and stature become more dwarflike. After seven days, the creature looks like a typical dwarf, but the creature neither loses its racial traits nor gains the racial traits of a dwarf. The physical changes wrought by the axe aren’t considered magical in nature (and therefore can’t be dispelled), but they can be undone by any effect that removes a curse, such as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-greater-restoration\">Greater Restoration</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-remove-curse\">Remove Curse</a> spell.</p><p><strong>Destroying the Axe.</strong> The only way to destroy the axe is to melt it down in the Earthheart Forge, where it was created. It must remain in the burning forge for fifty years before it finally succumbs to the fire and is consumed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sword-of-kas", "title": "Sword of Kas", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Longsword), Artifact</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>The Sword of Kas is a magic, sentient longsword that grants a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. It scores a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-critical-hit\">Critical Hit</a> on a roll of 19 or 20, and deals an extra 2d10 Slashing damage to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a>.</p><p>If the sword isn’t bathed in blood within 1 minute of being drawn from its scabbard, its wielder must make a DC 15 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. On a successful save, the wielder takes 3d6 Psychic damage. On a failed save, the wielder is dominated by the sword, as if by the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dominate-monster\">Dominate Monster</a> spell, and the sword demands that it be bathed in blood. The spell effect ends when the sword’s demand is met.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The Sword of Kas has the following random properties: 1 minor beneficial property, 1 major beneficial property, 1 minor detrimental property, and 1 major detrimental property.</p><p><strong>Spirit of Kas.</strong> While the sword is on your person, you add a d10 to your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> roll at the start of every combat. In addition, when you use an action to attack with the sword, you can transfer some or all of its attack bonus to your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a> instead. The adjusted bonuses remain in effect until the start of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> While the sword is on your person, you can use an action to cast one of the following spells (save DC 18) from it: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-call-lightning\">Call Lightning</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-divine-word\">Divine Word</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-finger-of-death\">Finger of Death</a>. Once you use the sword to cast a spell, you can’t cast that spell again from it until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Sentience.</strong> The Sword of Kas is a sentient chaotic evil weapon with an Intelligence of 15, a Wisdom of 13, and a Charisma of 16. It has hearing and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkvision\">Darkvision</a> out to a range of 120 feet. The weapon communicates telepathically with its wielder and can speak, read, and understand Common.</p><p><strong>Personality.</strong> The sword’s purpose is to bring ruin to Vecna. Killing Vecna’s worshipers, destroying the lich’s works, and foiling his machinations all help to fulfill this goal. The sword also seeks to destroy anyone corrupted by the Eye and Hand of Vecna. The sword’s obsession with those artifacts eventually becomes a fixation for its wielder.</p><p><strong>Destroying the Sword.</strong> A creature attuned to both the Eye of Vecna and the Hand of Vecna can use the Wish property of those combined artifacts to unmake the Sword of Kas. The creature must cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> and make a Charisma check contested by the Charisma check of the sword. The sword must be within 30 feet of the creature, or the spell fails. If the sword wins the contest, nothing happens, and the Wish spell is wasted. If the sword loses the contest, it is destroyed.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items", "title": "Wondrous Items", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-bead-of-nourishment", "title": "Bead of Nourishment", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This flavorless, gelatinous bead dissolves on your tongue and gives you as much nourishment as one day of Rations.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bead-of-refreshment", "title": "Bead of Refreshment", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This flavorless, gelatinous bead dissolves in a liquid, turning up to a pint of it into fresh, cold drinking water. It has no effect on magical liquids or on harmful substances such as poison.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-boots-of-false-tracks", "title": "Boots of False Tracks", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear these boots, you can make them leave tracks matching those of any kind of Humanoid of your size.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>Only humanoids can wear these boots. While wearing them, you can choose to have them leave tracks like those of another kind of humanoid of your size.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-candle-of-the-deep", "title": "Candle of the Deep", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This candle's flame isn't extinguished when the candle is immersed in water. It gives off light and heat like an ordinary candle.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-charlatan-s-die", "title": "Charlatan's Die", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Whenever you roll this six-sided die, you can choose which number it shows.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-billowing", "title": "Cloak of Billowing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>While wearing this cloak, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to make it billow dramatically for 1 minute.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-many-fashions", "title": "Cloak of Many Fashions", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>While wearing this cloak, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to change the garment's style, color, and apparent quality. Its weight doesn't change. Whatever it looks like, it can only ever be a cloak; it can copy the look of other magic cloaks but doesn't gain their magical properties.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-clockwork-amulet", "title": "Clockwork Amulet", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This copper amulet holds tiny interlocking gears and is powered by magic from Mechanus, the plane of clockwork predictability; faint ticking and whirring comes from inside it. When you make an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> while wearing it, you can skip rolling the d20 and treat the die as showing a 10. Once you use this property, you can't use it again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-clothes-of-mending", "title": "Clothes of Mending", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This elegant outfit mends itself to counteract daily wear and tear. Pieces of the outfit that are destroyed can't be repaired this way.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-dark-shard-amulet", "title": "Dark Shard Amulet", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement by a Warlock)</p><p>This amulet is made from a shard of resilient material that comes from an otherworldly realm. While you wear it, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use the amulet as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spellcasting-focus\">Spellcasting Focus</a> for your Warlock spells.</p><p><strong>Unknown Spell.</strong> As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can try to cast a cantrip you don't know. The cantrip must be on the Warlock spell list and have a casting time of an action, and you make a DC 10 Intelligence (Arcana) check. On a success, you cast the spell. On a failure, the spell fails and the action used to cast it is wasted. Either way, you can't use this property again until you finish a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-long-rest\">Long Rest</a>.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-dread-helm", "title": "Dread Helm", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>While you wear this fearsome steel helm, your eyes glow red and the rest of your face is hidden in shadow.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ear-horn-of-hearing", "title": "Ear Horn of Hearing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>While you hold this horn up to your ear, it suppresses the effects of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafened</a> condition on you.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-enduring-spellbook", "title": "Enduring Spellbook", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This spellbook, and anything written in it, can't be damaged by fire or water. It also doesn't deteriorate with age.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ersatz-eye", "title": "Ersatz Eye", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This magical eye replaces one that was lost or removed. While it sits in your eye socket, you can see through the tiny orb as though it were your natural eye. You can insert or remove it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, and it can't be removed against your will while you are alive.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This artificial eye replaces a real one that was lost or removed. While the ersatz eye is embedded in your eye socket, it can't be removed by anyone other than you, and you can see through the tiny orb as though it were a normal eye.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-hat-of-vermin", "title": "Hat of Vermin", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This hat has 3 charges. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and expend 1 charge to summon your choice of a Bat, a Frog, or a Rat. The creature appears in the hat and tries to get away from you as fast as it can. It is Indifferent toward you and everyone else, isn't under your control, behaves like an ordinary creature of its kind, and disappears after 1 hour or when it drops to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>. The hat regains all expended charges daily at dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-hat-of-wizardry", "title": "Hat of Wizardry", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement by a Wizard)</p><p>This cone-shaped hat is decorated with moons and stars. While you wear it, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use the hat as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spellcasting-focus\">Spellcasting Focus</a> for your Wizard spells.</p><p><strong>Unknown Spell.</strong> As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can try to cast a cantrip you don't know. The cantrip must be on the Wizard spell list and have a casting time of an action, and you make a DC 10 Intelligence (Arcana) check. On a success, you cast the spell. On a failure, the spell fails and the action used to cast it is wasted. Either way, you can't use this property again until you finish a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-long-rest\">Long Rest</a>.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-heward-s-handy-spice-pouch", "title": "Heward's Handy Spice Pouch", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This belt pouch looks empty and has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and expend 1 charge to name any nonmagical food seasoning (salt, pepper, saffron, cilantro, and so on) and pull a pinch of it from the pouch; a pinch is enough to season one meal. The pouch regains 1d6 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-horn-of-silent-alarm", "title": "Horn of Silent Alarm", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This horn has 4 charges and regains 1d4 expended charges daily at dawn. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can blow the horn and expend 1 charge. One creature of your choice within 600 feet of the horn hears its blare; no one else does.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-instrument-of-illusions", "title": "Instrument of Illusions", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>While you play this musical instrument, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to create harmless, illusory visual effects in a 5-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a> originating from the instrument. If you are a Bard, the Emanation is 15 feet instead. Sample effects include luminous musical notes, a spectral dancer, butterflies, and gently falling snow. The effects have no substance or sound and are obviously illusory. They end when you stop playing.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item (Instrument), Common</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you are playing this musical instrument, you can create harmless, illusory visual effects within a 5-foot-radius sphere centered on the instrument. If you are a bard, the radius increases to 15 feet. Sample visual effects include luminous musical notes, a spectral dancer, butterflies, and gently falling snow. The magical effects have neither substance nor sound, and they are obviously illusory. The effects end when you stop playing.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-instrument-of-scribing", "title": "Instrument of Scribing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This musical instrument has 3 charges and regains all expended charges daily at dawn. While you play it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and expend 1 charge to write a magical message on a nonmagical object or surface you can see within 30 feet of you. The message can be up to six words long and is written in a language you know. If you are a Bard, you can scribe an additional seven words and make the message glow faintly, so it can be read even in nonmagical <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkness\">Darkness</a>. Casting <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dispel-magic\">Dispel Magic</a> on the message erases it; otherwise it fades after 24 hours.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item (Instrument), Common</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This musical instrument has 3 charges. While you are playing it, you can use an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to expend 1 charge from the instrument and write a magical message on a nonmagical object or surface that you can see within 30 feet of you. The message can be up to six words long and is written in a language you know. If you are a bard, you can scribe an additional seven words and choose to make the message glow faintly, so that it can be read in nonmagical darkness. Casting <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dispel-magic\">Dispel Magic</a> on the message erases it. Otherwise, the message fades away after 24 hours. The instrument regains all expended charges daily at dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-lock-of-trickery", "title": "Lock of Trickery", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This lock looks like an ordinary lock (the kind described in the Player's Handbook) and comes with a single key. Its tumblers magically shift to thwart burglars, so Dexterity checks made to pick it have Disadvantage.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-mystery-key", "title": "Mystery Key", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>A question mark is worked into the head of this key. The key has a 5 percent chance of unlocking any lock it is inserted into. Once it unlocks something, the key disappears.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-orb-of-direction", "title": "Orb of Direction", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>You can use this orb as an Arcane Focus. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to learn which way is magnetic north. Nothing happens if you use it somewhere that has no magnetic north.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-orb-of-time", "title": "Orb of Time", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>You can use this orb as an Arcane Focus. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to learn whether it is morning, afternoon, evening, or nighttime. This works only on the Material Plane.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-perfume-of-bewitching-wondrous", "title": "Perfume of Bewitching", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This tiny vial holds enough magic perfume for one use. You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to apply it to yourself, and its effect lasts 1 hour. For that duration, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on all Charisma (Deception and Persuasion) checks made to influence a creature within 5 feet of you.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-pipe-of-smoke-monsters", "title": "Pipe of Smoke Monsters", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>While smoking this pipe, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to exhale a puff of smoke shaped like a creature, such as a dragon, a flumph, or a slaad. The shape must fit within a 1-foot cube and loses its form after a few seconds, becoming an ordinary puff of smoke.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-pole-of-angling", "title": "Pole of Angling", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This item works as a Pole. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to turn it into a fishing pole with a hook, line, and reel, or to turn the fishing pole back into a Pole.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-pole-of-collapsing", "title": "Pole of Collapsing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This item works as a Pole. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to collapse it into a 1-foot-long rod for easy storage (its weight doesn't change), or to return the rod to a Pole. The rod lengthens only as far as the surrounding space allows.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-pot-of-awakening", "title": "Pot of Awakening", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>If you plant an ordinary shrub in this 10-pound clay pot and let it grow for 30 days, the shrub magically becomes an Awakened Shrub at the end of that time. When it awakens, its roots break the pot and destroy it. The awakened shrub is Friendly toward you and obeys your commands; without commands from you, it does nothing.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-prosthetic-limb", "title": "Prosthetic Limb", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This magic item replaces a lost limb, such as a hand, arm, foot, leg, or similar body part. While attached, it works exactly like the part it replaces. You can detach or reattach it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, and it can't be removed against your will while you are alive.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-rival-coin", "title": "Rival Coin", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This gold coin has a creature embossed on each face. The two must be famous rivals or enemies of each other (for example, Iggwilv on one side and Mordenkainen on the other, or Venger and Tiamat). One figure is on the heads side, the other on the tails side.</p><p>The coin has 1 charge and regains it daily at dawn. You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss the coin and expend its charge. Roll any die: an even number means heads, an odd number means tails, and the result also decides the effect.</p><p><strong>Heads.</strong> Target one creature you can see within 60 feet. The target makes a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 2d4 Psychic damage and has Disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the end of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and suffers no other effect.</p><p><strong>Tails.</strong> You take 1d4 Psychic damage.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-rope-of-mending", "title": "Rope of Mending", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This 50-foot coil of rope repairs itself when cut into any number of smaller pieces. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can make all pieces that are touching each other and not otherwise in use knit back together. If a section of the rope is lost or destroyed, it is permanently shorter.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ruby-of-the-war-mage", "title": "Ruby of the War Mage", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement by a Spellcaster)</p><p>Etched with eldritch runes, this 1-inch-diameter ruby lets you use a Simple or Martial weapon as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spellcasting-focus\">Spellcasting Focus</a> for your spells. For this to work, you must attach the ruby to the weapon by pressing it against the weapon for at least 10 minutes. After that, the ruby can't be removed unless you detach it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, the weapon is destroyed, or your attunement to the ruby ends.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-talking-doll", "title": "Talking Doll", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While this doll is within 5 feet of you, you can spend a Short Rest telling it up to six phrases, none longer than six words, and setting a condition under which it speaks each one. You can also replace old phrases with new ones. Whatever the condition is, it must occur within 5 feet of the doll to make it speak. For example, whenever someone picks the doll up, it might say, \"I want a piece of candy.\" The doll's phrases are lost when your attunement to it ends.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-tankard-of-sobriety", "title": "Tankard of Sobriety", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This tankard has a stern face sculpted into one side. You can drink ale, wine, or any other nonmagical alcoholic drink poured into it without becoming inebriated. The tankard has no effect on magical liquids or on harmful substances such as poison.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-veteran-s-cane", "title": "Veteran's Cane", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>, you can turn this walking cane into an ordinary Longsword, or turn the Longsword back into a walking cane. You must be holding the item to do either.</p>\n"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-alchemy-jug", "title": "Alchemy Jug", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This ceramic jug appears to hold a gallon of liquid and weighs 12 pounds whether full or empty. It sloshes when shaken, even if empty.</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and name one liquid from the table below to make the jug produce it. Afterward, you can uncork the jug as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> and pour that liquid out, up to 2 gallons per minute. The maximum amount of liquid the jug can produce depends on the liquid you named.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Liquid</th><th>Maximum Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Acid</td><td>8 ounces</td></tr><tr><td>Basic Poison</td><td>4 ounces</td></tr><tr><td>Beer</td><td>4 gallons</td></tr><tr><td>Honey</td><td>1 gallon</td></tr><tr><td>Mayonnaise</td><td>2 gallons</td></tr><tr><td>Oil</td><td>1 quart</td></tr><tr><td>Vinegar</td><td>2 gallons</td></tr><tr><td>Water, fresh</td><td>8 gallons</td></tr><tr><td>Water, salt</td><td>12 gallons</td></tr><tr><td>Wine</td><td>1 gallon</td></tr></tbody></table><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This ceramic jug appears to hold a gallon of liquid and weighs 12 pounds whether full or empty. Sloshing sounds can be heard inside when it is shaken, even if empty.</p><p>You can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and name one liquid from the table below to make the jug produce it. Afterward, you can uncork the jug as an action and pour that liquid out, up to 2 gallons per minute. The maximum amount of liquid the jug can produce depends on the liquid you named. Once the jug starts producing a liquid, it can't produce a different one, or more of one that has reached its maximum, until the next dawn.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Liquid</th><th>Maximum Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Acid</td><td>8 ounces</td></tr><tr><td>Basic poison</td><td>1/2 ounce</td></tr><tr><td>Beer</td><td>4 gallons</td></tr><tr><td>Honey</td><td>1 gallon</td></tr><tr><td>Mayonnaise</td><td>2 gallons</td></tr><tr><td>Oil</td><td>1 quart</td></tr><tr><td>Vinegar</td><td>2 gallons</td></tr><tr><td>Water, fresh</td><td>8 gallons</td></tr><tr><td>Water, salt</td><td>12 gallons</td></tr><tr><td>Wine</td><td>1 gallon</td></tr></tbody></table>"}, {"id": "magic-item-amulet-of-proof-against-detection-and-location", "title": "Amulet of Proof against Detection and Location", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear this amulet, you can't be targeted by Divination spells or perceived through magical scrying sensors unless you allow it.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-baba-yaga-s-dancing-broom", "title": "Baba Yaga's Dancing Broom", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>The archfey Baba Yaga crafted many of these magic brooms, and no two look exactly alike.</p><p>While holding the broom, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to transform it into an Animated Broom under your control. The broom moves into an unoccupied space as close to you as possible, acts immediately after you on your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> count, and remains animate until you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> and use a command word to render it inanimate.</p><p>On your turn, you can mentally command the animated broom (no action required) if it is within 30 feet of you and you don't have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> condition. You decide what action the broom takes and where it moves during its next turn, or you can issue a general command, such as to attack your enemies or guard a location.</p><p>If the broom is reduced to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>, it shatters and is destroyed. If it reverts to its inanimate form before losing all its Hit Points, it regains all of them.</p><p><strong>Animated Broom.</strong> Small <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a>, Unaligned. <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">AC</a> 15. HP 14 (4d6). <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> 5 feet, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-fly-speed\">Fly Speed</a> 50 feet (hover). Initiative +5. Str 10 (+0), Dex 17 (+3), Con 10 (+0), Int 1 (−5), Wis 5 (−3), Cha 1 (−5). Immunities: Poison and Psychic damage; <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-charmed\">Charmed</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafened</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-paralyzed\">Paralyzed</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-petrified\">Petrified</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> conditions. Senses: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-blindsight\">Blindsight</a> 60 feet, Passive Perception 7. Languages: none. CR 1/4 (XP 50).</p><p><strong>Flyby.</strong> The broom doesn't provoke an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-opportunity-attacks\">Opportunity Attack</a> when it flies out of an enemy's reach.</p><p><strong>Slam.</strong> Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 feet. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-bag-of-holding", "title": "Bag of Holding", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This bag's interior is far larger than its outside, roughly 2 feet square and 4 feet deep inside. It can hold up to 500 pounds, not exceeding 64 cubic feet, and it weighs 5 pounds regardless of its contents. Retrieving an item from it requires a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>.</p><p>If the bag is overloaded, pierced, or torn, it is destroyed and its contents scatter across the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-astral\">Astral Plane</a>. If it's turned inside out, its contents spill out unharmed, but the bag must be put right before it can be used again. It holds enough air for 10 minutes of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside.</p><p>Placing a Bag of Holding inside an extradimensional space created by a Heward's Handy Haversack, a Portable Hole, or a similar item instantly destroys both items and opens a one-way gate to the Astral Plane at that spot. Each creature within a 10-foot-radius <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-sphere\">Sphere</a> centered on the gate is sucked through to a random location on the Astral Plane, and the gate then closes for good.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bag-of-tricks", "title": "Bag of Tricks", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This bag, made of gray, rust, or tan cloth, seems empty, but reaching inside reveals a small, fuzzy object. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can pull the object out and throw it up to 20 feet. When it lands, it becomes a creature determined by rolling on the table matching the bag's color (stat blocks are in the Monster Manual). The creature vanishes at the next dawn or when it drops to 0 Hit Points.</p><p>The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies and acts immediately after you on your Initiative count. You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to command how it moves and acts on its next turn; without orders, it acts as befits its nature. Once three fuzzy objects have been pulled from the bag, it can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d8</th><th>Gray Bag</th><th>Rust Bag</th><th>Tan Bag</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Weasel</td><td>Rat</td><td>Jackal</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Giant Rat</td><td>Owl</td><td>Ape</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Badger</td><td>Mastiff</td><td>Baboon</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Boar</td><td>Goat</td><td>Axe Beak</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Panther</td><td>Giant Goat</td><td>Black Bear</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Giant Badger</td><td>Giant Boar</td><td>Giant Weasel</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Dire Wolf</td><td>Lion</td><td>Giant Hyena</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Giant Elk</td><td>Brown Bear</td><td>Tiger</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-boots-of-elvenkind", "title": "Boots of Elvenkind", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While you wear these boots, your steps make no sound regardless of the surface, and you have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-boots-of-striding-and-springing", "title": "Boots of Striding and Springing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear these boots, your Speed becomes 30 feet unless it's higher, and it isn't reduced by carrying weight over your carrying capacity or by wearing Heavy armor. Once on each of your turns, you can jump up to 30 feet by spending only 10 feet of movement.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-boots-of-the-winterlands", "title": "Boots of the Winterlands", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>These furred boots are snug and warm. While wearing them, you have Resistance to Cold damage and can tolerate temperatures of 0 degrees Fahrenheit or lower without extra protection. You also ignore <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficult-terrain\">Difficult Terrain</a> created by ice or snow.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bracers-of-archery", "title": "Bracers of Archery", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing these bracers, you have proficiency with the Longbow and Shortbow, and you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls made with those weapons.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-brooch-of-shielding", "title": "Brooch of Shielding", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this brooch, you have Resistance to Force damage and Immunity to damage from the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-missile\">Magic Missile</a> spell.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-broom-of-flying", "title": "Broom of Flying", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This wooden broom works like an ordinary one until you stand astride it and take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to make it hover beneath you, at which point you can ride it through the air. It has a Fly Speed of 50 feet and can carry up to 400 pounds, but its Fly Speed drops to 30 feet while carrying more than 200 pounds. It stops hovering when you land or when you're no longer riding it.</p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can send the broom to travel alone to a destination within 1 mile if you name the location and are familiar with it. It returns to you when you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and use a command word, provided it's still within 1 mile of you.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This wooden broom weighs 3 pounds and functions like an ordinary broom until you stand astride it and speak its command word. It then hovers beneath you and can be ridden through the air. It has a flying speed of 50 feet and can carry up to 400 pounds, but its flying speed becomes 30 feet while it carries more than 200 pounds. The broom stops hovering when you land.</p><p>You can send the broom to travel alone to a destination within 1 mile of you if you speak the command word, name the location, and are familiar with that place. The broom returns to you when you speak another command word, provided it is still within 1 mile of you.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-cap-of-water-breathing", "title": "Cap of Water Breathing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While you wear this cap underwater, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to create a bubble of air around your head that lets you breathe normally underwater. The bubble stays with you until the cap is removed or you are no longer underwater.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While you wear this cap underwater, you can speak its command word as an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to create a bubble of air around your head that lets you breathe normally underwater. The bubble stays with you until you speak the command word again, the cap is removed, or you are no longer underwater.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-circlet-of-blasting", "title": "Circlet of Blasting", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing this circlet, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scorching-ray\">Scorching Ray</a> with it (+5 to hit). The circlet can't cast the spell again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-elvenkind", "title": "Cloak of Elvenkind", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear this cloak, Wisdom (Perception) checks made to perceive you have Disadvantage, and you have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-protection", "title": "Cloak of Protection", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class and saving throws while you wear this cloak.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-the-manta-ray", "title": "Cloak of the Manta Ray", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this cloak, you can breathe underwater and have a Swim Speed of 60 feet.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing this cloak with its hood up, you can breathe underwater, and you have a swimming speed of 60 feet. Pulling the hood up or down requires an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-decanter-of-endless-water", "title": "Decanter of Endless Water", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This 2-pound stoppered flask sloshes when shaken as if it holds water. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can remove the stopper and speak one of three command words, and fresh or salt water (your choice) pours out until the start of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Splash.</strong> 1 gallon of water.</p><p><strong>Fountain.</strong> 5 gallons of water.</p><p><strong>Geyser.</strong> 30 gallons of water gush out in a 30-foot-long, 1-foot-wide <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-line\">Line</a>. If you're holding the decanter, you can aim the geyser (no action required). One creature of your choice in the Line must succeed on a DC 13 Strength <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 1d4 Bludgeoning damage and have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a> condition. Instead of a creature, you can target one unattended object in the Line that weighs no more than 200 pounds; the geyser knocks it over.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-deck-of-illusions", "title": "Deck of Illusions", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This box holds a full deck of 34 cards: 32 depicting specific creatures and 2 with mirrored surfaces. A deck found as treasure is usually missing 1d20 − 1 cards. The magic works only if cards are drawn at random.</p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can draw a random card and throw it to the ground within 30 feet of you. An illusion of the creature it depicts (see the table) forms over the card and remains until dispelled. It looks and behaves like a real creature of its kind but can do no harm. While you're within 120 feet of it and can see it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to move it anywhere within 30 feet of its card.</p><p>Any physical interaction reveals the illusion, since objects pass through it. A creature that takes a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-study\">Study action</a> to inspect it recognizes it as an illusion with a successful DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) check. The illusion lasts until its card is moved or the illusion is dispelled (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dispel-magic\">Dispel Magic</a> or similar). When it ends, the card's image disappears and the card can't be used again.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Illusion</th><th>1d100</th><th>Illusion</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–03</td><td>Adult Red Dragon</td><td>52–54</td><td>Hobgoblin Warrior</td></tr><tr><td>04–06</td><td>Archmage</td><td>55–57</td><td>Incubus</td></tr><tr><td>07–09</td><td>Assassin</td><td>58–60</td><td>Iron Golem</td></tr><tr><td>10–12</td><td>Bandit Captain</td><td>61–63</td><td>Knight</td></tr><tr><td>13–15</td><td>Beholder</td><td>64–66</td><td>Kobold Warrior</td></tr><tr><td>16–18</td><td>Berserker</td><td>67–69</td><td>Lich</td></tr><tr><td>19–21</td><td>Bugbear Warrior</td><td>70–72</td><td>Medusa</td></tr><tr><td>22–24</td><td>Cloud Giant</td><td>73–75</td><td>Night Hag</td></tr><tr><td>25–27</td><td>Druid</td><td>76–78</td><td>Ogre</td></tr><tr><td>28–30</td><td>Erinyes</td><td>79–81</td><td>Oni</td></tr><tr><td>31–33</td><td>Ettin</td><td>82–84</td><td>Priest</td></tr><tr><td>34–36</td><td>Fire Giant</td><td>85–87</td><td>Succubus</td></tr><tr><td>37–39</td><td>Frost Giant</td><td>88–90</td><td>Troll</td></tr><tr><td>40–42</td><td>Gnoll Warrior</td><td>91–93</td><td>Warrior Veteran</td></tr><tr><td>43–45</td><td>Goblin Warrior</td><td>94–96</td><td>Wyvern</td></tr><tr><td>46–48</td><td>Guardian Naga</td><td>97–00</td><td>The card drawer</td></tr><tr><td>49–51</td><td>Hill Giant</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-driftglobe", "title": "Driftglobe", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This small sphere of thick glass weighs 1 pound. If you are within 60 feet of it, you can command it to emanate light equivalent to that of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-light\">Light</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-daylight\">Daylight</a> spell (your choice). Once used, the Daylight effect can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><p>You can issue another command as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to make the illuminated globe rise into the air and float no more than 5 feet off the ground. It hovers there until you or another creature grasps it. If you move more than 60 feet from the hovering globe, it follows you by the shortest route until it is within 60 feet of you. If it is prevented from moving, it sinks gently to the ground and becomes inactive, and its light winks out.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This small sphere of thick glass weighs 1 pound. If you are within 60 feet of it, you can speak its command word to make it emanate the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-light\">Light</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-daylight\">Daylight</a> spell. Once used, the daylight effect can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><p>You can speak another command word as an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to make the illuminated globe rise into the air and float no more than 5 feet off the ground. It hovers there until you or another creature grasps it. If you move more than 60 feet from the hovering globe, it follows you by the shortest route until it is within 60 feet of you. If it is prevented from moving, it sinks gently to the ground and becomes inactive, and its light winks out.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dust-of-disappearance", "title": "Dust of Disappearance", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This fine, sand-like powder comes in a quantity sufficient for one use. When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to throw the dust into the air, you and each creature and object within a 10-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a> originating from you have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-invisible\">Invisible</a> condition for 2d4 minutes. The duration is the same for all subjects, and the dust is consumed. Immediately after an affected creature makes an attack roll, deals damage, or casts a spell, the condition ends for that creature.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-dust-of-dryness", "title": "Dust of Dryness", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This small packet holds 1d6 + 4 pinches of dust. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can sprinkle a pinch over water to turn up to a 15-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-cube\">Cube</a> of it into a marble-sized pellet that floats or rests nearby and weighs almost nothing. A creature can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to smash the pellet on a hard surface, shattering it and releasing the water; this destroys the pellet and ends its magic.</p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can also sprinkle a pinch on an Elemental within 5 feet of you that's composed mostly of water, such as a Water Elemental. The creature makes a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 10d6 Necrotic damage on a failure or half as much on a success.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-dust-of-sneezing-and-choking", "title": "Dust of Sneezing and Choking", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Found in a small container, this powder resembles Dust of Disappearance, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-identify\">Identify</a> reveals it as such. There is enough for one use. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can throw the dust into the air, forcing you and every creature in a 30-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a> originating from you to make a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. Constructs, Elementals, Oozes, Plants, and Undead succeed automatically.</p><p>On a failed save, a creature sneezes uncontrollably, has the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> condition, and is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-suffocation\">suffocating</a>. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. The effect also ends on a creature targeted by <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lesser-restoration\">Lesser Restoration</a>.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-elemental-gem", "title": "Elemental Gem", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This gem holds a mote of elemental energy. When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to break it, an elemental is summoned and the gem stops being magical. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the broken gem as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and acts immediately after you on your Initiative count. It disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Gem</th><th>Summoned Elemental</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blue sapphire</td><td>Air Elemental</td></tr><tr><td>Emerald</td><td>Water Elemental</td></tr><tr><td>Red corundum</td><td>Fire Elemental</td></tr><tr><td>Yellow diamond</td><td>Earth Elemental</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-eversmoking-bottle", "title": "Eversmoking Bottle", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can open or close this bottle. Opening it releases thick smoke that fills a 60-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a> originating from the bottle, and the area within is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-heavily-obscured\">Heavily Obscured</a>. Each minute the bottle stays open, the Emanation grows by 10 feet, up to a maximum of 120 feet. Closing the bottle fixes the cloud in place until it disperses after 10 minutes. A strong wind, such as one from <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gust-of-wind\">Gust of Wind</a>, disperses it after 1 minute.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-eyes-of-charming", "title": "Eyes of Charming", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>These crystal lenses fit over the eyes and have 3 charges. While wearing them, you can expend 1 or more charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-charm-person\">Charm Person</a> (save DC 13): 1 charge casts it at level 1, and each additional charge raises the spell's level by 1. The lenses regain all expended charges daily at dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-eyes-of-minute-seeing", "title": "Eyes of Minute Seeing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>These crystal lenses fit over the eyes. While wearing them, your vision improves out to 1 foot, giving you <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkvision\">Darkvision</a> within that range and Advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) checks made to examine something within it.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-eyes-of-the-eagle", "title": "Eyes of the Eagle", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>These crystal lenses fit over the eyes. While wearing them, you have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight. In clear conditions, you can make out details of even very distant creatures and objects as small as 2 feet across.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>These crystal lenses fit over the eyes. While wearing them, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">advantage</a> on Wisdom (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-perception\">Perception</a>) checks that rely on sight. In conditions of clear visibility, you can make out details of even extremely distant creatures and objects as small as 2 feet across.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-silver-raven", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Silver Raven)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, it becomes the living creature described below; if the space is occupied by creatures or objects, or is too small, it doesn't. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine, then reverts to figurine form. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it to make it revert. When it becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until the time given in its description has passed.</p><p>This silver statuette of a raven can become a Raven for up to 12 hours. Once used, it can't be used again until 2 days have passed. While it is in raven form, the figurine lets you cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animal-messenger\">Animal Messenger</a> on it.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-gauntlets-of-ogre-power", "title": "Gauntlets of Ogre Power", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Your Strength is 19 while you wear these gauntlets. They have no effect on you if your Strength is already 19 or higher.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-gem-of-brightness", "title": "Gem of Brightness", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This prism has 50 charges. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and use one of three command words to cause one of the following effects.</p><p><strong>First Command Word.</strong> The gem sheds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bright-light\">Bright Light</a> in a 30-foot radius and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> for another 30 feet. This costs no charge. It lasts until you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to repeat the command word or use another function of the gem.</p><p><strong>Second Command Word.</strong> You expend 1 charge and the gem fires a brilliant beam of light at one creature you can see within 60 feet of you. The creature must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a> condition for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns and ending the effect on itself on a success.</p><p><strong>Third Command Word.</strong> You expend 5 charges and the gem flares with intense light in a 30-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-cone\">Cone</a>. Each creature in the Cone makes the same saving throw as for the second command word's beam.</p><p>When all the gem's charges are spent, it becomes a nonmagical jewel worth 50 GP.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-gloves-of-missile-snaring", "title": "Gloves of Missile Snaring", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>If you're hit by an attack roll made with a Ranged or Thrown weapon while wearing these gloves, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to reduce the damage by 1d10 plus your Dexterity modifier, provided you have a free hand. If you reduce the damage to 0, you can catch the ammunition or weapon if it is small enough to hold in that hand.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-gloves-of-swimming-and-climbing", "title": "Gloves of Swimming and Climbing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing these gloves, you have a Climb Speed and a Swim Speed equal to your Speed, and you gain a +5 bonus to Strength (Athletics) checks made to climb or swim.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-gloves-of-thievery", "title": "Gloves of Thievery", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>These gloves are imperceptible while worn. While wearing them, you gain a +5 bonus to Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-goggles-of-night", "title": "Goggles of Night", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing these dark lenses, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkvision\">Darkvision</a> out to 60 feet. If you already have Darkvision, wearing the goggles increases its range by 60 feet.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-hag-eye", "title": "Hag Eye", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>A Hag Eye has 3 charges. While wearing or holding it, you can expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-darkvision\">Darkvision</a> (targeting yourself only) or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-see-invisibility\">See Invisibility</a>. The Hag Eye regains all expended charges daily at dawn.</p><p><strong>Coven Sensor.</strong> The Hag Eye is usually entrusted to a hag's minion for safekeeping and transport. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, a hag who belongs to the coven that created the Hag Eye can see what it sees, provided the hag and the Hag Eye are on the same plane of existence. This effect lasts as long as the hag maintains <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>. Multiple hags in the coven can see through the Hag Eye at the same time.</p><p><strong>Creating a Hag Eye.</strong> Only a hag coven can craft this item, which is made from a real eye coated in varnish and often fitted to a pendant or another wearable item. A coven can have only one Hag Eye at a time, and creating a new one requires all three members of the coven to perform a special rite. The rite takes 1 hour, and the hags can't perform it if one or more of them has the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> condition.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-hat-of-disguise", "title": "Hat of Disguise", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this hat, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-disguise-self\">Disguise Self</a> with it. The spell ends if the hat is removed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-headband-of-intellect", "title": "Headband of Intellect", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Your Intelligence is 19 while you wear this headband. It has no effect on you if your Intelligence is 19 or higher without it.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-helm-of-comprehending-languages", "title": "Helm of Comprehending Languages", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing this helm, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-comprehend-languages\">Comprehend Languages</a> from it.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-helm-of-telepathy", "title": "Helm of Telepathy", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this helm, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-telepathy\">Telepathy</a> with a range of 30 feet, and you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-thoughts\">Detect Thoughts</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-suggestion\">Suggestion</a> (save DC 13) from it. Once either spell has been cast from the helm, that spell can't be cast from it again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-instrument-of-the-bards-doss-lute", "title": "Instrument of the Bards (Doss Lute)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard)</p><p>This instrument is superior to an ordinary instrument of its kind in every way, and is named after one of seven legendary bard colleges. A creature that tries to play it without being attuned to it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d4 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>.</p><p>You can play the instrument to cast one of its spells, using your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Once the instrument has been used to cast a spell, it can't be used to cast that spell again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> The instrument holds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fly\">Fly</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-invisibility\">Invisibility</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-levitate\">Levitate</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-protection-from-evil-and-good\">Protection from Evil and Good</a>, plus the following: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animal-friendship\">Animal Friendship</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-protection-from-energy\">Protection from Energy</a> (Fire damage only), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-protection-from-poison\">Protection from Poison</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-instrument-of-the-bards-fochlucan-bandore", "title": "Instrument of the Bards (Fochlucan Bandore)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard)</p><p>This instrument is superior to an ordinary instrument of its kind in every way, and is named after one of seven legendary bard colleges. A creature that tries to play it without being attuned to it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d4 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>.</p><p>You can play the instrument to cast one of its spells, using your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Once the instrument has been used to cast a spell, it can't be used to cast that spell again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> The instrument holds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fly\">Fly</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-invisibility\">Invisibility</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-levitate\">Levitate</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-protection-from-evil-and-good\">Protection from Evil and Good</a>, plus the following: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-entangle\">Entangle</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-faerie-fire\">Faerie Fire</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-shillelagh\">Shillelagh</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-speak-with-animals\">Speak with Animals</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-instrument-of-the-bards-mac-fuirmidh-cittern", "title": "Instrument of the Bards (Mac-Fuirmidh Cittern)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard)</p><p>This instrument is superior to an ordinary instrument of its kind in every way, and is named after one of seven legendary bard colleges. A creature that tries to play it without being attuned to it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d4 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>.</p><p>You can play the instrument to cast one of its spells, using your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Once the instrument has been used to cast a spell, it can't be used to cast that spell again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> The instrument holds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fly\">Fly</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-invisibility\">Invisibility</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-levitate\">Levitate</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-protection-from-evil-and-good\">Protection from Evil and Good</a>, plus the following: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-barkskin\">Barkskin</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-cure-wounds\">Cure Wounds</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fog-cloud\">Fog Cloud</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-keoghtom-s-ointment", "title": "Keoghtom's Ointment", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This glass jar, 3 inches in diameter, contains 1d4 + 1 doses of a thick mixture that smells faintly of aloe. The jar and its contents weigh 1/2 pound.</p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can swallow one dose of the ointment or apply it to a creature within 5 feet of you. The creature that receives it regains 2d8 + 2 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> and ceases to have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This glass jar, 3 inches in diameter, contains 1d4 + 1 doses of a thick mixture that smells faintly of aloe. The jar and its contents weigh 1/2 pound.</p><p>As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, you can swallow one dose of the ointment or apply it to the skin. The creature that receives it regains 2d8 + 2 hit points, ceases to be poisoned, and is cured of any disease.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-lantern-of-revealing", "title": "Lantern of Revealing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While lit, this hooded lantern burns for 6 hours on 1 pint of oil, shedding <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bright-light\">Bright Light</a> in a 30-foot radius and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> for another 30 feet. <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-invisible\">Invisible</a> creatures and objects are visible while in the lantern's Bright Light. You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to lower the hood, reducing the light to Dim Light in a 5-foot radius.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-medallion-of-thoughts", "title": "Medallion of Thoughts", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>The medallion has 5 charges. While wearing it, you can expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-thoughts\">Detect Thoughts</a> (save DC 13) from it. The medallion regains 1d4 expended charges daily at dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-nature-s-mantle", "title": "Nature's Mantle", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a Druid or Ranger)</p><p>This cloak shifts color and texture to blend with the terrain around you. While wearing it, you can use it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spellcasting-focus\">Spellcasting Focus</a> for your Druid and Ranger spells.</p><p>While you are in an area that is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-lightly-obscured\">Lightly Obscured</a>, you can take the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hide\">Hide</a> action as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> even if you are being directly observed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-necklace-of-adaptation", "title": "Necklace of Adaptation", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this necklace, you can breathe normally in any environment, and you have Advantage on saving throws made to avoid or end the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-pearl-of-power", "title": "Pearl of Power", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a Spellcaster)</p><p>While this pearl is on your person, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to regain one expended spell slot of level 3 or lower. Once you use the pearl, it can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-periapt-of-health", "title": "Periapt of Health", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this pendant, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to regain 2d4 + 2 Hit Points. Once used, this property can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><p>In addition, you have Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition while you wear this pendant.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>You are immune to contracting any disease while you wear this pendant. If you are already infected with a disease, its effects are suppressed for as long as you wear the pendant.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-periapt-of-wound-closure", "title": "Periapt of Wound Closure", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this pendant, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Life Preservation.</strong> Whenever you make a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-death-saving-throw\">Death Saving Throw</a>, you can change a roll of 9 or lower to a 10, turning a failed save into a successful one.</p><p><strong>Natural Healing Boost.</strong> Whenever you roll a Hit Point Die to regain Hit Points, double the number of Hit Points it restores.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear this pendant, you stabilize whenever you are dying at the start of your turn. In addition, whenever you roll a Hit Die to regain hit points, double the number of hit points it restores.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-pipes-of-haunting", "title": "Pipes of Haunting", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>These pipes have 3 charges and regain 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to play them and expend 1 charge to create an eerie, spellbinding tune. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> condition for 1 minute. A creature that fails the save repeats it at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. A creature that succeeds is immune to these pipes' effect for 24 hours.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-pipes-of-the-sewers", "title": "Pipes of the Sewers", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While these pipes are on your person, ordinary rats and Giant Rats are Indifferent toward you and won't attack you unless you threaten or harm them.</p><p>The pipes have 3 charges and regain 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. If you play them as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can then take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to expend 1 to 3 charges, calling forth one Swarm of Rats per expended charge, provided enough rats are within half a mile of you (as the DM determines). If there aren't enough rats to form a swarm, the charge is wasted. Called swarms move toward the music by the shortest available route but aren't otherwise under your control.</p><p>Whenever a Swarm of Rats not under another creature's control comes within 30 feet of you while you play the pipes, the swarm makes a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw. On a success, it behaves normally and can't be swayed by the pipes for the next 24 hours. On a failure, it is swayed by the music and becomes <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies for as long as you keep playing the pipes each round as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>. A Friendly swarm obeys your commands; if you give none, it defends itself but takes no other actions. If a Friendly swarm starts its turn more than 30 feet from you, your control over it ends, and it behaves normally and can't be swayed by the pipes for the next 24 hours.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-quaal-s-feather-token-anchor", "title": "Quaal's Feather Token (Anchor)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Feather Tokens look like feathers. Each type has a different single-use effect, and the type determines its rarity. The DM chooses the type or rolls 1d100: 01–20 Anchor, 21–35 Bird, 36–50 Fan, 51–65 Swan Boat, 66–90 Tree, 91–00 Whip.</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to touch the token to a boat or ship. For the next 24 hours, the vessel can't be moved by any means. Touching the token to the vessel again ends the effect. When the effect ends, the token disappears.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-quaal-s-feather-token-fan", "title": "Quaal's Feather Token (Fan)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Feather Tokens look like feathers. Each type has a different single-use effect, and the type determines its rarity. The DM chooses the type or rolls 1d100: 01–20 Anchor, 21–35 Bird, 36–50 Fan, 51–65 Swan Boat, 66–90 Tree, 91–00 Whip.</p><p>If you are on a boat or ship, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss the token up to 10 feet into the air. The token disappears and a giant flapping fan takes its place, floating and creating a strong wind. The wind can fill the sails of one ship, increasing its speed by 5 miles per hour for 8 hours. You can dismiss the fan as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-quaal-s-feather-token-tree", "title": "Quaal's Feather Token (Tree)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Feather Tokens look like feathers. Each type has a different single-use effect, and the type determines its rarity. The DM chooses the type or rolls 1d100: 01–20 Anchor, 21–35 Bird, 36–50 Fan, 51–65 Swan Boat, 66–90 Tree, 91–00 Whip.</p><p>You must be outdoors to use this token. You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to touch it to an unoccupied space on the ground. The token disappears and a nonmagical oak tree springs up in its place. The tree is 60 feet tall with a 5-foot-diameter trunk, and its branches spread in a 20-foot radius at the top.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-quiver-of-ehlonna", "title": "Quiver of Ehlonna", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Each of this quiver's three compartments connects to an extradimensional space, letting it hold many items while never weighing more than 2 pounds. The shortest compartment holds up to 60 Arrows, Bolts, or similar objects. The midsize compartment holds up to 18 Javelins or similar objects. The longest compartment holds up to 6 long objects, such as bows, Quarterstaffs, or Spears.</p><p>You can draw any item the quiver holds as if from an ordinary quiver or scabbard.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-robe-of-useful-items", "title": "Robe of Useful Items", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This robe is covered in cloth patches of various shapes and colors. While wearing it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to detach one patch, causing it to become the object or creature it represents. Once the last patch is removed, the robe becomes an ordinary garment.</p><p>The robe has two of each of these patches: Bullseye Lantern (filled and lit), Dagger, Mirror, Pole, Rope (coiled), and Sack.</p><p>In addition, it has 4d4 other patches. The DM chooses them or rolls on the table.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Patch</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–08</td><td>Bag of 100 GP</td></tr><tr><td>09–15</td><td>Silver coffer (1 foot long, 6 inches wide and deep) worth 500 GP</td></tr><tr><td>16–22</td><td>Iron door (up to 10 feet wide and 10 feet high, barred on one side of your choice), which you can place in an opening you can reach; it conforms to fit the opening, attaching and hinging itself</td></tr><tr><td>23–30</td><td>10 gems worth 100 GP each</td></tr><tr><td>31–44</td><td>Wooden ladder (24 feet long)</td></tr><tr><td>45–51</td><td>Riding Horse with a Riding Saddle</td></tr><tr><td>52–59</td><td>Open pit (a 10-foot Cube), which you can place on the ground within 10 feet of yourself</td></tr><tr><td>60–68</td><td>4 Potions of Healing</td></tr><tr><td>69–75</td><td>Rowboat (12 feet long)</td></tr><tr><td>76–83</td><td>Spell Scroll containing one spell of level 1, 2, or 3 (your choice)</td></tr><tr><td>84–90</td><td>2 Mastiffs</td></tr><tr><td>91–96</td><td>Window (2 feet by 4 feet, up to 2 feet deep), which you can place on a vertical surface you can reach</td></tr><tr><td>97–00</td><td>Portable Ram</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-rope-of-climbing", "title": "Rope of Climbing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This 60-foot length of rope can hold up to 3,000 pounds. While holding one end, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to command the other end to animate and move toward a destination you choose, up to the rope's length away from you. That end moves 10 feet on your turn when you first command it and 10 feet at the start of each of your later turns until it reaches its destination or you tell it to stop. You can also tell the rope to fasten itself securely to an object or unfasten itself, to knot or unknot itself, or to coil itself for carrying.</p><p>If you tell the rope to knot, large knots appear at 1-foot intervals along it. While knotted, the rope shortens to 50 feet and grants Advantage on ability checks made to climb with it. The rope has AC 20, 20 Hit Points, and Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage. It regains 1 Hit Point every 5 minutes as long as it has at least 1 Hit Point, and it is destroyed if it drops to 0 Hit Points.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-saddle-of-the-cavalier", "title": "Saddle of the Cavalier", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This saddle confers the following benefits while you are seated in it and astride a mount.</p><p><strong>Protected Mount.</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">Attack rolls</a> against the mount have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a>.</p><p><strong>Secure Rider.</strong> You can't be dismounted against your will. This property is suppressed while you have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> condition.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While you are in this saddle on a mount, you can't be dismounted against your will if you're conscious, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> against the mount have disadvantage.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sending-stones", "title": "Sending Stones", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Sending Stones come in pairs, each carved to match the other so the pairing is easy to recognize. While you touch one stone, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-sending\">Sending</a> from it. The target is the bearer of the other stone. If no creature bears the other stone, you know that as soon as you use the stone, and you don't cast the spell.</p><p>Once Sending has been cast using either stone, the stones can't be used again until the next dawn. If one stone of a pair is destroyed, the other becomes nonmagical.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-slippers-of-spider-climbing", "title": "Slippers of Spider Climbing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear these light shoes, you can move up, down, and across vertical surfaces and along ceilings while leaving your hands free. You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. However, the slippers don't let you move this way on a slippery surface, such as one covered in ice or oil.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-stone-of-good-luck-luckstone", "title": "Stone of Good Luck (Luckstone)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While this polished agate is on your person, you gain a +1 bonus to ability checks and saving throws.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-wind-fan", "title": "Wind Fan", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While holding this fan, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gust-of-wind\">Gust of Wind</a> (save DC 13) from it. Each subsequent time the fan is used before the next dawn, it has a cumulative 20 percent chance of not working; if it fails, it tears into useless, nonmagical tatters.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-winged-boots", "title": "Winged Boots", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>These boots have 4 charges and regain 1d4 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing them, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and expend 1 charge to gain a Fly Speed of 30 feet for 1 hour. If you are flying when the duration expires, you descend at 30 feet per round until you land.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-wraps-of-unarmed-power-1", "title": "Wraps of Unarmed Power +1", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing these wraps, you have a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-unarmed-strike\">Unarmed Strikes</a>. Those strikes deal your choice of Force damage or their normal damage type.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-amulet-of-health", "title": "Amulet of Health", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Your Constitution score is 19 while you wear this amulet. It has no effect on you if your Constitution is already 19 or higher.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bag-of-beans", "title": "Bag of Beans", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This heavy cloth bag holds 3d4 dry beans when found. It weighs half a pound no matter how many beans are inside and becomes nonmagical once it holds none.</p><p>If you dump one or more beans out of the bag, they explode in a 10-foot-radius <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-sphere\">Sphere</a> centered on them. The dumped beans are destroyed, and each creature in the Sphere, you included, makes a DC 15 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 5d4 Force damage on a failed save or half as much on a success.</p><p>If you remove a bean, plant it in dirt or sand, and water it, the bean disappears and produces an effect from the ground 1 minute later. The DM can pick an effect from the table or roll for it.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01</td><td>5d4 toadstools sprout. When a creature eats one, roll any die. On an odd roll, the eater must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or take 5d6 Poison damage and have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. On an even roll, the eater gains 5d6 Temporary Hit Points for 1 hour.</td></tr><tr><td>02–10</td><td>A geyser erupts and spouts water, beer, mayonnaise, tea, vinegar, wine, or oil (DM's choice) 30 feet into the air for 1d4 minutes.</td></tr><tr><td>11–20</td><td>A Treant sprouts. Roll any die: on an odd roll the treant is Chaotic Evil, on an even roll it is Chaotic Good.</td></tr><tr><td>21–30</td><td>An animate but immobile stone statue in your likeness rises and makes verbal threats against you. If you leave it and others come near, it describes you as the most heinous of villains and directs the newcomers to find and attack you. If you're on the same plane of existence as the statue, it knows where you are. It becomes inanimate after 24 hours.</td></tr><tr><td>31–40</td><td>A campfire with green flames springs forth and burns for 24 hours or until it is extinguished.</td></tr><tr><td>41–50</td><td>Three Shrieker Fungi sprout.</td></tr><tr><td>51–60</td><td>1d4 + 4 bright-pink toads crawl forth. Whenever a toad is touched, it turns into a Large or smaller monster of the DM's choice that acts according to its alignment and nature. The monster remains for 1 minute, then vanishes in a puff of bright-pink smoke.</td></tr><tr><td>61–70</td><td>A hungry Bulette burrows up and attacks.</td></tr><tr><td>71–80</td><td>A fruit tree grows with 1d10 + 20 fruit, 1d8 of which act as randomly determined potions. The tree vanishes after 1 hour. Picked fruit stays and keeps its magic for 30 days.</td></tr><tr><td>81–90</td><td>A nest of 1d4 + 3 rainbow-colored eggs springs up. A creature that eats an egg makes a DC 20 Constitution saving throw. On a success, it permanently raises its lowest ability score by 1 (choosing randomly among ties). On a failure, it takes 10d6 Force damage from an internal explosion.</td></tr><tr><td>91–95</td><td>A pyramid with a 60-foot-square base bursts upward. Inside is a burial chamber holding a Mummy, a Mummy Lord, or another Undead of the DM's choice, and its sarcophagus contains treasure of the DM's choice.</td></tr><tr><td>96–00</td><td>A giant beanstalk sprouts to a height of the DM's choice. Its top leads wherever the DM wants, such as a great view, a cloud giant's castle, or another plane of existence.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bead-of-force", "title": "Bead of Force", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This small black sphere is 3/4 of an inch across; 1d4 + 4 of them are usually found together. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can throw the bead up to 60 feet. It explodes on impact and is destroyed. Each creature within 10 feet of where it landed makes a DC 15 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 5d4 Force damage on a failure. A transparent sphere of force then fills the area for 1 minute. A creature that failed the save and is completely inside is trapped; one that succeeded, or is only partly inside, is pushed out. Only breathable air passes through the sphere's wall; no attack or other effect does. A trapped creature can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to push against the wall and move the sphere up to half its Speed. The sphere can be picked up and weighs only 1 pound regardless of what's inside.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-belt-of-dwarvenkind", "title": "Belt of Dwarvenkind", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Dwarvish.</strong> You know Dwarvish.</p><p><strong>Friend of Dwarvenkind.</strong> You have Advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks made to interact with dwarves and duergar.</p><p><strong>Toughness.</strong> Your Constitution increases by 2, to a maximum of 20.</p><p>In addition, while attuned to the belt, you have a 50 percent chance each day at dawn of growing a full beard if you can grow one, or a thicker beard if you already have one.</p><p>If you aren't a dwarf or duergar, you also gain these benefits while wearing it.</p><p><strong>Darkvision.</strong> You have Darkvision with a range of 60 feet.</p><p><strong>Resilience.</strong> You have Resistance to Poison damage and Advantage on saving throws made to avoid or end the Poisoned condition.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-belt-of-hill-giant-strength", "title": "Belt of Hill Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 21. It has no effect on you if your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-boots-of-levitation", "title": "Boots of Levitation", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear these boots, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-levitate\">Levitate</a> on yourself at will.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-boots-of-speed", "title": "Boots of Speed", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear these boots, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to click the heels together. This doubles your Speed, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-opportunity-attacks\">Opportunity Attacks</a> made against you have Disadvantage. When you click your heels again, the effect ends. Once the boots' property has been used for a total of 10 minutes, it stops working until you finish a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-long-rest\">Long Rest</a>.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bowl-of-commanding-water-elementals", "title": "Bowl of Commanding Water Elementals", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>While this bowl is filled with water and you are within 5 feet of it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to summon a Water Elemental. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the bowl as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> count. It disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>. The bowl can't be used this way again until the next dawn.</p><p>The bowl is about 1 foot across and half as deep, and holds about 3 gallons.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-bracers-of-defense", "title": "Bracers of Defense", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing these bracers, you gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class if you are wearing no armor and using no Shield.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-brazier-of-commanding-fire-elementals", "title": "Brazier of Commanding Fire Elementals", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>While you are within 5 feet of this brazier, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to summon a Fire Elemental. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the brazier as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> count. It disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>. The brazier can't be used this way again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-cape-of-the-mountebank", "title": "Cape of the Mountebank", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This cape smells faintly of brimstone. While wearing it, you can use it to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dimension-door\">Dimension Door</a> as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>. This property can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><p>When you teleport with that spell, you leave behind a cloud of smoke. The space you left is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-lightly-obscured\">Lightly Obscured</a> by that smoke until the end of your next turn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-censer-of-controlling-air-elementals", "title": "Censer of Controlling Air Elementals", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>While gently swinging this censer, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to summon an Air Elemental. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the censer as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> count. It disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>. The censer can't be used this way again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-chime-of-opening", "title": "Chime of Opening", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This hollow metal tube is about 1 foot long and weighs 1 pound. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can strike the chime to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-knock\">Knock</a>. The spell's usual knocking sound is replaced by the chime's clear, ringing tone, which is audible out to 300 feet.</p><p>The chime can be used 10 times. After the tenth use, it cracks and becomes useless.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-displacement", "title": "Cloak of Displacement", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear this cloak, it magically projects an illusion that makes you appear to be standing near your actual location, causing any creature to have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> against you. If you take damage, this property ceases to function until the start of your next turn. It is suppressed while your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> is 0.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-the-bat", "title": "Cloak of the Bat", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this cloak, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Dexterity (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-stealth\">Stealth</a>) checks. In an area of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkness\">Darkness</a>, you can grip the edges of the cloak to gain a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-fly-speed\">Fly Speed</a> of 40 feet. You lose this Fly Speed if you fail to keep gripping the cloak's edges while flying, or if you are no longer in Dim Light or Darkness.</p><p>While wearing the cloak in an area of Dim Light or Darkness, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> on yourself, shape-shifting into a Bat. In that form, you retain your Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. The cloak can't be used this way again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-cube-of-force", "title": "Cube of Force", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This cube is about an inch across, and each face bears a distinct marking. You can press one face, expend the number of charges it costs, and cast the spell tied to it (save DC 17).</p><p>The cube starts with 10 charges and regains 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Spell</th><th>Charge Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-mage-armor\">Mage Armor</a></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-shield\">Shield</a></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-leomund-s-tiny-hut\">Tiny Hut</a></td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-mordenkainen-s-private-sanctum\">Private Sanctum</a></td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-otiluke-s-resilient-sphere\">Resilient Sphere</a></td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-force\">Wall of Force</a></td><td>5</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cube-of-summoning", "title": "Cube of Summoning", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This Tiny cube looks like a jack-in-the-box. When you wind its crank as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, a merry tune plays, the lid pops open, a creature appears in the nearest unoccupied space, and the lid closes. The lid can't otherwise be opened.</p><p>Roll on the table below to determine which spell the cube casts to summon the creature. The spell is cast at level 5 (save DC 17, +9 attack bonus) and doesn't require <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>, but you otherwise function as the spell's caster. Once the cube summons a creature, it can't do so again until the next dawn.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d6</th><th>Spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-summon-aberration\">Summon Aberration</a></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-summon-beast\">Summon Beast</a></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-summon-construct\">Summon Construct</a></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-summon-dragon\">Summon Dragon</a></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-summon-elemental\">Summon Elemental</a></td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-summon-fey\">Summon Fey</a></td></tr></tbody></table>"}, {"id": "magic-item-daern-s-instant-fortress", "title": "Daern's Instant Fortress", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can place this 1-inch adamantine statuette on the ground and, using a command word, make it grow rapidly into a square adamantine tower. Repeating the command word returns it to statuette form, which works only if the tower is empty. Each creature in the area where the tower appears is pushed to an unoccupied space outside but next to the tower, and unattended objects in the area are pushed clear too.</p><p>The tower is 20 feet on a side and 30 feet high, with arrow slits on all sides and a battlement on top. Its interior has two floors joined by a ladder, staircase, or ramp (your choice) that ends at a trapdoor to the roof. When created, the tower has a single door at ground level on the side facing you. The door opens only at your command, which you can give as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>, and it is immune to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-knock\">Knock</a> and similar magic.</p><p>Magic prevents the tower from being tipped over. The roof, door, and walls each have AC 20, 100 Hit Points, Immunity to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage except that dealt by siege equipment, and Resistance to all other damage.</p><p>Shrinking the tower doesn't repair damage to it. Only a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> spell can repair it (this counts as replicating a spell of level 8 or lower), and each casting restores the tower to full Hit Points.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>You can use an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to place this 1-inch metal cube on the ground and speak its command word. The cube rapidly grows into a fortress that remains until you use an action to speak the command word that dismisses it, which works only if the fortress is empty.</p><p>The fortress is a square tower 20 feet on a side and 30 feet high, with arrow slits on all sides and a battlement on top. Its interior is divided into two floors, with a ladder running along one wall to connect them and ending at a trapdoor to the roof. When activated, the tower has a small door on the side facing you. The door opens only at your command, which you can speak as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">bonus action</a>, and it is immune to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-knock\">Knock</a> spell and similar magic, such as that of a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"magic-item-chime-of-opening\">Chime of Opening</a>.</p><p>Each creature in the area where the fortress appears makes a DC 15 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 10d10 Bludgeoning damage on a failed save or half as much on a successful one. In either case, the creature is pushed to an unoccupied space outside but next to the fortress. Objects in the area that aren't being worn or carried take this damage and are pushed automatically.</p><p>The tower is made of adamantine, and its magic prevents it from being tipped over. The roof, the door, and the walls each have 100 hit points and immunity to damage from nonmagical weapons, excluding siege weapons. If reduced to 0 hit points, a section is destroyed and has no effect on the integrity of the rest. Only a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> spell can repair the fortress (this use of the spell counts as replicating a spell of 8th level or lower), and each casting restores the roof, the door, or one wall to full hit points.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dimensional-shackles", "title": "Dimensional Shackles", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to place these shackles on an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> creature. They adjust to fit a creature of Small to Large size. Besides working as ordinary manacles, they stop the bound creature from using any extradimensional movement, including teleportation and travel to another plane. They don't stop it from passing through an interdimensional portal. You and any creature you designate when you use the shackles can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to remove them. Once every 30 days, the bound creature can make a DC 30 Strength (Athletics) check; on a success, it breaks free and destroys the shackles.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-bronze-griffon", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Bronze Griffon)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, it becomes the living creature described below; if the space is occupied by creatures or objects, or is too small, it doesn't. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine, then reverts to figurine form. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it to make it revert. When it becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until the time given in its description has passed.</p><p>This bronze statuette of a griffon rampant can become a Griffon for up to 6 hours. Once used, it can't be used again until 5 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-ebony-fly", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Ebony Fly)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, it becomes the living creature described below; if the space is occupied by creatures or objects, or is too small, it doesn't. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine, then reverts to figurine form. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it to make it revert. When it becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until the time given in its description has passed.</p><p>This ebony statuette, carved in the likeness of a horsefly, can become a Giant Fly for up to 12 hours and can be ridden as a mount. Once used, it can't be used again until 2 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-golden-lions", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Golden Lions)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, it becomes the living creature described below; if the space is occupied by creatures or objects, or is too small, it doesn't. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine, then reverts to figurine form. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it to make it revert. When it becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until the time given in its description has passed.</p><p>These gold statuettes of lions are always made in pairs. You can use one figurine or both at once. Each can become a Lion for up to 1 hour. Once a lion has been used, it can't be used again until 7 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-ivory-goat-of-terror", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Ivory Goat of Terror)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, it becomes the living creature described below; if the space is occupied by creatures or objects, or is too small, it doesn't. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine, then reverts to figurine form. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it to make it revert. When it becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until the time given in its description has passed.</p><p>Ivory goats are always made in sets of three, each looking unique and working differently.</p><p>The Goat of Terror can become a Giant Goat for up to 3 hours. It can't attack, but you can harmlessly remove its horns and use them as weapons: one becomes a +1 Lance and the other a +2 Longsword. Removing a horn takes a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, and the weapons vanish and the horns return when the goat reverts. While you ride the goat, any Hostile creature that starts its turn within a 30-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a> originating from the goat must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> condition for 1 minute, until you stop riding the goat, or until it reverts. A Frightened creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success, and a creature that succeeds is immune to this effect for 24 hours. Once the figurine has been used, it can't be used again until 15 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-ivory-goat-of-travail", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Ivory Goat of Travail)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, it becomes the living creature described below; if the space is occupied by creatures or objects, or is too small, it doesn't. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine, then reverts to figurine form. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it to make it revert. When it becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until the time given in its description has passed.</p><p>Ivory goats are always made in sets of three, each looking unique and working differently.</p><p>The Goat of Travail can become a Giant Goat for up to 3 hours. Once used, it can't be used again until 30 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-ivory-goat-of-traveling", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Ivory Goat of Traveling)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, it becomes the living creature described below; if the space is occupied by creatures or objects, or is too small, it doesn't. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine, then reverts to figurine form. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it to make it revert. When it becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until the time given in its description has passed.</p><p>Ivory goats are always made in sets of three, each looking unique and working differently.</p><p>The Goat of Traveling can become a Large goat with the statistics of a Riding Horse. It has 24 charges, and each hour or portion of an hour it spends in goat form costs 1 charge. While it has charges, you can use it as often as you like. When it runs out, it reverts to a figurine and can't be used again until 7 days have passed, when it regains all expended charges.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-marble-elephant", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Marble Elephant)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, it becomes the living creature described below; if the space is occupied by creatures or objects, or is too small, it doesn't. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine, then reverts to figurine form. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it to make it revert. When it becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until the time given in its description has passed.</p><p>This marble statuette of a trumpeting elephant can become an Elephant for up to 24 hours. Once used, it can't be used again until 7 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-onyx-dog", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Onyx Dog)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, it becomes the living creature described below; if the space is occupied by creatures or objects, or is too small, it doesn't. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine, then reverts to figurine form. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it to make it revert. When it becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until the time given in its description has passed.</p><p>This onyx statuette of a dog can become a Mastiff for up to 6 hours. The mastiff has an Intelligence of 8, can speak Common, and has <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-blindsight\">Blindsight</a> with a range of 60 feet. Once used, it can't be used again until 7 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-serpentine-owl", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Serpentine Owl)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, it becomes the living creature described below; if the space is occupied by creatures or objects, or is too small, it doesn't. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine, then reverts to figurine form. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it to make it revert. When it becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until the time given in its description has passed.</p><p>This serpentine statuette of an owl can become a Giant Owl for up to 8 hours. The owl can communicate telepathically with you at any range as long as you and it are on the same plane of existence. Once used, it can't be used again until 2 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-folding-boat", "title": "Folding Boat", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This object appears as a wooden box 12 inches long, 6 inches wide, and 6 inches deep. It weighs 4 pounds, floats, and can be opened to store items inside. It has three command words, each requiring a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to use:</p><p><strong>First Command Word.</strong> The box unfolds into a Rowboat.</p><p><strong>Second Command Word.</strong> The box unfolds into a Keelboat.</p><p><strong>Third Command Word.</strong> The Folding Boat folds back into a box, provided no creatures are aboard. Any objects in the vessel that can fit inside the box do so; any that can't remain outside it.</p><p>When the box becomes a vessel, its weight becomes that of a normal vessel its size, and anything that was stored in the box remains in the boat. If either vessel is reduced to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>, the Folding Boat is destroyed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-gem-of-seeing", "title": "Gem of Seeing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This gem has 3 charges. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can expend 1 charge. For the next 10 minutes, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-truesight\">Truesight</a> out to 120 feet when you peer through the gem.</p><p>The gem regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-helm-of-teleportation", "title": "Helm of Teleportation", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This helm has 3 charges. While wearing it, you can expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-teleport\">Teleport</a> from it. The helm regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-heward-s-handy-haversack", "title": "Heward's Handy Haversack", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This backpack has a central pouch and two side pouches, each an extradimensional space. Each side pouch holds up to 200 pounds of material, not exceeding 25 cubic feet. The central pouch holds up to 500 pounds, not exceeding 64 cubic feet. The haversack always weighs 5 pounds regardless of its contents.</p><p>Retrieving an item requires a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> or a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> (your choice). When you reach in for a specific item, it is always magically on top.</p><p>If any pouch is overloaded, pierced, or torn, the haversack ruptures and is destroyed, and its contents are lost forever, though an Artifact always turns up again somewhere. If it is turned inside out, its contents spill out unharmed, and it must be put right before it can be used again. Each pouch holds enough air for 10 minutes of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside.</p><p>Placing the haversack inside an extradimensional space created by a Bag of Holding, a Portable Hole, or a similar item instantly destroys both items and opens a gate to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-astral\">Astral Plane</a>. The gate originates where one item was placed in the other. Any creature within 10 feet of the gate that isn't behind <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-total-cover\">Total Cover</a> is sucked through and deposited in a random location on the Astral Plane. The gate then closes, and it is one-way and can't be reopened.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-horn-of-blasting", "title": "Horn of Blasting", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to blow this horn, which emits a thunderous blast in a 30-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-cone\">Cone</a> that is audible out to 600 feet. Each creature in the Cone makes a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. On a failed save, a creature takes 5d8 Thunder damage and has the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafened</a> condition for 1 minute. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage only. Glass or crystal objects in the Cone that aren't worn or carried take 10d8 Thunder damage.</p><p>Each use of the horn's magic has a 20 percent chance of making it explode. The explosion deals 10d6 Force damage to the user and destroys the horn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-horn-of-valhalla", "title": "Horn of Valhalla", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to blow this horn. In response, warrior spirits from the plane of Ysgard appear in unoccupied spaces within 60 feet of you. Each spirit uses the Berserker stat block and returns to Ysgard after 1 hour or when it drops to 0 Hit Points. The spirits look like living, breathing warriors and have Immunity to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-charmed\">Charmed</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> conditions. Once you use the horn, it can't be used again until 7 days have passed.</p><p>Four types of Horn of Valhalla exist, each made of a different metal. The type determines how many spirits it summons and the requirement for using it. The DM chooses the type or rolls on the table.</p><p>If you blow the horn without meeting its requirement, the summoned spirits attack you. If you meet it, they are <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies and follow your commands.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Horn Type</th><th>Spirits</th><th>Requirement</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–40</td><td>Silver</td><td>2</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>41–75</td><td>Brass</td><td>3</td><td>Proficiency with all Simple weapons</td></tr><tr><td>76–90</td><td>Bronze</td><td>4</td><td>Training with all Medium armor</td></tr><tr><td>91–00</td><td>Iron</td><td>5</td><td>Proficiency with all Martial weapons</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-horseshoes-of-speed", "title": "Horseshoes of Speed", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>These horseshoes come in a set of four. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can touch one to the hoof of a horse or similar creature, and it affixes itself there. Removing a horseshoe also takes a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>.</p><p>While all four horseshoes are attached to the same creature, its Speed increases by 30 feet.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-instrument-of-the-bards-canaith-mandolin", "title": "Instrument of the Bards (Canaith Mandolin)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard)</p><p>This instrument is superior to an ordinary instrument of its kind in every way, and is named after one of seven legendary bard colleges. A creature that tries to play it without being attuned to it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d4 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>.</p><p>You can play the instrument to cast one of its spells, using your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Once the instrument has been used to cast a spell, it can't be used to cast that spell again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> The instrument holds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fly\">Fly</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-invisibility\">Invisibility</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-levitate\">Levitate</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-protection-from-evil-and-good\">Protection from Evil and Good</a>, plus the following: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-cure-wounds\">Cure Wounds</a> (level 3 version), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dispel-magic\">Dispel Magic</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-protection-from-energy\">Protection from Energy</a> (Lightning damage only).</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-instrument-of-the-bards-cli-lyre", "title": "Instrument of the Bards (Cli Lyre)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard)</p><p>This instrument is superior to an ordinary instrument of its kind in every way, and is named after one of seven legendary bard colleges. A creature that tries to play it without being attuned to it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d4 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>.</p><p>You can play the instrument to cast one of its spells, using your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Once the instrument has been used to cast a spell, it can't be used to cast that spell again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> The instrument holds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fly\">Fly</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-invisibility\">Invisibility</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-levitate\">Levitate</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-protection-from-evil-and-good\">Protection from Evil and Good</a>, plus the following: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stone-shape\">Stone Shape</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-fire\">Wall of Fire</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wind-wall\">Wind Wall</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-awareness", "title": "Ioun Stone of Awareness", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>While this dark-blue rhomboid orbits your head, you have Advantage on Initiative rolls and Wisdom (Perception) checks.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-protection", "title": "Ioun Stone of Protection", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class while this dusty-rose prism orbits your head.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-reserve", "title": "Ioun Stone of Reserve", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>This vibrant purple prism stores spells cast into it and holds them until you use them. It can store up to 4 levels of spells at a time. When found, it contains 1d4 levels of stored spells chosen by the DM.</p><p>Any creature can cast a spell of level 1 through 4 into the stone by touching it as the spell is cast. The spell has no effect other than being stored; if the stone can't hold it, the spell is expended without effect. The level of the slot used determines how much space the spell takes.</p><p>While the stone orbits your head, you can cast any spell stored in it. The spell uses the slot level, spell save DC, spell attack bonus, and spellcasting ability of the original caster but is otherwise treated as though you cast it. The spell is no longer stored once cast, freeing up space.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-sustenance", "title": "Ioun Stone of Sustenance", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>You don't need to eat or drink while this clear spindle orbits your head.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-iron-bands-of-bilarro", "title": "Iron Bands of Bilarro", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This rusty iron sphere is 3 inches across and weighs 1 pound. You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it at a Huge or smaller creature you can see within 60 feet of you. As the sphere flies, it opens into a tangle of metal bands.</p><p>Make a ranged attack roll with an attack bonus equal to your Dexterity modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus. On a hit, the target has the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a> condition until you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to issue a command that releases it. Doing so, or missing with the attack, makes the bands contract into a sphere again.</p><p>A creature that can touch the bands, including the Restrained one, can take an action to make a DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check to break them. On a success, the item is destroyed and the Restrained creature is freed. On a failure, that creature's further attempts automatically fail until 24 hours have passed.</p><p>Once the bands are used, they can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-mantle-of-spell-resistance", "title": "Mantle of Spell Resistance", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You have Advantage on saving throws against spells while you wear this cloak.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-necklace-of-fireballs", "title": "Necklace of Fireballs", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This necklace has 1d6 + 3 beads hanging from it. You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to detach a bead and throw it up to 60 feet. When it reaches the end of its flight, the bead detonates as a level 3 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (save DC 15).</p><p>You can hurl multiple beads, or even the whole necklace, at once. When you do, increase the Fireball's damage by 1d6 for each bead after the first (maximum 12d6).</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-necklace-of-prayer-beads", "title": "Necklace of Prayer Beads", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Cleric, Druid, or Paladin)</p><p>This necklace has 1d4 + 2 magic beads made of aquamarine, black pearl, or topaz, plus many nonmagical beads of stones such as amber, bloodstone, citrine, coral, jade, pearl, or quartz. If a magic bead is removed from the necklace, it loses its magic.</p><p>Six types of magic bead exist. The DM decides the type of each bead on the necklace or rolls on the table, and a necklace can hold more than one bead of the same type. To use a bead, you must be wearing the necklace. Each bead holds a spell that you can cast from it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> (using your spell save DC if a save is needed). Once a bead's spell has been cast, that bead can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d20</th><th>Bead</th><th>Spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1–6</td><td>Bead of Blessing</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-bless\">Bless</a></td></tr><tr><td>7–12</td><td>Bead of Curing</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-cure-wounds\">Cure Wounds</a> (level 2 version)</td></tr><tr><td>13–16</td><td>Bead of Favor</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-greater-restoration\">Greater Restoration</a></td></tr><tr><td>17–18</td><td>Bead of Smiting</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-shining-smite\">Shining Smite</a></td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>Bead of Summons</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-guardian-of-faith\">Guardian of Faith</a></td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>Bead of Wind Walking</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wind-walk\">Wind Walk</a></td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-periapt-of-proof-against-poison", "title": "Periapt of Proof against Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This delicate silver chain has a brilliant-cut black gem pendant. While you wear it, you have Immunity to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition and to Poison damage.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This delicate silver chain has a brilliant-cut black gem pendant. While you wear it, poisons have no effect on you. You are immune to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">poisoned</a> condition and have immunity to poison damage.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-portable-hole", "title": "Portable Hole", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This fine black cloth, soft as silk, is folded to the size of a handkerchief. It unfolds into a circular sheet 6 feet across.</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to unfold the Portable Hole and place it on or against a solid surface, whereupon it creates an extradimensional hole 10 feet deep. The cylindrical space within exists on a different plane, so it can't be used to create open passages. Any creature inside an open hole can exit by climbing out.</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to close the hole by taking hold of the cloth's edges and folding it up. Folding the cloth closes the hole, and any creatures or objects inside remain in the extradimensional space. No matter what's in it, the hole weighs next to nothing.</p><p>If the hole is folded up, a creature inside its extradimensional space can take an action to make a DC 10 Strength (Athletics) check. On a success, the creature forces its way out and appears within 5 feet of the Portable Hole. A closed Portable Hole holds enough air for 1 hour of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside.</p><p>Placing a Portable Hole inside an extradimensional space created by a Bag of Holding, a Heward's Handy Haversack, or a similar item instantly destroys both items and opens a gate to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-astral\">Astral Plane</a>. The gate originates where one item was placed in the other. Any creature within 10 feet of the gate that isn't behind <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-total-cover\">Total Cover</a> is sucked through and deposited in a random location on the Astral Plane. The gate then closes, and it is one-way and can't be reopened.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-quaal-s-feather-token-bird", "title": "Quaal's Feather Token (Bird)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>Feather Tokens look like feathers. Each type has a different single-use effect, and the type determines its rarity. The DM chooses the type or rolls 1d100: 01–20 Anchor, 21–35 Bird, 36–50 Fan, 51–65 Swan Boat, 66–90 Tree, 91–00 Whip.</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss the token 5 feet into the air. It disappears and an enormous, multicolored bird takes its place. The bird has the statistics of a Roc but can't attack. It obeys your simple commands and can carry up to 500 pounds while flying at its maximum speed (16 miles per hour, up to 144 miles per day, with a 1-hour rest for every 3 hours of flying) or 1,000 pounds at half that speed. It disappears after flying its maximum distance for a day or when it drops to 0 Hit Points. You can dismiss it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-quaal-s-feather-token-swan-boat", "title": "Quaal's Feather Token (Swan Boat)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>Feather Tokens look like feathers. Each type has a different single-use effect, and the type determines its rarity. The DM chooses the type or rolls 1d100: 01–20 Anchor, 21–35 Bird, 36–50 Fan, 51–65 Swan Boat, 66–90 Tree, 91–00 Whip.</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to touch the token to a body of water at least 60 feet across. The token disappears and a swan-shaped boat 50 feet long and 20 feet wide takes its place. The boat is self-propelled and moves across water at 6 miles per hour. While aboard, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to command it to move or turn up to 90 degrees. It remains for 24 hours, then disappears, and you can dismiss it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-quaal-s-feather-token-whip", "title": "Quaal's Feather Token (Whip)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>Feather Tokens look like feathers. Each type has a different single-use effect, and the type determines its rarity. The DM chooses the type or rolls 1d100: 01–20 Anchor, 21–35 Bird, 36–50 Fan, 51–65 Swan Boat, 66–90 Tree, 91–00 Whip.</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw the token to a point within 10 feet of yourself. It disappears and a floating whip takes its place. You can then take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to make a melee spell attack (attack bonus +9) against a creature within 10 feet of the whip; on a hit, the target takes 1d6 + 5 Force damage.</p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>, you can direct the whip to fly up to 20 feet and repeat the attack against a creature within 10 feet of it. The whip disappears after 1 hour, when you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to dismiss it, or when you die or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> condition.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-robe-of-eyes", "title": "Robe of Eyes", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This robe is adorned with eyelike patterns. While you wear it, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>All-Around Vision.</strong> You have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.</p><p><strong>Special Senses.</strong> You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkvision\">Darkvision</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-truesight\">Truesight</a>, both with a range of 120 feet.</p><p><strong>Drawbacks.</strong> A <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-light\">Light</a> spell cast on the robe, or a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-daylight\">Daylight</a> spell cast within 5 feet of it, gives you the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a> condition for 1 minute. At the end of each of your turns, you make a Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 11 for Light, DC 15 for Daylight), ending the condition on yourself on a success.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-rope-of-entanglement", "title": "Rope of Entanglement", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This rope is 30 feet long. While holding one end, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to command the other end to dart forward and entangle one creature you can see within 20 feet of you. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a> condition. You can release the target by letting go of your end (the rope coils up in the target's space) or by taking a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to repeat the command (the rope coils up in your hand).</p><p>A target Restrained by the rope can take an action to make a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check (its choice). On a success, it is no longer Restrained by the rope. If you're still holding the rope when a target escapes, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to command it to coil up in your hand; otherwise it coils up in the target's space.</p><p>The rope has AC 20, 20 Hit Points, and Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage. It regains 1 Hit Point every 5 minutes as long as it has at least 1 Hit Point, and it is destroyed if it drops to 0 Hit Points.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-stone-of-controlling-earth-elementals", "title": "Stone of Controlling Earth Elementals", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>While touching this 5-pound stone to the ground, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to summon an Earth Elemental. It appears in an unoccupied space you choose within 30 feet of you, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>. The stone can't be used this way again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-wings-of-flying", "title": "Wings of Flying", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this cloak, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to turn it into a pair of wings on your back. The wings last for 1 hour or until you end the effect early as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, and they give you a Fly Speed of 60 feet. If you are aloft when the wings disappear, you fall. When they disappear, you can't use them again for 1d12 hours.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-wraps-of-unarmed-power-2", "title": "Wraps of Unarmed Power +2", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>While wearing these wraps, you have a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-unarmed-strike\">Unarmed Strikes</a>. Those strikes deal your choice of Force damage or their normal damage type.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-amulet-of-the-planes", "title": "Amulet of the Planes", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this amulet, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to name a location you are familiar with on another plane of existence, then make a DC 15 Intelligence (Arcana) check. On a success, you cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-plane-shift\">Plane Shift</a>. On a failure, you and each creature and object within 15 feet of you travel to a random destination determined by rolling 1d100 on the table, which gives the creature type that predominates on the plane you land on.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Creature Type</th><th>1d100</th><th>Creature Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–10</td><td>Aberrations</td><td>51–60</td><td>Fey</td></tr><tr><td>11–15</td><td>Beasts</td><td>61–70</td><td>Fiends</td></tr><tr><td>16–20</td><td>Celestials</td><td>71–75</td><td>Giants</td></tr><tr><td>21–25</td><td>Constructs</td><td>76–80</td><td>Monstrosities</td></tr><tr><td>26–35</td><td>Dragons</td><td>81–85</td><td>Oozes</td></tr><tr><td>36–45</td><td>Elementals</td><td>86–90</td><td>Plants</td></tr><tr><td>46–50</td><td>Humanoids</td><td>91–00</td><td>Undead</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bag-of-devouring", "title": "Bag of Devouring", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This bag resembles a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"magic-item-bag-of-holding\">Bag of Holding</a> but is actually the feeding orifice of a gigantic extradimensional creature. Turning the bag inside out closes the orifice. The creature can sense whatever is placed inside the bag. Animal or vegetable matter placed wholly inside is devoured and lost forever.</p><p>When part of a living creature is placed in the bag, as when someone reaches inside it, there is a 50 percent chance the creature is pulled in. A creature inside the bag can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to try to escape with a successful DC 15 Strength (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-athletics\">Athletics</a>) check. Another creature can take an action to reach in and pull a creature out with a successful DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check, provided the puller isn't pulled in first. Any creature that starts its turn inside the bag is devoured, its body destroyed.</p><p>Inanimate objects can be stored in the bag, which holds a cubic foot of such material. However, once each day, the bag swallows any objects inside it and spits them out into another plane of existence, at a time and onto a plane determined by the DM. If the bag is pierced or torn, it is destroyed, and anything inside it is transported to a random location on the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-astral\">Astral Plane</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-belt-of-fire-giant-strength", "title": "Belt of Fire Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 25. It has no effect on you if your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-belt-of-frost-giant-strength", "title": "Belt of Frost Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 23. It has no effect on you if your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-belt-of-stone-giant-strength", "title": "Belt of Stone Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 23. It has no effect on you if your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-candle-of-invocation", "title": "Candle of Invocation", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This candle's magic is activated when you light it, which takes a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>. After burning for 4 hours, it is destroyed. You can snuff it out early to use it later; deduct the time it burned, in increments of 1 minute, from its total burn time.</p><p>While lit, the candle sheds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> in a 30-foot radius. While you are within that light, you have Advantage on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-d20-test\">D20 Tests</a>. In addition, a Cleric or Druid in the light can cast level 1 spells they have prepared without expending spell slots.</p><p>Alternatively, when you light the candle for the first time, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gate\">Gate</a> with it, which destroys the candle. The portal links to a particular Outer Plane chosen by the DM or determined by rolling on the table.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Outer Plane</th><th>1d100</th><th>Outer Plane</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–05</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-abyss\">Abyss</a></td><td>55–59</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-gehenna\">Gehenna</a></td></tr><tr><td>06–10</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-acheron\">Acheron</a></td><td>60–64</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-hades\">Hades</a></td></tr><tr><td>11–17</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-arborea\">Arborea</a></td><td>65–69</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-limbo\">Limbo</a></td></tr><tr><td>18–25</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-arcadia\">Arcadia</a></td><td>70–77</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-mechanus\">Mechanus</a></td></tr><tr><td>26–33</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-beastlands\">Beastlands</a></td><td>78–85</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-mount-celestia\">Mount Celestia</a></td></tr><tr><td>34–41</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-bytopia\">Bytopia</a></td><td>86–90</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-nine-hells\">Nine Hells</a></td></tr><tr><td>42–46</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-carceri\">Carceri</a></td><td>91–95</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-pandemonium\">Pandemonium</a></td></tr><tr><td>47–54</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-elysium\">Elysium</a></td><td>96–00</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-ysgard\">Ysgard</a></td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-carpet-of-flying", "title": "Carpet of Flying", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>You can make this carpet hover and fly by taking a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and using its command word. It moves according to your directions as long as you are within 30 feet of it.</p><p>Four sizes of Carpet of Flying exist. The DM chooses a carpet's size or rolls on the table. A carpet can carry up to twice the weight listed, but its Fly Speed is halved if it carries more than its normal capacity.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Size</th><th>Capacity</th><th>Fly Speed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–20</td><td>3 ft. × 5 ft.</td><td>200 lb.</td><td>80 feet</td></tr><tr><td>21–55</td><td>4 ft. × 6 ft.</td><td>400 lb.</td><td>60 feet</td></tr><tr><td>56–80</td><td>5 ft. × 7 ft.</td><td>600 lb.</td><td>40 feet</td></tr><tr><td>81–00</td><td>6 ft. × 9 ft.</td><td>800 lb.</td><td>30 feet</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cauldron-of-rebirth", "title": "Cauldron of Rebirth", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Druid or Warlock)</p><p>This Tiny pot bears relief scenes of heroes on its cast-iron sides.</p><p>You can use the cauldron as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spellcasting-focus\">Spellcasting Focus</a> for your spells, and it functions as a suitable component for the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scrying\">Scrying</a> spell.</p><p><strong>Brew Potion.</strong> When you finish a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-long-rest\">Long Rest</a>, you can use the cauldron to create a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"magic-item-potion-of-healing-greater\">Potion of Healing</a> (greater), which takes 1 minute. The potion lasts for 24 hours, then loses its magic if not consumed.</p><p><strong>Raise Dead.</strong> As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can cause the cauldron to grow large enough for a Medium creature to crouch within. You can revert the cauldron to its normal size as a Magic action, harmlessly shunting anything that can't fit inside to the nearest unoccupied space.</p><p>If you place the corpse of a Humanoid into the cauldron and cover it with 200 pounds of salt (which costs 10 GP) for at least 8 hours, the salt is consumed and the creature returns to life as if by <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-raise-dead\">Raise Dead</a> at the next dawn. Once used, this property can't be used again for 7 days.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a druid or warlock)</p><p>This Tiny pot bears relief scenes of heroes on its cast-iron sides. You can use the cauldron as a spellcasting focus for your druid spells, and it functions as a suitable component for the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scrying\">Scrying</a> spell.</p><p>When you finish a long rest, you can use the cauldron to create a potion of greater healing. The potion lasts for 24 hours, then loses its magic if not consumed.</p><p>As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, you can cause the cauldron to grow large enough for a Medium creature to crouch within. You can revert it to its normal size as an action, harmlessly shunting anything that can't fit inside to the nearest unoccupied space.</p><p>If you place the corpse of a humanoid into the cauldron and cover it with 200 pounds of salt (which costs 10 gp) for at least 8 hours, the salt is consumed and the creature returns to life as if by <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-raise-dead\">Raise Dead</a> at the next dawn. Once used, this property can't be used again for 7 days.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-arachnida", "title": "Cloak of Arachnida", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This fine garment is made of black silk interwoven with faint, silvery threads. While wearing it, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Poison Resistance.</strong> You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Poison damage.</p><p><strong>Spider Climb.</strong> You have a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-climb-speed\">Climb Speed</a> equal to your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> and can move up, down, and across vertical surfaces and along ceilings while leaving your hands free.</p><p><strong>Spider Walk.</strong> You can't be caught in webs of any sort and can move through webs as if they were <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficult-terrain\">Difficult Terrain</a>.</p><p><strong>Web.</strong> You can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-web\">Web</a> (save DC 13). The web created by the spell fills twice its normal area. Once used, this property can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-crystal-ball", "title": "Crystal Ball", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While touching this crystal orb, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scrying\">Scrying</a> (save DC 17) with it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-efreeti-bottle", "title": "Efreeti Bottle", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to remove the stopper from this painted brass bottle, thick smoke pours out. At the end of your turn, the smoke vanishes with a flash of harmless fire and an Efreeti appears in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of you.</p><p>The first time the bottle is opened, the DM rolls 1d10 to see what happens.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d10</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>The efreeti attacks you. After fighting for 5 rounds, it disappears and the bottle loses its magic.</td></tr><tr><td>2–9</td><td>The efreeti understands your languages and obeys your commands for 1 hour, then returns to the bottle and a new stopper contains it. The stopper can't be removed for 24 hours. The same effect occurs the next two times the bottle is opened. If it is opened a fourth time, the efreeti escapes and disappears, and the bottle loses its magic.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>The efreeti understands your languages and can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> once for you. It disappears when it grants the wish or after 1 hour, and the bottle loses its magic.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-obsidian-steed", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Obsidian Steed)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, it becomes the living creature described below; if the space is occupied by creatures or objects, or is too small, it doesn't. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine, then reverts to figurine form. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it to make it revert. When it becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until the time given in its description has passed.</p><p>This polished obsidian horse can become a Nightmare for up to 24 hours. The nightmare fights only to defend itself. Once used, it can't be used again until 5 days have passed.</p><p>Each time you use the figurine, there is a 10 percent chance it ignores your orders, including a command to revert to figurine form. If you mount the nightmare while it is ignoring your orders, you and the nightmare are instantly transported to a random location on the plane of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-hades\">Hades</a>, where the nightmare reverts to figurine form.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-hat-of-many-spells", "title": "Hat of Many Spells", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Wizard)</p><p>This pointed hat has the following properties.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> While holding the hat, you can use it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spellcasting-focus\">Spellcasting Focus</a> for your Wizard spells. Any spell you cast using the hat gains a special Somatic component: you must reach into the hat and \"pull\" the spell out of it.</p><p><strong>Unknown Spell.</strong> While holding the hat, you can try to cast a level 1+ spell you don't know. The spell must be on the Wizard spell list, be of a level you can cast, and have no Material components costing more than 1,000 GP. Once you decide on the spell, you must expend a spell slot of its level. Then make an Intelligence (Arcana) check (DC 10 plus the spell's level). On a success, you cast the spell with its normal casting time and can't use this property again until you finish a Short or Long Rest. On a failure, you fail to cast the spell and a random effect occurs instead, determined on the table.</p><p>Any spell you cast from the hat uses your spell save DC and spell attack bonus.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–50</td><td>You cast a random spell determined by rolling 1d10: 1, Enlarge/Reduce (enlarge effect); 2, Enlarge/Reduce (reduce effect); 3, Faerie Fire; 4, Fireball; 5, Gust of Wind; 6, Invisibility (cast on yourself); 7, Lightning Bolt; 8, Phantasmal Force; 9, Polymorph; 10, Stinking Cloud.</td></tr><tr><td>51–55</td><td>You have the Stunned condition until the end of your next turn, believing something awesome just happened.</td></tr><tr><td>56–60</td><td>A harmless swarm of butterflies fills a 10-foot Cube within 30 feet of you. The swarm disperses after 1 minute.</td></tr><tr><td>61–65</td><td>You pull a nonmagical object out of the hat. Roll 1d4: 1, a vial of Acid; 2, a flask of Alchemist's Fire; 3, a Crowbar; 4, a lit Torch.</td></tr><tr><td>66–70</td><td>You suffer a bout of \"magic sickness\" and have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour.</td></tr><tr><td>71–75</td><td>You have the Petrified condition until the end of your next turn.</td></tr><tr><td>76–80</td><td>You pull a nonmagical object out of the hat. Roll 1d4: 1, a Dagger; 2, a Rope with a Grappling Hook tied to one end; 3, a bag of Caltrops; 4, a gem worth 50 GP.</td></tr><tr><td>81–85</td><td>A creature appears in an unoccupied space as close to you as possible. It isn't under your control, acts as it normally would, and disappears after 1 hour or when it drops to 0 Hit Points. Roll 1d4: 1, a Camel; 2, a Constrictor Snake; 3, an Elephant; 4, a Mule.</td></tr><tr><td>86–90</td><td>A Hostile Swarm of Bats flies out of the hat, occupies your space, and attacks you.</td></tr><tr><td>91–95</td><td>A vertical, 10-foot-diameter, two-way portal to another plane of existence opens in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of you and stays open until the end of your next turn. The DM determines where it leads.</td></tr><tr><td>96–00</td><td>You pull a magic item out of the hat. Roll 1d6 for its rarity: 1–3, Common; 4–5, Uncommon; 6, Rare. The DM chooses the item, which disappears after 1 hour if it isn't consumed or destroyed before then.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-helm-of-brilliance", "title": "Helm of Brilliance", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This helm is set with 1d10 diamonds, 2d10 rubies, 3d10 fire opals, and 4d10 opals. Any gem pried from the helm crumbles to dust. When all the gems are removed or destroyed, the helm loses its magic.</p><p>You gain the following benefits while wearing it.</p><p><strong>Diamond Light.</strong> As long as the helm has at least one diamond, it emits a 30-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a>. When at least one Undead is within that area, the Emanation is filled with <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a>. Any Undead that starts its turn in the area takes 1d6 Radiant damage.</p><p><strong>Fire Opal Flames.</strong> As long as the helm has at least one fire opal, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to make one weapon you are holding burst into flames. The flames emit <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bright-light\">Bright Light</a> in a 10-foot radius and Dim Light for another 10 feet, and are harmless to you and the weapon. When you hit with an attack using the blazing weapon, the target takes an extra 1d6 Fire damage. The flames last until you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to extinguish them or until you drop or stow the weapon.</p><p><strong>Ruby Resistance.</strong> As long as the helm has at least one ruby, you have Resistance to Fire damage.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> You can cast one of the following spells (save DC 18), using one of the helm's gems of the specified type as a component: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-daylight\">Daylight</a> (opal), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (fire opal), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-prismatic-spray\">Prismatic Spray</a> (diamond), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-fire\">Wall of Fire</a> (ruby). The gem is destroyed when the spell is cast and disappears from the helm.</p><p><strong>Taking Fire Damage.</strong> Roll 1d20 if you are wearing the helm and take Fire damage from failing a saving throw against a spell. On a 1, the helm emits beams of light from its remaining gems and is then destroyed. Each creature within a 60-foot Emanation originating from you must succeed on a DC 17 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be struck by a beam, taking Radiant damage equal to the number of gems in the helm.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-horseshoes-of-a-zephyr", "title": "Horseshoes of a Zephyr", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>These horseshoes come in a set of four. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can touch one to the hoof of a horse or similar creature, and it affixes itself there. Removing a horseshoe also takes a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>.</p><p>While all four are affixed to a creature's hooves, it moves normally while floating 4 inches above a surface. It can cross or stand on nonsolid or unstable surfaces such as water or lava, leaves no tracks, and ignores <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficult-terrain\">Difficult Terrain</a>. It can also travel up to 12 hours a day without gaining <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> levels from extended travel.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-instrument-of-the-bards-anstruth-harp", "title": "Instrument of the Bards (Anstruth Harp)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard)</p><p>This instrument is superior to an ordinary instrument of its kind in every way, and is named after one of seven legendary bard colleges. A creature that tries to play it without being attuned to it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d4 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>.</p><p>You can play the instrument to cast one of its spells, using your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Once the instrument has been used to cast a spell, it can't be used to cast that spell again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> The instrument holds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fly\">Fly</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-invisibility\">Invisibility</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-levitate\">Levitate</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-protection-from-evil-and-good\">Protection from Evil and Good</a>, plus the following: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-cure-wounds\">Cure Wounds</a> (level 5 version), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-ice-storm\">Ice Storm</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-thorns\">Wall of Thorns</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-absorption", "title": "Ioun Stone of Absorption", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>While this pale lavender ellipsoid orbits your head, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to cancel a spell of level 4 or lower cast by a creature you can see. A canceled spell has no effect, and any resources used to cast it are wasted. Once the stone has canceled 20 levels of spells, it burns out, turns dull gray, and loses its magic.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-agility", "title": "Ioun Stone of Agility", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>Your Dexterity increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, while this deep-red sphere orbits your head.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-fortitude", "title": "Ioun Stone of Fortitude", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>Your Constitution increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, while this pink rhomboid orbits your head.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-insight", "title": "Ioun Stone of Insight", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>Your Wisdom increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, while this incandescent blue sphere orbits your head.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-intellect", "title": "Ioun Stone of Intellect", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>Your Intelligence increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, while this marbled scarlet and blue sphere orbits your head.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-leadership", "title": "Ioun Stone of Leadership", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>Your Charisma increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, while this marbled pink and green sphere orbits your head.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-strength", "title": "Ioun Stone of Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>Your Strength increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, while this pale blue rhomboid orbits your head.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-manual-of-bodily-health", "title": "Manual of Bodily Health", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This book contains health and nutrition tips, and its words are charged with magic.</p><p>If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Constitution increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic but regains it in a century.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-manual-of-gainful-exercise", "title": "Manual of Gainful Exercise", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This book describes fitness exercises, and its words are charged with magic.</p><p>If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Strength increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic but regains it in a century.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-manual-of-golems", "title": "Manual of Golems", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This tome contains the information and incantations needed to make a particular type of golem. The DM chooses the type or rolls on the table. To decipher and use the manual, you must be a spellcaster with at least two level 5 spell slots. A creature that can't use a Manual of Golems and tries to read it takes 6d6 Psychic damage.</p><p>To create a golem, you must spend the time shown on the table, working without interruption with the manual at hand and resting no more than 8 hours per day. You must also pay the listed cost for supplies.</p><p>Once you finish creating the golem, the book is consumed in eldritch flames. The golem becomes animate when the manual's ashes are sprinkled on it. See the Monster Manual for the golem's stat block. The golem is under your control and understands and obeys your commands.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d20</th><th>Golem</th><th>Time</th><th>Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1–5</td><td>Clay Golem</td><td>30 days</td><td>65,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>6–17</td><td>Flesh Golem</td><td>60 days</td><td>50,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>18</td><td>Iron Golem</td><td>120 days</td><td>100,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>19–20</td><td>Stone Golem</td><td>90 days</td><td>80,000 GP</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-manual-of-quickness-of-action", "title": "Manual of Quickness of Action", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This book contains coordination and balance exercises, and its words are charged with magic.</p><p>If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Dexterity increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic but regains it in a century.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-mirror-of-life-trapping", "title": "Mirror of Life Trapping", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When this 4-foot-tall, 2-foot-wide mirror is viewed indirectly, its surface shows faint images of creatures. The mirror weighs 50 pounds and has AC 11, 10 Hit Points, Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage, and Vulnerability to Bludgeoning damage. It shatters and is destroyed when reduced to 0 Hit Points.</p><p>If the mirror is hanging on a vertical surface and you are within 5 feet of it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and use a command word to activate it. It stays activated until you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and repeat the command word.</p><p>Any creature other than you that sees its reflection in the activated mirror while within 30 feet of it must succeed on a DC 15 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be trapped, along with anything it wears or carries, in one of the mirror's twelve extradimensional cells. A creature that knows the mirror's nature makes the save with Advantage, and Constructs succeed automatically.</p><p>An extradimensional cell is an infinite expanse filled with thick fog that reduces visibility to 10 feet. Trapped creatures don't age and don't need to eat, drink, or sleep. A trapped creature can escape using magic that permits planar travel; otherwise it is confined to the cell until freed.</p><p>If the mirror traps a creature but all twelve cells are occupied, it frees one trapped creature at random to make room. A freed creature appears in an unoccupied space within sight of the mirror, facing away from it. If the mirror is shattered, all creatures it holds are freed and appear in unoccupied spaces near it.</p><p>While within 5 feet of the mirror, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to name one trapped creature or call out a cell by number. The creature named or in that cell appears as an image on the mirror's surface, and you and the creature can communicate. Similarly, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and use a second command word to free one trapped creature, which appears with its possessions in the unoccupied space nearest the mirror, facing away from it.</p><p>Placing the mirror inside an extradimensional space created by a Bag of Holding, a Portable Hole, or a similar item instantly destroys both items and opens a gate to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-astral\">Astral Plane</a>. The gate originates where one item was placed in the other. Any creature within 10 feet of the gate that isn't behind <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-total-cover\">Total Cover</a> is sucked through to a random location on the Astral Plane. The gate then closes, and it is one-way and can't be reopened.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-nolzur-s-marvelous-pigments", "title": "Nolzur's Marvelous Pigments", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This fine wooden box holds 1d4 pots of pigment and a brush (weighing 1 pound in total).</p><p>Using the brush and expending 1 pot of pigment, you can paint any number of three-dimensional objects and terrain features (such as walls, doors, trees, flowers, weapons, webs, and pits), as long as they are all confined to a 20-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-cube\">Cube</a>. The effort takes 10 minutes (regardless of how many elements you create), during which you must remain in the Cube, and it requires <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>. If your Concentration is broken or you leave the Cube before the work is done, all the painted elements vanish and the pot of pigment is wasted.</p><p>When the work is done, the painted objects and terrain features become real. Painting a door on a wall creates an actual door that can be opened to whatever lies beyond. Painting a pit creates a real pit, the entire depth of which must lie within the 20-foot Cube.</p><p>No object created by a pot of pigment can be worth more than 25 GP, and the total value of everything created by one pot can't exceed 500 GP. If you paint objects of greater value (such as a large pile of gold), they look authentic, but close inspection reveals they're made of paste, cookies, or some other worthless material.</p><p>If you paint a form of energy such as fire or lightning, the energy dissipates as soon as you finish the painting, doing no harm.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-robe-of-scintillating-colors", "title": "Robe of Scintillating Colors", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This robe has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While you wear it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and expend 1 charge to make the garment display a shifting pattern of dazzling hues until the end of your next turn. During this time, the robe sheds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bright-light\">Bright Light</a> in a 30-foot radius and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> for another 30 feet, and creatures that can see you have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you. Any creature in the Bright Light that can see you when the robe's power is activated must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-stunned\">Stunned</a> condition until the effect ends.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-robe-of-stars", "title": "Robe of Stars", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This black or dark-blue robe is embroidered with small white or silver stars. You gain a +1 bonus to saving throws while you wear it.</p><p>Six stars on the robe's upper front are particularly large. While wearing the robe, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to remove one of these stars and expend it to cast the level 5 version of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-missile\">Magic Missile</a>. Daily at dusk, 1d6 removed stars reappear on the robe.</p><p>While you wear the robe, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to enter the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-astral\">Astral Plane</a> along with everything you are wearing and carrying. You remain there until you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to return to the plane you were on. You reappear in the last space you occupied or, if it is occupied, the nearest unoccupied space.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-spirit-board", "title": "Spirit Board", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This ornate wooden board has the letters of the Common alphabet printed on one side, alongside the words \"Yes\" and \"No\" and symbols representing \"Weal\" and \"Woe.\" It comes with a heart-shaped wooden planchette, which must be resting on the lettered side of the board for the board's magic to function.</p><p>The board has 3 charges and regains 1 expended charge daily at dawn. While touching the planchette, you can take 1 minute to cast one of the spells in the table below, expending the listed number of charges. As you cast the spell, you call on the spirits of the dead to guide the planchette across the board, answering your questions by pointing to letters or words on its surface.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Spell</th><th>Charge Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-augury\">Augury</a></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-commune\">Commune</a></td><td>3</td></tr></tbody></table>"}, {"id": "magic-item-tome-of-clear-thought", "title": "Tome of Clear Thought", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This book contains memory and logic exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Intelligence increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic but regains it in a century.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-tome-of-leadership-and-influence", "title": "Tome of Leadership and Influence", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This book contains guidelines for influencing and charming others, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Charisma increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic but regains it in a century.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-tome-of-understanding", "title": "Tome of Understanding", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This book contains intuition and insight exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Wisdom increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic but regains it in a century.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-wraps-of-unarmed-power-3", "title": "Wraps of Unarmed Power +3", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>While wearing these wraps, you have a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-unarmed-strike\">Unarmed Strikes</a>. Those strikes deal your choice of Force damage or their normal damage type.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-apparatus-of-kwalish", "title": "Apparatus of Kwalish", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong></p><p>This item looks like a sealed iron barrel weighing 500 pounds. A hidden catch, found with a successful DC 20 Intelligence (Investigation) check, unlocks a hatch at one end that lets two Medium or smaller creatures crawl inside. Ten levers, each in a neutral position and able to move up or down, are set in a row at the far end. When certain levers are used, the apparatus transforms to resemble a giant lobster.</p><p>The apparatus is a Large object with AC 20, 200 Hit Points, Speed 30 feet, Swim Speed 30 feet (both 0 if the legs aren't extended), and Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage. As a vehicle it needs one pilot. While the hatch is closed, the compartment is airtight and watertight and holds enough air for 10 hours of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside. It floats on water and can dive to a depth of 900 feet; below that, it takes 2d6 Bludgeoning damage each minute from pressure.</p><p>A creature in the compartment can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to move up to two levers up or down. After each use, a lever returns to neutral. From left to right, the levers work as follows.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Lever</th><th>Up</th><th>Down</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Legs extend, letting the apparatus walk and swim.</td><td>Legs retract, reducing its Speed and Swim Speed to 0 and making it unable to benefit from bonuses to speed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Forward window shutter opens.</td><td>Forward window shutter closes.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Side window shutters open (two per side).</td><td>Side window shutters close (two per side).</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Two claws extend from the front of the apparatus.</td><td>The claws retract.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Each extended claw makes a melee attack: +8 to hit, reach 5 ft.; 7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage.</td><td>Each extended claw makes a melee attack: +8 to hit, reach 5 ft.; the target has the Grappled condition (escape DC 15).</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>The apparatus walks or swims forward, provided its legs are extended.</td><td>The apparatus walks or swims backward, provided its legs are extended.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>The apparatus turns 90 degrees counterclockwise, provided its legs are extended.</td><td>The apparatus turns 90 degrees clockwise, provided its legs are extended.</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Eyelike fixtures emit Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for another 30 feet.</td><td>The light turns off.</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>The apparatus sinks up to 20 feet if it's in liquid.</td><td>The apparatus rises up to 20 feet if it's in liquid.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>The rear hatch unseals and opens.</td><td>The rear hatch closes and seals.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-belt-of-cloud-giant-strength", "title": "Belt of Cloud Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 27. It has no effect on you if your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-belt-of-storm-giant-strength", "title": "Belt of Storm Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 29. It has no effect on you if your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-invisibility", "title": "Cloak of Invisibility", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This cloak has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to pull its hood over your head and expend 1 charge to give yourself the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-invisible\">Invisible</a> condition for 1 hour. The effect ends early if you pull the hood down (no action required) or stop wearing the cloak.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-crystal-ball-of-mind-reading", "title": "Crystal Ball of Mind Reading", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While touching this crystal orb, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scrying\">Scrying</a> (save DC 17) with it. In addition, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-thoughts\">Detect Thoughts</a> (save DC 17) targeting creatures you can see within 30 feet of the spell's sensor. You don't need to concentrate on this Detect Thoughts spell to maintain it, but it ends if the Scrying spell ends.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-crystal-ball-of-telepathy", "title": "Crystal Ball of Telepathy", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While touching this crystal orb, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scrying\">Scrying</a> (save DC 17) with it. In addition, you can communicate telepathically with creatures you can see within 30 feet of the spell's sensor. You can also cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-suggestion\">Suggestion</a> (save DC 17) through the sensor on one of those creatures. You don't need to concentrate on this Suggestion to maintain it, but it ends if Scrying ends. You can't cast Suggestion this way again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-crystal-ball-of-true-seeing", "title": "Crystal Ball of True Seeing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While touching this crystal orb, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scrying\">Scrying</a> (save DC 17) with it. In addition, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-truesight\">Truesight</a> with a range of 120 feet centered on the spell's sensor.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-cubic-gate", "title": "Cubic Gate", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong></p><p>This cube is 3 inches across and radiates palpable magical energy. Its six sides are each keyed to a different plane of existence, one of which is the Material Plane; the others are linked to planes the DM determines.</p><p>The cube has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can expend 1 charge to cast one of the following spells with it.</p><p><strong>Gate.</strong> Press one side of the cube to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gate\">Gate</a>, opening a portal to the plane keyed to that side.</p><p><strong>Plane Shift.</strong> Press one side twice to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-plane-shift\">Plane Shift</a>, transporting the targets to the plane keyed to that side.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-deck-of-many-things", "title": "Deck of Many Things", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong></p><p>Usually kept in a box or pouch, this deck holds cards of ivory or vellum. Most such decks (75 percent) have thirteen cards, but some have twenty-two. Use the matching column of the table when determining cards at random.</p><p>Before drawing, you must declare how many cards you will draw, then draw them at random; any cards drawn beyond that number have no effect. Each card's magic takes effect as soon as you draw it, and you must draw each card within 1 hour of the previous one. If you fail to draw your declared number, the remaining cards fly from the deck on their own and take effect all at once.</p><p>A drawn card disappears. Unless it was the Fool or the Jester, it reappears in the deck, so the same card can be drawn twice. Once the Fool or Jester has left the deck, reroll if it comes up again.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100 (13-Card)</th><th>1d100 (22-Card)</th><th>Card</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>—</td><td>01–05</td><td>Balance</td></tr><tr><td>—</td><td>06–10</td><td>Comet</td></tr><tr><td>—</td><td>11–14</td><td>Donjon</td></tr><tr><td>01–08</td><td>15–18</td><td>Euryale</td></tr><tr><td>—</td><td>19–23</td><td>Fates</td></tr><tr><td>09–16</td><td>24–27</td><td>Flames</td></tr><tr><td>—</td><td>28–31</td><td>Fool</td></tr><tr><td>—</td><td>32–36</td><td>Gem</td></tr><tr><td>17–24</td><td>37–41</td><td>Jester</td></tr><tr><td>25–32</td><td>42–46</td><td>Key</td></tr><tr><td>33–40</td><td>47–51</td><td>Knight</td></tr><tr><td>41–48</td><td>52–56</td><td>Moon</td></tr><tr><td>—</td><td>57–60</td><td>Puzzle</td></tr><tr><td>49–56</td><td>61–64</td><td>Rogue</td></tr><tr><td>57–64</td><td>65–68</td><td>Ruin</td></tr><tr><td>—</td><td>69–73</td><td>Sage</td></tr><tr><td>65–72</td><td>74–77</td><td>Skull</td></tr><tr><td>73–80</td><td>78–82</td><td>Star</td></tr><tr><td>81–88</td><td>83–87</td><td>Sun</td></tr><tr><td>—</td><td>88–91</td><td>Talons</td></tr><tr><td>89–96</td><td>92–96</td><td>Throne</td></tr><tr><td>97–100</td><td>97–100</td><td>Void</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Balance.</strong> You can raise one ability score by 2 (maximum 22) if you also lower another by 2. You can't lower a score of 5 or less. You can instead choose not to adjust anything, in which case the card has no effect.</p><p><strong>Comet.</strong> The next time you enter combat against one or more Hostile creatures, you can choose one as your foe when you roll Initiative. If you reduce that foe to 0 Hit Points during the combat, you have Advantage on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-death-saving-throw\">Death Saving Throws</a> for 1 year. If someone else drops the foe or you pick none, the card has no effect.</p><p><strong>Donjon.</strong> You vanish and are entombed in suspended animation inside an extradimensional sphere. Everything you wear and carry goes with you except Artifacts, which stay where you were. You remain imprisoned until someone finds and removes you from the sphere. Divination magic can't locate you, but a spell can reveal the prison's location. You draw no more cards.</p><p><strong>Euryale.</strong> The card's medusa-like face curses you, giving you a −2 penalty to saving throws. Only a god or the Fates card can end the curse.</p><p><strong>Fates.</strong> Reality unravels and re-spins, letting you avoid or erase one event as if it never happened. You can use this as soon as you draw the card or at any later time before you die.</p><p><strong>Flames.</strong> A powerful devil becomes your enemy. It seeks your ruin and torments you, savoring your suffering before it tries to kill you. The enmity lasts until you or the devil dies.</p><p><strong>Fool.</strong> You have Disadvantage on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-d20-test\">D20 Tests</a> for the next 72 hours. Draw another card; this draw doesn't count toward your declared total.</p><p><strong>Gem.</strong> Twenty-five pieces of jewelry worth 2,000 GP each, or fifty gems worth 1,000 GP each, appear at your feet.</p><p><strong>Jester.</strong> You have Advantage on D20 Tests for the next 72 hours, or you can draw two extra cards beyond your declared total.</p><p><strong>Key.</strong> A magic weapon of Rare or higher rarity that you're proficient with appears on your person, chosen by the DM.</p><p><strong>Knight.</strong> A Knight appears in an unoccupied space of your choice within 30 feet and enters your service. It shares your alignment and serves you loyally until death, believing fate drew you together. Work with the DM on its name and backstory; the DM can swap in a different stat block.</p><p><strong>Moon.</strong> You can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> 1d3 times.</p><p><strong>Puzzle.</strong> Permanently reduce your Intelligence or Wisdom by 1d4 + 1 (minimum 1). You can draw one extra card beyond your declared total.</p><p><strong>Rogue.</strong> An NPC of the DM's choice becomes Hostile toward you, and you don't know who it is until they or someone else reveals it. Nothing short of a Wish spell or divine intervention ends the hostility.</p><p><strong>Ruin.</strong> All wealth you carry or own other than magic items is lost. Portable property vanishes; businesses, buildings, and land are lost in the way that changes reality least. Any documents proving ownership vanish too.</p><p><strong>Sage.</strong> At any time within a year of drawing this card, you can ask a question in meditation and mentally receive a truthful answer.</p><p><strong>Skull.</strong> An Avatar of Death appears in the nearest unoccupied space and attacks only you. It looks like a ghostly skeleton in a tattered black robe carrying a spectral scythe. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or you die. If one of your allies damages it, that ally summons another avatar, which appears near them and attacks only them. You and each ally can summon only one avatar from this draw. A creature slain by an avatar can't be restored to life. The avatar has <em>Incorporeal Movement</em> (it moves through creatures and objects as if they were Difficult Terrain and takes 5 (1d10) Force damage if it ends its turn inside an object), and its <em>Multiattack</em> is a number of Reaping Scythe attacks equal to half the summoner's Proficiency Bonus, rounded up. <em>Reaping Scythe:</em> automatic hit, reach 5 ft.; 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage.</p><p><strong>Star.</strong> Increase one ability score by 2, to a maximum of 24.</p><p><strong>Sun.</strong> A magic item chosen by the DM appears on your person. You also gain 10 Temporary Hit Points daily at dawn until you die.</p><p><strong>Talons.</strong> Every magic item you wear or carry disintegrates; Artifacts in your possession vanish instead.</p><p><strong>Throne.</strong> You gain proficiency and Expertise in your choice of History, Insight, Intimidation, or Persuasion, and you gain rightful ownership of a small keep somewhere in the world. The keep is home to one or more monsters that must be cleared out before you can claim it.</p><p><strong>Void.</strong> Your soul is drawn from your body and held in an object in a place of the DM's choice, guarded by one or more powerful beings. While trapped, your body is inert, doesn't age, and needs no food, air, or water. A Wish spell can't return your soul to your body, but it reveals where the object is. You draw no more cards.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-instrument-of-the-bards-ollamh-harp", "title": "Instrument of the Bards (Ollamh Harp)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard)</p><p>This instrument is superior to an ordinary instrument of its kind in every way, and is named after one of seven legendary bard colleges. A creature that tries to play it without being attuned to it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d4 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>.</p><p>You can play the instrument to cast one of its spells, using your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Once the instrument has been used to cast a spell, it can't be used to cast that spell again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> The instrument holds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fly\">Fly</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-invisibility\">Invisibility</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-levitate\">Levitate</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-protection-from-evil-and-good\">Protection from Evil and Good</a>, plus the following: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-confusion\">Confusion</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-control-weather\">Control Weather</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fire-storm\">Fire Storm</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-greater-absorption", "title": "Ioun Stone of Greater Absorption", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>While this marbled lavender and green ellipsoid orbits your head, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to cancel a spell of level 8 or lower cast by a creature you can see. A canceled spell has no effect, and any resources used to cast it are wasted. Once the stone has canceled 20 levels of spells, it burns out, turns dull gray, and loses its magic.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-mastery", "title": "Ioun Stone of Mastery", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>Your Proficiency Bonus increases by 1 while this pale green prism orbits your head.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ioun-stone-of-regeneration", "title": "Ioun Stone of Regeneration", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types exist, each a distinct combination of shape and color.</p><p>When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, it orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit on you. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at once. An orbiting stone counts as an object you are wearing; it avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to dodge collisions and thwarting all attempts by others to attack or snatch it. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can seize and stow any number of stones orbiting your head. If your attunement to a stone ends while it orbits your head, it falls as though you had dropped it.</p><p>You regain 15 Hit Points at the end of each hour this pearly white spindle orbits your head, provided you have at least 1 Hit Point.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-iron-flask", "title": "Iron Flask", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong></p><p>While holding this brass-stoppered iron flask, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to target a creature you can see within 60 feet of you. If the flask is empty and the target is native to a plane of existence other than the one you're on, the target must succeed on a DC 17 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be trapped in the flask. If the target has been trapped by the flask before, it has Advantage on the save. Once trapped, a creature remains in the flask until released. The flask holds only one creature at a time. A trapped creature doesn't age and doesn't need to breathe, eat, or drink.</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to remove the stopper and release the creature. It then obeys your commands for 1 hour, understanding them even if it doesn't know the language they're given in. If you issue no commands, or give one likely to result in its death or imprisonment, it defends itself but otherwise takes no actions. When the hour ends, the creature acts according to its normal disposition and alignment.</p><p><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-identify\">Identify</a> reveals whether the flask contains a creature, but the only way to learn its type is to open the flask. A newly discovered Iron Flask might already contain a creature chosen by the DM.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-robe-of-the-archmagi", "title": "Robe of the Archmagi", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>This elegant garment is made from exquisite cloth and adorned with runes. You gain these benefits while wearing the robe.</p><p><strong>Armor.</strong> If you aren't wearing armor, your base Armor Class is 15 plus your Dexterity modifier.</p><p><strong>Magic Resistance.</strong> You have Advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.</p><p><strong>War Mage.</strong> Your spell save DC and spell attack bonus each increase by 2.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-scarab-of-protection", "title": "Scarab of Protection", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This beetle-shaped medallion provides three benefits while it is on your person.</p><p><strong>Defense.</strong> You gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class.</p><p><strong>Preservation.</strong> The scarab has 12 charges. If you fail a saving throw against a Necromancy spell or a harmful effect originating from an Undead, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to expend 1 charge and turn the failed save into a success. The scarab crumbles to powder and is destroyed when its last charge is expended.</p><p><strong>Spell Resistance.</strong> You have Advantage on saving throws against spells.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-sovereign-glue", "title": "Sovereign Glue", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong></p><p>This viscous, milky-white substance forms a permanent adhesive bond between any two objects. It must be stored in a jar or flask coated on the inside with Oil of Slipperiness. When found, a container holds 1d6 + 1 ounces.</p><p>One ounce of the glue covers a 1-foot-square surface. Applying an ounce takes a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, and the applied glue takes 1 minute to set. Once set, the bond can be broken only by applying Universal Solvent or Oil of Etherealness, or by a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> spell.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-sphere-of-annihilation", "title": "Sphere of Annihilation", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong></p><p>This 2-foot-diameter black sphere is a hole in the multiverse, hovering in space and stabilized by a magical field around it.</p><p>The sphere obliterates all matter it passes through and all matter that passes through it. Artifacts are the exception: unless an Artifact is susceptible to damage from a Sphere of Annihilation, it passes through unscathed. Anything else that touches the sphere without being wholly engulfed and obliterated takes 8d10 Force damage.</p><p><strong>Controlling the Sphere.</strong> A Sphere of Annihilation is stationary until someone takes control of it. If you are within 60 feet of a sphere, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to make a DC 25 Intelligence (Arcana) check. On a success, you control the sphere until the start of your next turn, and if another creature controlled it, that creature loses control. On a failure, the sphere moves 10 feet toward you in a straight line.</p><p>While you control the sphere, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to move it in one direction of your choice, up to a number of feet equal to 5 times your Intelligence modifier (minimum 5 feet). Any creature whose space the sphere enters must succeed on a DC 19 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be touched by it, taking 8d10 Force damage. A creature reduced to 0 Hit Points by this damage is obliterated, leaving its possessions behind but no other physical remains.</p><p><strong>Sphere Interactions.</strong> If the sphere touches a planar portal (such as one created by <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gate\">Gate</a>) or an extradimensional space (such as that within a Portable Hole), the DM determines randomly what happens.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–50</td><td>The sphere is destroyed.</td></tr><tr><td>51–85</td><td>The sphere moves through the portal or into the extradimensional space.</td></tr><tr><td>86–00</td><td>A spatial rift sends the sphere and each creature and object within 180 feet of it to a random plane of existence.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-talisman-of-pure-good", "title": "Talisman of Pure Good", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement by a Cleric or Paladin)</p><p>This talisman is a mighty symbol of goodness. A Fiend or an Undead that touches it takes 8d6 Radiant damage, and takes the damage again each time it ends its turn holding or carrying the talisman.</p><p><strong>Holy Symbol.</strong> You can use the talisman as a Holy Symbol. You gain a +2 bonus to spell attack rolls while you wear or hold it.</p><p><strong>Pure Rebuke.</strong> The talisman has 7 charges. While wearing or holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and expend 1 charge to target one creature you can see on the ground within 120 feet of you. A flaming fissure opens under the target, which makes a DC 20 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. A Fiend or an Undead has Disadvantage on the save. On a failed save, the target falls into the fissure and is destroyed, leaving no remains. On a successful save, it isn't cast into the fissure but takes 4d6 Psychic damage from the ordeal. Either way, the fissure then closes without a trace. When you expend the last charge, the talisman disperses into motes of golden light and is destroyed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-talisman-of-the-sphere", "title": "Talisman of the Sphere", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While holding or wearing this talisman, you have Advantage on any Intelligence (Arcana) check you make to control a Sphere of Annihilation. In addition, when you start your turn in control of a Sphere of Annihilation, you can take a Magic action to move it 10 feet plus a number of additional feet equal to 10 times your Intelligence modifier. This movement doesn't have to be in a straight line.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-talisman-of-ultimate-evil", "title": "Talisman of Ultimate Evil", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This item symbolizes unrepentant evil. A creature that isn't a Fiend or an Undead and touches the talisman takes 8d6 Necrotic damage, and takes the damage again each time it ends its turn holding or carrying the talisman.</p><p><strong>Holy Symbol.</strong> You can use the talisman as a Holy Symbol. You gain a +2 bonus to spell attack rolls while you wear or hold it.</p><p><strong>Ultimate End.</strong> The talisman has 6 charges. While wearing or holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and expend 1 charge to target one creature you can see on the ground within 120 feet of you. A flaming fissure opens under the target, which makes a DC 20 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. A Celestial has Disadvantage on the save. On a failed save, the target falls into the fissure and is destroyed, leaving no remains. On a successful save, it isn't cast into the fissure but takes 4d6 Psychic damage from the ordeal. Either way, the fissure then closes without a trace. When you expend the last charge, the talisman dissolves into foul-smelling slime and is destroyed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-tome-of-the-stilled-tongue", "title": "Tome of the Stilled Tongue", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement by a Wizard)</p><p>This book has a desiccated tongue pinned to its front cover. Five of these tomes exist, and it's unknown which one is the original. The tongue on the first tome belonged to a treacherous former servant of the lich Vecna; the tongues on the other four copies came from other spellcasters who crossed Vecna. The first few pages of each tome are filled with indecipherable scrawls, and the remaining pages are blank.</p><p>While attuned to the tome, you can use it as a Spellbook and an Arcane Focus (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spellcasting-focus\">Spellcasting Focus</a>). In addition, while holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to cast a spell you have written in it, without expending a spell slot or using any Verbal or Somatic components. Once used, this property can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><p>Only you can remove the tongue from the book's cover. If you do so, all spells written in the book are permanently erased.</p><p>Vecna watches anyone using this tome and can write cryptic messages in it. These messages typically fade away after they are read.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement by a wizard)</p><p>If you can attune to this item, you can use it as a spellbook and an arcane focus. In addition, while holding the tome, you can use a bonus action to cast a spell you have written in it, without expending a spell slot or using any verbal or somatic components. Once used, this property can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><p>While attuned to the book, you can remove the tongue from its cover. If you do so, all spells written in the book are permanently erased.</p><p>Vecna watches anyone using this tome and can also write cryptic messages in it. These messages appear at midnight and fade away after they are read.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-universal-solvent", "title": "Universal Solvent", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong></p><p>This tube holds a milky liquid with a strong alcohol smell. When found, a tube contains 1d6 + 1 ounces.</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to pour 1 or more ounces of the solvent from the tube onto a surface within reach. Each ounce instantly dissolves up to 1 square foot of adhesive it touches, including Sovereign Glue.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-well-of-many-worlds", "title": "Well of Many Worlds", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong></p><p>This fine black cloth, soft as silk, is folded to the size of a handkerchief. It unfolds into a circular sheet 6 feet across.</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to unfold the Well of Many Worlds and place it on a solid surface, whereupon it forms a two-way, 6-foot-diameter circular portal to another world or plane of existence. Each time the item opens a portal, the DM decides where it leads. The portal stays open until a creature within 5 feet of it takes a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to close it by taking hold of the cloth's edges and folding it up.</p><p>Once the Well has opened a portal, it can't do so again for 1d8 hours.</p>\n"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items-artifact", "title": "Artifact", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-book-of-exalted-deeds", "title": "Book of Exalted Deeds", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Artifact</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This treatise on all that is good in the multiverse figures in many religions. It rarely stays in one place: as soon as it has been read, it vanishes to another corner of the multiverse where its moral guidance can bring hope to an endangered world. Copies can't capture its magic or its benefits. A heavy clasp shaped like angel wings holds it shut, and only an attuned creature can release the clasp. Once the book is open, the attuned creature must spend 80 hours reading and studying it to gain its benefits. Other creatures can read the text but glean nothing from it.</p><p>A <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiend</a>, an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a>, or a servant of a god from the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"lore-lower-planes\">Lower Planes</a> that tries to read from the book takes 24d6 Radiant <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. This damage ignores <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-immunity\">Immunity</a> and can't be reduced or avoided by any means. A creature reduced to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> by it disappears in a flash and is destroyed, leaving its possessions behind; the book then vanishes and the creature's attunement to it ends.</p><p>The book's benefits last only as long as you strive to do good. If 10 days pass without you performing at least one act of kindness or generosity, or if you willingly perform an evil act, you lose all the benefits the book has granted.</p><p><strong>Celestial Calm.</strong> While attuned to the book, you have Immunity to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-charmed\">Charmed</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> conditions and Resistance to Psychic damage. These benefits become permanent after you finish reading and studying the book.</p><p><strong>Divine Wisdom.</strong> After you finish reading and studying the book, your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-wisdom\">Wisdom</a> increases by 2, to a maximum of 24. You can't gain this benefit from the book more than once.</p><p><strong>Enlightened Magic.</strong> After you finish reading and studying the book, any spell slot you expend to cast a spell counts as a spell slot one level higher.</p><p><strong>Halo.</strong> After you finish reading and studying the book, you gain a protective halo that sheds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bright-light\">Bright Light</a> in a 10-foot radius and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> for another 10 feet. You can dismiss or manifest the halo as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>. While it is present, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Charisma (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-persuasion\">Persuasion</a>) checks, and Fiends and Undead within the halo's Bright Light make <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> against you with <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a>.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The book has 2 minor beneficial properties and 2 major beneficial properties.</p><p><strong>Destroying the Book.</strong> The book can't be destroyed. However, drowning it in the River Styx removes all writing and imagery from its pages and leaves it powerless for 1d100 years.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-book-of-vile-darkness", "title": "Book of Vile Darkness", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Artifact</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>The contents of this foul manuscript are the meat and drink of the wicked, and knowledge so horrid that even glimpsing its pages invites doom. Most believe the lich-god Vecna wrote it, recording every horrid idea, corrupt thought, and example of foul magic he came across or devised; other practitioners of evil have added their own pages since, stitching them in or annotating the existing text. Some pages are missing, torn, or so thoroughly covered in ink, blood, and scratches that the original text can't be read.</p><p>Nature can't abide the book's presence. Ordinary plants wither near it, common animals refuse to approach it, and it gradually destroys whatever it touches. Even stone cracks and turns to powder if the book rests on it long enough.</p><p>Whenever a creature that isn't a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiend</a> or an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> attunes to the book, it makes a DC 17 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. On a failed save, it is magically transformed into a Larva under the DM's control. Only a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> spell can reverse this transformation.</p><p>A creature attuned to the book must spend 80 hours reading and studying it to use its Adjusted Ability Scores, Tireless Form, Spells, Vile Lore, and Vile Speech properties.</p><p>The book remains with you only as long as you strive to work evil. If 10 days pass without you performing at least one evil act, or if you willingly perform a good act, the book disappears, your attunement to it ends immediately, and you lose all its benefits. If you die while attuned to it, an entity of great evil claims your soul, and you can't be restored to life by any means while that soul remains imprisoned.</p><p><strong>Adjusted Ability Scores.</strong> One ability score of your choice increases by 2, to a maximum of 24, and another ability score of your choice decreases by 2, to a minimum of 3. The book can't adjust your ability scores again.</p><p><strong>Tireless Form.</strong> While the book is on your person, you have Immunity to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> condition.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The book has 3 minor beneficial properties, 1 major beneficial property, 3 minor detrimental properties, and 2 major detrimental properties.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> While attuned to the book and holding it, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animate-dead\">Animate Dead</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-circle-of-death\">Circle of Death</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dominate-monster\">Dominate Monster</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-finger-of-death\">Finger of Death</a> from it (save DC 18). Once you use the book to cast a spell, you can't cast that spell from it again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Vile Lore.</strong> You can reference the book whenever you make an Intelligence check to recall information about some aspect of evil, such as lore about demons, and you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on that check. At the DM's discretion, the book might reveal secrets no mortal should know, such as the true names of powerful Fiends, foul rites that transform a creature into a death knight or lich, or long-lost spells crafted by beings whose names ought never to be spoken.</p><p><strong>Vile Speech.</strong> While the book is on your person, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to recite words from its pages in a foul, dead language. Each time you do so, you take 1d12 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, and each creature within 15 feet of you takes 3d6 Psychic damage unless it is a Fiend or an Undead.</p><p><strong>Destroying the Book.</strong> Pages can be torn from the book, but any evil lore on them eventually finds its way back into it, usually when a new author adds pages to the tome. If a solar tears the book in two, it is destroyed for 1d100 years, after which it re-forms in some far corner of the multiverse. A creature attuned to the book for 100 years can unearth a phrase hidden in the original text that, when translated to Celestial and spoken aloud, destroys both the speaker and the book in a flash of radiance. However, as long as evil exists in the multiverse, the book re-forms 1d10 × 100 years later.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-demonomicon-of-iggwilv", "title": "Demonomicon of Iggwilv", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Artifact</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This treatise by the archmage Iggwilv documents the layers and inhabitants of the Abyss and is regarded as the most thorough and blasphemous tome of demonology in the multiverse. It records both the oldest and the newest profanities of the Abyss and its demons. Demons have tried to censor the text and sections have been ripped from its spine, but a secret piece of the Abyss caged behind the lines of script keeps the book up to date no matter how many pages are removed, and it longs to be more than a reference work.</p><p><strong>Abyssal Lore.</strong> You can reference the Demonomicon whenever you make an Intelligence check to discern information about demons or a Wisdom (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-survival\">Survival</a>) check related to the Abyss. When you do so, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on the check.</p><p><strong>Containment.</strong> The first ten pages are blank. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while holding the book, you can target a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiend</a> you can see that is trapped within the area of a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-circle\">Magic Circle</a> spell. The Fiend must succeed on a DC 20 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> with <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> or become trapped within one of the blank pages, which fills with writing detailing the creature's widely known name and depravities. Once you use this action, you can't use it again until the next dawn.</p><p>When you finish a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-long-rest\">Long Rest</a>, if you and the Demonomicon are on the same plane of existence, one trapped creature within the book can attempt to possess you. You make a DC 20 Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, you are possessed by the creature, which controls you like a puppet. As a Magic action, the possessing creature can release you and appear in the closest unoccupied space to you. On a successful save, that Fiend can't try to possess you again for 7 days (though another Fiend trapped in the book can). When the tome is discovered, 1d4 Fiends, typically demons, occupy its pages.</p><p><strong>Ensnarement.</strong> While you carry the book, whenever you cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-circle\">Magic Circle</a> naming only Fiends or cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-planar-binding\">Planar Binding</a> targeting a Fiend, the spell is cast at level 9 regardless of the spell slot used, if any. Additionally, the Fiend has Disadvantage on its saving throw against the spell.</p><p><strong>Fiendish Scourging.</strong> While you carry the book, whenever you make a damage roll for a spell you cast against a Fiend, you use the maximum possible result instead of rolling.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The Demonomicon has 2 minor beneficial properties, 1 minor detrimental property, and 1 major detrimental property.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> The book has 8 charges and regains 1d8 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take a Magic action to cast a spell from the table below (save DC 20), expending the listed number of charges.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Spell</th><th>Charge Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-circle\">Magic Circle</a></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-jar\">Magic Jar</a></td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-planar-ally\">Planar Ally</a></td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-planar-binding\">Planar Binding</a></td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-plane-shift\">Plane Shift</a></td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-summon-fiend\">Summon Fiend</a></td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-tasha-s-hideous-laughter\">Tasha's Hideous Laughter</a></td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Destroying the Demonomicon.</strong> To destroy the book, six different demon lords must each tear out a sixth of its pages, after which the pages reappear after 24 hours. Before those hours pass, anyone who opens the book's remaining binding is transported to a nascent layer of the Abyss hidden within it. At the heart of that deadly, semisentient domain lies a long-lost Artifact, Fraz-Urb'luu's Staff. If the staff is dragged out of the pocket plane, the tome becomes a mundane, out-of-date copy of the Tome of Zyx, the work that served as the foundation of the Demonomicon, which can be destroyed like any ordinary book. The demon lord Fraz-Urb'luu knows instantly when the staff emerges.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-eye-and-hand-of-vecna", "title": "Eye and Hand of Vecna", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Artifact</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Of the lich Vecna, only one hand and one eye remain, grisly Artifacts that still work to carry out his will. The Eye of Vecna and the Hand of Vecna are separate Artifacts that might be found together or separately. The eye looks like a bloodshot organ torn free from its socket; the hand is a shriveled left extremity.</p><p><strong>Random Properties of the Eye and Hand.</strong> The Eye of Vecna and the Hand of Vecna each have 1 minor beneficial property, 1 major beneficial property, and 1 minor detrimental property.</p><p><strong>Attuning to the Eye.</strong> To attune to the eye, you must press it into your empty eye socket. The eye grafts itself to your head and remains there until you die. If the eye is ever removed, you die.</p><p><strong>Properties of the Eye.</strong> While you are attuned to the eye, your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-alignment\">alignment</a> is Neutral Evil and you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Truesight.</strong> You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-truesight\">Truesight</a> out to 240 feet.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting.</strong> The eye has 8 charges and regains 1d4 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. You can cast a spell from the table below from the eye (save DC 18), expending the listed number of charges. Each time you cast a spell from the eye, there is a 5 percent chance that Vecna tears your soul from your body, devours it, and takes control of the body like a puppet. If that happens, you become an NPC under the DM's control.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Spell</th><th>Charge Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-clairvoyance\">Clairvoyance</a></td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-crown-of-madness\">Crown of Madness</a></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-disintegrate\">Disintegrate</a></td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dominate-monster\">Dominate Monster</a></td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-eyebite\">Eyebite</a></td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>X-ray Vision.</strong> You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to gain X-ray vision with a range of 30 feet for 1 minute. To you, solid objects within that radius appear transparent and don't block light. The vision penetrates 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, or up to 3 feet of wood or dirt. Thicker substances block it, as does a thin sheet of lead.</p><p><strong>Attuning to the Hand.</strong> To attune to the hand, you must press it against the stump where your left hand was. The hand grafts itself to your arm and becomes a functioning appendage. If the hand is ever removed, you die.</p><p><strong>Properties of the Hand.</strong> While you are attuned to the hand, your alignment is Neutral Evil and you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Great Strength.</strong> Your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-strength\">Strength</a> becomes 20 unless it is already 20 or higher.</p><p><strong>Icy Touch.</strong> Any melee spell attack you make with the hand, and any melee attack made with a weapon held by it, deals an extra 2d8 Cold <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> on a hit.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting.</strong> The hand has 8 charges and regains 1d4 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. You can cast a spell from the table below from the hand (save DC 18), expending the listed number of charges. Each time you cast a spell from the hand, it casts <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-suggestion\">Suggestion</a> on you (save DC 18; no <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a> required), demanding that you commit an evil act. The hand might have a specific act in mind or leave the choice to you.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Spell</th><th>Charge Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-finger-of-death\">Finger of Death</a></td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-sleep\">Sleep</a></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-slow\">Slow</a></td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-teleport\">Teleport</a></td><td>3</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Properties of the Eye and Hand.</strong> While you are attuned to both the hand and the eye, you also gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Danger Sense.</strong> You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> rolls.</p><p><strong>Necrotic Reduction.</strong> As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can target one creature you can see within 5 feet of you. The target makes a DC 18 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 7d6 Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much on a successful one. A creature reduced to 0 Hit Points by this damage is transformed into green slime that covers the ground in its space, each 5-foot square of slime representing a separate patch. Nonmagical objects of metal or organic material that the target wore or carried are destroyed by the slime.</p><p><strong>Poison Immunity.</strong> You have Immunity to Poison damage and the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition.</p><p><strong>Regeneration.</strong> If you start your turn with at least 1 Hit Point, you regain 1d10 Hit Points.</p><p><strong>Wish.</strong> You can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a>. Once you do, you can't use this property again until 30 days have passed.</p><p><strong>Destroying the Eye and Hand.</strong> If both are attached to the same creature and that creature is slain by the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"magic-item-sword-of-kas\">Sword of Kas</a>, the eye and hand burst into flame, turn to ash, and are destroyed. Any other attempt to destroy either one seems to work, but the Artifact reappears in one of Vecna's many hidden vaults, where it waits to be rediscovered.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-orb-of-dragonkind", "title": "Orb of Dragonkind", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Artifact</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>An orb is an etched crystal globe about 10 inches across. When used, it grows to about 20 inches across and mist swirls inside it.</p><p>While attuned to an orb, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to peer into its depths and must then make a DC 15 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. On a success, you control the orb for as long as you stay attuned to it. On a failure, the orb imposes the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-charmed\">Charmed</a> condition on you for as long as you stay attuned to it.</p><p>While you're Charmed by the orb, you can't voluntarily end your attunement to it, and it casts <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-suggestion\">Suggestion</a> on you at will (save DC 18), urging you toward the evil ends it desires. The dragon essence inside might want many things: the annihilation of a particular society or organization, freedom from the orb, spreading suffering, advancing the worship of Tiamat, or something else the DM decides.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> The orb has 7 charges and regains 1d4 + 3 expended charges daily at dawn. If you control it, you can cast one of the spells below from it, expending the listed number of charges.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Spell</th><th>Charge Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-cure-wounds\">Cure Wounds</a> (level 9 version)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-daylight\">Daylight</a></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-death-ward\">Death Ward</a></td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-magic\">Detect Magic</a></td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scrying\">Scrying</a> (save DC 18)</td><td>3</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Call Dragons.</strong> While you control the orb, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to make it issue a telepathic call in all directions out to 40 miles. Chromatic dragons in range feel compelled to come to the orb as soon as possible by the most direct route. Dragon deities such as Tiamat are unaffected. Dragons drawn to the orb might be Hostile toward you for compelling them. Once used, this property can't be used again for 1 hour.</p><p><strong>Destroying an Orb.</strong> A Dragon Orb has AC 20 and is destroyed if it takes damage from a +3 weapon or a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-disintegrate\">Disintegrate</a> spell. Nothing else can harm it.</p>\n"}]}]}]};
